(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Executive Director of Vaccination, Ministry of National Defense, called on people to take the third dose of vaccination to increase their antibodies to better protect their health. From the Kovid 19 virus outbreak.
On the morning of October 14, 2021, General Ith Sarath continued to inspect a number of sites that are in the process of vaccinating against the first 19 doses of measles vaccine, or boosting the population in Phnom Penh, including at some factories.
General Ith Sarath noted that the third vaccination process was in good condition and that the people who went to the vaccination were following the arrangements of the vaccination team because they all understood From the principles and rules of the Ministry of Health to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19.
During the visit to the vaccination site, General Ith Sarath also observed that most of the people who go to the vaccination site go in the morning or during the day, which is free time from work.
General Ith Sarath reminded the people that vaccination against Kovid 19 is very important in helping to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and not to make it worse when infected. The third dose, or boosting dose, is even more important in protecting health because it can produce stronger antibodies to health.
The general called on all citizens to receive this booster dose, take time to give it to everyone, no matter how busy they are, do not give up.
"Work is important to support our family, but our health and our ability to avoid contracting 19 are even more important." "If we do not get vaccinated and we contract Kovid 19 or endanger our lives, it will be a huge loss for our family, so we need to get vaccinated no matter how busy we are." This is what General Ith Sarath said.
