Train and sedan accident in Prey Nob district solved, the driver returned home
(Phnom Penh): The accident between the train and the Samsung car in Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province has been resolved this morning, October 14, 2021, and the train driver was allowed to return home without any guilt. .
Please be reminded that at around 6 am on October 13, 2021, a traffic accident occurred when a train was driving a Samsung car at the intersection of National Road No. 4 near Veal Renh town in Samrong Krom village, Samrong district. Prey Nob, Preah Sihanouk Province. The driver of the car died on the way to the hospital.
After the incident, the man who was the driver of the train was also arrested. According to the police report, the train driver was Seng Sophal, a Cambodian living in Phnom Penh. The victim was the driver of the car, Chhin Sokchea, male, 31 years old, in Toul Toteung 1 village, Toul Toteung commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
This accident led to a discrepancy between the train and the car.
Sources from the official pointed out that this problem was caused by a communication problem between the train driver and the parachute drop. That is, when the car approached the crossing, no one came to drop the parapet.
But it is also said that for railways, trains are a priority. At the crossing point, there is also a warning sign because it is a train crossing point, so when you reach the railway point, you have to stop the car and look left and right before crossing to prevent accidents like this.
However, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport stressed that the dispute was resolved in the spirit of mutual understanding and reconciliation between the two parties. The authorities released the train driver to return only by questioning and building some cases.
Separately, the railway company also went to share the grief with the families of the victims.
