BEIJING, Oct. 10 (Xinhua) - The Chinese Academy of Sciences presented a variety of seeds through the "Warehouse" exhibition at the Kunming Institute of Plant Research, Yunnan Province, on October 10, 2021. "Seeds."
To prevent global biodiversity loss, the United Nations "Convention on Biological Diversity" entered into force on December 29, 1993. China was one of the first signatories.
At the same time, the work of conserving wild plants has yielded fruitful results. At present, China has planted 206 endangered species in forest areas, of which 112 are Chinese special species. In addition, China has established about 200 botanical gardens and established 11,800 protected areas of all kinds and levels across the country, accounting for 18% of China's total land area.
