Expert: Despite the Kovid 19 crisis, the Cambodian construction sector is still doing well, 8 months this year, investment in the construction sector is nearly 4 billion dollars
(Phnom Penh): The Kovid 19 crisis, especially after the events of February 20, which affected many sectors in Cambodia, but in the construction sector is seen by experts in this field is not very affected almost all projects in In the first eight months of 2021, Cambodia received nearly $ 4 billion in investment in this sector.
According to the socio-economic trends report of the Ministry of Economy, in the first eight months of 2021 from January to August 2021, a total of 2,901 projects received construction permits, with a total value of 3,843 million. The dollar was down 24.4 percent, with 2,530 residential projects accounting for 87.2 percent of the total construction applications, down 449 percent from the same period last year.
The tycoon said that the decline in construction projects this year was due to the decline in the construction of condominiums and high-rise buildings due to the large number of foreign investors, while local people are not as inclined to live in condominiums as the adjoining houses. No, that is why the construction of condominiums has to be stagnant.
Mr. Oknha Cheng Kheng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, said that the construction and land sectors will remain strong in 2021, despite the fact that Cambodia, like the world, is facing the Kovid 19 crisis.
He observed that construction projects, both old and new, are still under construction, especially in Sihanoukville.
He expects the real estate sector in Cambodia to recover in line with economic growth when the government launches the economy and people can do business normally. General Neang Phat inspects the third vaccination activity at two different targets in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Subcommittee on Kovid 19 Vaccination, Ministry of National Defense, this morning, October 14, 2021, led a team to inspect the third dose of vaccination. At two different destinations in Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that the vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense has vaccinated more than 130,000 people in Phnom Penh in the past 3 days.
