(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, reiterated his position on climate change to the EU Ambassador to Cambodia. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Environment on October 14, 2021.
This discussion focused on the Royal Government of Cambodia's vision for the 26th United Nations Conference (COP26) on Climate Change in Glasgow, UK.
She said the European Union pays close attention to and supports countries in developing long-term plans to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by keeping global temperatures below 2 degrees Celsius. She also highlighted key issues to be discussed and addressed in (COP26), including climate change adaptation, climate financing and transparent carbon markets.
