First, the examination and evaluation of real problems that can still provide opportunities for criminals to divert and bring chemicals to drug production in various areas, especially the Golden Triangle.
Second, to continue to strengthen the effectiveness and cooperation of sharing crime information with each other.
Third, continued cooperation helps strengthen the capacity, resources and capabilities of member countries.
Fourth, to further strengthen cooperation between anti-drug institutions to reduce and eliminate drug supply and demand in the region.
