(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Politics and Foreign Affairs, Ministry of National Defense, on October 13, 2021, presented the results of the ASEAN NADI Network Workshop under the theme "Values and Role of Military History in "Strengthen and maintain peace, security and practical cooperation in the region."
At the beginning of the second day of the workshop, Lt. Gen. Nem Sovath summarized the results of the workshop on October 12, 2021 yesterday, with some important content, including:
First, through the presentations and discussions in the workshop, all participants recognized that understanding of military history is very important for the region to build trust and deepen cooperation. History as a whole, and especially military history, enables ASEAN countries to understand past events, both negative and positive, which can be lessons to learn from and avoid making mistakes like in the past.
Second, reflecting on military history, the workshop sees the role of the military not only as a tool for war, but also as a key player in peace and national identity building.
Third, some of the countries participating in the seminar presented their military history as well as their military history, all of which were maintained and organized for study and training. Train young officers to better understand history in the direction of defending national sovereignty and continuing to maintain security in their own country and in the region.
Fifth, the presentation highlighted the important role of the armed forces in peace building as well as peacekeeping. In particular, the past participation of the armed forces of each ASEAN member country in regional and international peacekeeping missions.
Sixth, the workshop also highlighted the importance of using the Fourth Industrial Revolution, technological advances as a platform for new and innovative approaches to strengthening regional cooperation through the study of military history.
Seventh, for ASEAN in the field of research as well as sharing is important. Therefore, in order to maintain strong ties and mutual understanding, ASEAN should have joint studies, such as the establishment of ASEAN Learning Centers or the ASEAN Common History Museum Network or military cooperation to increase understanding. Each other locally.
Before concluding the workshop, all participating institutions thanked and congratulated Cambodia for successfully conducting the seminar, which provided many benefits for the ASEAN region in strengthening cooperation and understanding. From each other in the field of defense to maintain peace and security in the region through the study of military history.
Through workshops on the values and role of military history in strengthening and safeguarding peace, security and cooperation in the region, it is possible to recognize and evaluate that military history is very important for ASEAN member countries and an important means in Strengthening mutual understanding and cooperation in the region through the establishment of a joint network to study military history.
