(Phnom Penh): After research by the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, it was found that the owners of some rented rooms have been selling water to workers and students at a price contrary to the agreement in the contract.
The price of water that some landlords sell to workers and students is between 1,000 Riel / cubic meter to 3,000 Riel / cubic meter, while the price of Water Supply to the landlord is only 700 Riel / cubic meter and requires the landlord to rent Resale to workers and students for only 800 riel per cubic meter.
The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority claims that the investigation was conducted after a report from the Workers' Information Center Association.
At the same time, some landlords still charge extra for the bias between the main clock and the distribution clock in the rental room, including water loss or leaks through the network connection in the rental premises, etc. Also reach an agreement between the tenant and the landlord.
Regarding the sale of water to workers and students at this high price, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will have the following measures:
* Strengthen the implementation of the above contract and take strict action against homeowners who resell water by using the water purchase contract to control the sale of water to workers and students.
Review and improve the water sales contract to be more effective to ensure effective implementation in accordance with the recommendations of the head of the Royal Government to help workers and students.
Please be informed that in accordance with the recommendation of the Head of the Royal Government, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has signed water sales contracts for 4,689 landlords for rent, equal to 121,313 rooms at a price of 700 Riels / cubic meter, which is lower than the original price and set for landlords The rent must be resold to workers and students at a price of 800 riels / cubic meter.
