Siem Reap Provincial Election Secretariat Holds a Meeting on Security, Safety and Order for Voter Registration and Voter Registration
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Election Secretariat has held a meeting on security, safety and order for the 2021 voter list and voter registration.
On October 12, Mr. Nim Van Sam, Director of Siem Reap Provincial Election Secretariat, and Mr. Koy Song, Member of Provincial Council, held a meeting on Security, Safety and Order for the upcoming 2021 Voter List and Voter Registration at the office. Siem Reap Provincial Election Secretariat.
Mr. Nim Vansam pointed out that voter registration refers to Cambodians who have the right to vote and have not previously registered to vote, who are 18 years old or older. Citizens who have moved to a new place must go to register to vote in the commune where they live or live there.
He added that the submission and receipt of applications for registration of political party agents must be signed by the chairman or representative of the political party, which has received a written transfer from the president of the political party. This transfer does not allow the transfer of rights, except in the letter of transfer that contains the content allows for the transfer of rights.
Separately, the deadline for filing and receiving applications for registration of political party agents is from October 5, 2021 to February 2, 2022 to ensure the process of reviewing the voter list and voter registration year. This 2021 is safe, secure and free of Kovid-19 disease.
It should be noted that the National Election Committee also called on all stakeholders, including political parties, associations and non-governmental organizations, media units and authorities at all levels to help disseminate the content of this appeal to the people of Cambodia. And encourage people to check the list and register to vote for everyone and on time.
