* Fourth: To increase awareness of the effects of disasters by adhering to new precautionary measures and high responsibility for clean lifestyle, personal health, personal hygiene, housing hygiene. Dispose of solid waste, reduce the use of plastic bags. Protect and maintain irrigation canals, drainage systems, drainage systems for comfortable living and well-being, avoiding various disasters.
Fifth, Ministries and Institutions at the national and sub-national levels need to strengthen disaster management mechanisms, focusing on disaster risk reduction and preparedness in response to various hazards related to climate change, in particular To the vulnerable, women, children, the elderly and the disabled.
* Sixth, the private sector, civil society development partners continue to cooperate in mobilizing the necessary resources to ensure effective implementation of disaster risk reduction for resilience to climate change.
