Kampong Speu Provincial Administration Continues to Implement Administrative Measures for 14 Days to Prevent Kovid 19
(Kampong Speu): The Kampong Speu Provincial Administration has decided to continue to issue temporary administrative measures for 14 days from October 12 to 25, 2021 to fight and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease. This is according to the decision that Fresh News received this morning, October 13, 2021.
The provincial administration has stated that during the implementation of the measures, administrative activities were temporarily suspended for activities, occupations or businesses that are at high risk of contracting Kovid 19, including: Karaoke, bars, discos and beer garden, massage business. Sell and drink all kinds of alcohol, museums, gyms and sports centers.
The provincial administration said that all the above-mentioned non-prohibited business activities must strictly implement health safety measures, such as the duty to wear a mask, the duty to maintain safety gaps, hygiene to disinfect, temperature measurement, QR Code scanning. And must follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health, in particular, must always adhere to the measures "3 do not and 3 protect" of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In addition, during the introduction of administrative measures, private gatherings of more than 10 people were suspended, except in the following cases:
* First: Reunion of family members living in the same residence or lodge * Second: Organizing funerals in accordance with health measures and as determined by the competent authorities * Third: Reunion of health workers who Perform other emergency care work * and 4th: the meeting of the competent authority, the force of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command.
