(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ken Sambath, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, stated that the implementation of value added tax (VAT) on e-commerce is a demonstration of honest and fair competition between system sellers. Online in Cambodia and abroad.
The Deputy Director General made the remarks in the program of the General Department of Taxation on "VAT on e-commerce transactions" on October 12, 2021.
"If we do not collect value added tax (VAT) from commercial activities on traders who do not have a permanent address in Cambodia and sell goods duty free (VAT), this is an injustice," he added. There is no competition between businesses with addresses in Cambodia. Focusing on these reasons, the Royal Government and the Ministry of Economy and Finance have issued sub-decrees to ensure fair competition.
He added that in order to facilitate the understanding of the value-added tax (VAT) obligation on e-commerce, the Ministry of Economy and Finance recently issued a statement detailing the procedures. Performing these activities as well.
The implementation of value added tax (VAT) on e-commerce is also often mistaken by the people as a new tax, and a senior official of the Ministry of Economy has confirmed this misunderstanding: the implementation of the tax on e-commerce. Value added to e-commerce is not a new tax.
