(Phnom Penh): After the launch of the campaign on October 11, 2021, the 19 3 doses of Kovid vaccination or booster dose is in good condition as people go to vaccinate. Enjoy.
On the morning of October 12, 2021, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief Executive Officer of the Ministry of National Defense, inspected the vaccination program in Tuol Kork and Khan. Top.
At the vaccination site, organized by the Ministry of Defense Vaccination Team, it was seen to be well organized with the strict implementation of the health rules to prevent Kovid 19, even though the population had been vaccinated in large numbers. Two doses already.
During a visit to inspect the booster dose this morning, General Ith Sarath also clarified some conditions for the booster dose given by the army. According to General Ith Sarath, the army-administered dose is given only to those who have been with the army in the first and second doses, with a gap of at least four months from the second dose.
In particular, for the people who received the first dose and the second dose with the medical team of the Ministry of Health, the army did not accept the injection. General Ith Sarath pointed out that the army's inability to inject the boost for the first and second injections, organized by the Ministry of Health, was due to some technical work on data entry.
However, the third dose, or boosting dose of the Vaccination Team of the Ministry of National Defense, facilitates the movement of people, as they can be vaccinated at a location close to where they live, without having to return to the site where they were vaccinated. In the first and second doses. For example, if the first and second doses he injected in Toul Kork district and now he lives in Kambol district, then they can find a place to inject in Kambol district and inject there.
Although most people are aware of the benefits and importance of vaccines in protecting themselves from the 19-year-old Kovid attack, the general continued to call on all citizens to participate. Vaccinate the dose to stimulate everyone.
For General Ith Sarath, the third dose of vaccination will further strengthen the health protection against Kovid 19. More importantly, vaccinating everyone will make Cambodian society more social, which allows the Royal Government to consider opening up economic activities, business and social activities more widely.
It should be noted that the army launched a 19-dose vaccination campaign in Phnom Penh on October 11, 2021. Vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense is responsible for vaccination in six districts, including: Kampoul, Dangkor, Meanchey, Por Senchey, Toul Kork, Russey Keo and factories in these six districts.
General Ith Sarath said that the total number of people in the six districts covered by the army was 1,026,126. The total number of troops to be involved in this operation is 3,578, with 152 medical teams equal to 1,091 and 2,487 personnel.
