(Pursat): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate of the Prime Minister, Director General of Electricity of Cambodia and Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat Province, this morning, October 12, 2021, led the team to bring donations from the Provincial Red Cross Branch. Handed over to 650 fishermen in Reang Til commune, Kandieng district, who suffered from food shortages during the outbreak of Kovid 19 and during the closed fishing season.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that the fishermen who live on the surface of Tonle Sap Lake in Reang Til commune, Kandieng district today have received many great achievements, directly and indirectly from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, such as the school. Learn about roads, health centers, power lines and solar panels in boats, homes and public places, not inferior to the people in the town.
Mr. Keo Rattanak added that in the past, Reang Til commune was underdeveloped, but only now, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun. Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, has considered and taken care to promote the development of infrastructure, which is the basic need of the fishermen living in this area to have a better life, reduce poverty.
He added that almost every fishing family relies entirely on fishing for their livelihood and daily livelihood, so that this business can get many benefits now and in the future, please help maintain and conserve natural resources. Which in the Tonle Sap Lake to be richer for the next generation as well.
It should be noted that the humanitarian donation of the Provincial Red Cross Branch, which was given to 650 families in Reang Til commune, Kandieng district, each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 bag of fish and 1 bag of fish sauce. Learners and monks call on the governor of Preah Vihear province, relevant institutions to intervene to build a school after the authorities of Kulen Tbong commune refused to build
(Preah Vihear): The School Construction Committee and Venerable Sean Kunleap, Preah Vihear Provincial Coordinator, through Fresh News, appealed to Mr. Prak Sovann, Preah Vihear Provincial Governor and other relevant institutions to intervene to build the school. A house on a plot of land to allow students to study after the Kulen Tbong commune chief, Kulen district, refused to build on the grounds that it was state land.
For this land, 35 meters wide and 175 meters long, located at the entrance of Wat Po 5000 Deum in Kulen Tbong Village, Kulen Tbong Commune, Kulen District, Preah Vihear Province, was approved by the former Chief of Kulen Tbong Chas Commune All stakeholders have handed over to Venerable Sien Kunleap for the construction of the school since 2016 because it is an annexed land of the commune which has been reserved since 2001.
According to the documents in the report of the meeting of Kulen Tbong Commune Council on October 16, 2021 on the handing over of a land west of O'Don Snguon antenna, 35 meters by 175 meters, with the consent of the relevant parties, as follows: In the document, Mr. Sim Sem, former chief of Kulen Tbong commune, decided to hand over the land reserved since 2001 to the Sean Koulap provincial chief for the construction of a school because it is an annex to the commune.
The construction committee, together with Venerable Sean Kunleap, "appealed to Preah Vihear provincial governor Prak Sovann and relevant institutions to intervene so that he could build a school on this land as state property."
Regarding the statement made by the construction committee together with Venerable Sien Kunleap and Mr. Son Kosal, the chief of Kulen Tbong commune, they all showed that they consider the national interest as a whole.
