(Kampong Chhnang): Rolea Bier District Authority and Kampong Chhnang Municipality Authority on the afternoon of October 11, 2021, handed over money to the families of two members who died due to 19 Kovid, who were forced to pay 1 million Riel per cremation fee. At the crematorium, Kovid 19 died in Damnak Key village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
The families of the two families are located in Trok Keut village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district. A family member named Ta Chuong Chut, over 80 years old, died of Kovid 19 on September 22, 2021, receiving a subsidy of 1 million Riels from the Rolea Bier District Administration.
The second family, a resident of Kampong Os village, Phsar Chhnang commune, Kampong Chhnang city, had a family member named Lach Lo, 42 years old, who died of Kovid 19 on September 24, 2021, received 1 million subsidy from Kampong Chhnang City Hall. Riel as well.
Mr. Seng Vichet, Deputy Governor of Rolea Bier District, confirmed that he had handed over the money to the families of the victims who had died due to 19 Kovid in Prok Village, Sre Thmei Commune, Rolea Bier District and had been burnt for a cremation. That million riel, now the district administration has taken 1 million riel to pay back to the family of the corpse instead of Pluk.
Meanwhile, the families of the two families thanked the provincial, district and municipal authorities and the team for taking into account the plight of those who lost family members due to Kovid-19 and returned the money to each of them. This family 1 million riel. They are overjoyed and wish the authorities and the team happiness, prosperity and success in all their endeavors.
It should be noted that as of October 10, 2021, there were 108 deaths due to Kovid-19 in Kampong Chhnang province. As for the policy of the provincial governor, as well as the provincial health department, it has never issued a policy to allow the collection of funds from the families of the bodies that died due to Kovid 19. This was confirmed by Mr. Am Sophea, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province.
On the other hand, Ms. O Vandin, a spokesperson for the Ministry of Health, also confirmed that the cremation of 19 people born in Kovid was free of charge, and that the cremation of 19 people in Kovid had a proper subcommittee.
