(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on October 12, 2021 decided to allow technical and vocational education and training institutions under the auspices of all ministries to reopen after the situation of Kovid 19 epidemic. There is a slight decrease. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News.
1: Apply for reopening to the ECCC Management and Evaluation Committee Re-review to evaluate re-authorization.
2. Sign a contract with the Ministry to ensure that the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) are implemented for the operation of the ECCC. Again in the context of Kovid-19 disease, dated October 8, 2021, Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
3. Establish a working group to prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19 disease at the ECCC.
4: Assign 2 focal points in charge of work, responsible for communication and information.
