Mr. Sar Sokha instructed the leadership of Chea Sim Kamchay Mear University to continue to improve health and hygiene in the context of Kovid 19 by following the "3 protection and 3 don't" approach.
(Prey Veng): Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, instructed the management of Chea Sim Kamchay Mear University to continue to improve health and hygiene in the context of Kovid 19 by following the "3 prevent and 3 prevent" approach and participate in preventing infection. Kovid 19 in the School of Health Safety Education.
Mr. Sar Sokha made this instruction on the occasion that he invited a representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports to preside over the opening ceremony of the new school year 2021-2022 of Chea Sim University. Kamchay Mear in Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, through the Zoom video system this morning, October 12, 2021.
On that occasion, on behalf of the Academy, Minister Sar Sokha would like to thank the leadership, professors, teachers, academic staff of Chea Sim Kamchay Mear University, parents, guardians and all students who overcame all obstacles to support and Provides excellent teaching and learning during the course of Kovid-19 disease.
In that, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has been paying attention to the first: the protection of health and safety of students and the second: the resumption of students' education.
"We know that school closures are affecting the education of our young people, because we do not know when Kovid 19 will end," said Sar Sokha. Therefore, we must be prepared to protect the health and safety of students by strictly implementing the measures of the Royal Government of Cambodia that have been put out effectively.
In addition, Mr. Sar Sokha also addressed the leadership and academic staff and all students of Chea Sim Kamchay Mear University as follows:
* First, please continue to improve health and hygiene in the context of Kovid 19 by following the "3 prevent and 3 do not" approach and participate in preventing Kovid 19 infection in educational health safety education.
* Third: Focus on the implementation of innovative teaching methods and the application of new teaching methods in the 21st century, which is a mixed approach, with students practicing in the classroom and self-study, focusing on education, science, technology, engineering. And mathematics, a necessary skill in the new era.
* Fourth: To continue to improve the qualifications and capacity of teachers, especially teaching and learning in modern technology by improving and developing new infrastructure in classrooms, laboratories, computer rooms and lecturers according to the actual situation and situation.
And 5: To pay attention to strengthening the implementation of roles and responsibilities in leading and managing for the quality of students' education, efficiency and participation in maintaining the university's infrastructure and other achievements for long-term use. After Pchum Ben Ceremony: Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration Tests Quickly 8 Civil Servants Under Kovid
(Tbong Khmum): After taking a break for 3 days on the occasion of Pchum Ben, Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration has launched a quick test campaign for civil servants in departments / units around the province, civil servants, municipalities, districts, communes, Sangkat, academic staff, teachers - Teachers and students at the reopened educational institution to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Tbong Khmum province.
At the same time, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, called on the leaders, civil servants and all citizens to work together to prevent this infection according to the "3 do not 3 prevent" by continuing to wear masks to keep the social gap, keep clean hands. With alcohol or soap, that is, remember that "prevention is better than cure."
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Provincial Governor, advised the civil servants in the departments / units around the province to take a quick test for everyone to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 when entering the profession. Respectively.
As of the afternoon of October 11, 2021, Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration has organized a rapid test sample at Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration to 454 civil servants under the provincial administration and departments / units around the province, 178 females, as a result Eight positive Kovid 19 individuals were found.
