NEC Releases Results of Third Dissemination Meeting with Stakeholders via Video
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) issued a press release on the results of the third outreach meeting with stakeholders via video this morning, October 11, 2021.
The NEC organized an online video conference with stakeholders chaired by NEC member Mean Sati to publicize the launch of the voter list review and commune voter registration procedures. Voter names in communes / sangkats, transmission of data to the NEC and provisional results of the distribution of voter registration invitations.
During the meeting, Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the NEC and chair of the meeting, stated that the examination of the voter list and voter registration lasted for 50 days, from October 12 to 30. November 2021.
He added that Cambodians living in communes who are at least 18 years old as of the date of the Commune / Sangkat Council Election, which will take place on June 5, 2022, are born before or by the 6th month. June 2004 Those who are not yet on the voter list of the commune where they live can apply to register to vote directly with the voter registration team.
For the submission of voter registration data, the voter registration team must be sent online to the NEC on a daily basis for the NEC to conduct regular inspections.
Mr. Mean Sati also highlighted the results of the distribution of invitations to voters as of October 11, 2021, distributed 7,916,745, equal to 89.64%. The invitation will be kept at the commune hall where the residents are living to continue distributing it to those who have not yet received their voter registration.
During the meeting, the NEC clarified the statements made by the stakeholders as follows:
Kovid 19 case is a challenge to register to vote, but the NEC already has preventive measures in place, and the NEC would like to thank the local authorities for their support in providing Kovid 19 prevention materials.
* Additional polling stations have been set up for six newly established communes based on population.
* The NEC has produced a number of radio, television and social media programs to inspire people to get information about voter registration. In particular, there is the participation of all stakeholders, including village chiefs and the spirit of participation of the people.
Stakeholders who attended the online video meeting included representatives of the Constitutional Council, the Senate, the National Assembly, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Information, Japanese Embassy officials, representatives of political parties, NGOs, media units and NEC officials, with a total of approximately 75 participants. . Senior Australian Embassy official praises Cambodia's Kovid 19 vaccination in ASEAN
