1 Million Riel from a Family of 19 Kovid Members Dead in Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Two families living in Kampong Chhnang province whose family members died due to Kovid-19 claimed that they were required to pay 1 million Riels for the cremation of one body.
One of the two families, a resident of Trok Keut village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, had a family member who died of Kovid-19 on September 22, 2021 and was taken by ambulance. To cremate at a newly established cremation site in Damnak Key village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district.
When the cremation is completed, the cremation committee there requires the family to pay 1 million riel for the cremation fee and 100,000 riel for the hospital vehicle that transported the body for cremation. The commission said that the 1 million riel was given to the department, but did not say which department. This is the claim of Mr. Prak Long, the family of the deceased living in the above commune village.
Mr. Sar Leang, Director of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Cult, confirmed by telephone this morning, October 11, 2021, that in the past, the cremation of Kovid-19 was the province that paid $ 700 per corpse. However, since the construction of the new crematorium, only one million riel per corpse, and the cost of cremation of the Kovid-19, the provincial administration has handed over to the districts as their respective departures.
Later, the districts and cities could not afford to pay for the cremation of Kovid-19, so the provincial health department issued a letter instructing the families of the bodies of Kovid-19 to come and be cremated at the crematorium. New in Cheung Kreav commune and the family helps to pay their own money to be before Mr. Pongsol and Achar, etc. according to their ability.
However, those in charge of cremation asked for 1 million riel for each cremation fee, as they had to pay for firewood and labor costs, and sometimes had to be cremated overnight. The cult department has no policy to take money from the family of the deceased Kovid-19 who was cremated, only to facilitate the cremation.
After the construction of the new crematorium, the provincial health department also issued a notice of cremation of the deceased due to Kovid-19, allowing the family to come and receive the body to be cremated at the designated place:
* 1: Cremation at the crematorium in Damnak Key village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district. * 2: Monasteries with proper cremation in Kampong Chhnang province and with the consent of the people in the community.
As of October 10, 2021, there were 108 deaths due to Kovid-19 in Kampong Chhnang province, he said. As for the policy of the provincial governor, as well as the provincial health department, it has never issued a policy to allow the collection of funds from the families of the bodies that died due to Kovid 19.
The Ministry of Health states that the cremation of the 19-year-old was not charged, and that the cremation of the 19th had a proper subcommittee. This is according to Mrs. O Vandin, spokesperson for the Ministry of Health.
