Military official reacts to defamation case over land dispute that has ended in court
(Preah Vihear): A military officer standing on the 1st Battlefield of Preah Vihear Province reacted and completely rejected the broadcast of a local online TV station defaming him in connection with a land dispute in the commune. Choam Ksan, Choam Ksan district, which has been settled in court.
Brigadier General Poch Sokchea described by recalling the history of the land dispute that he had sold a plot of land 170 meters wide by 180 meters long with a total area of 25,500 square meters to Mr. Omsin in 2017. With this sale, Mr. Oum Sin also asked to help make a letter of transfer to his son named Sin Chandun, with the acknowledgment of the village chief An Ses and the commune chief Choam Ksan on May 30, 2017.
Mr. Poch Sokchea described that after agreeing to sell, Sin Chandun suddenly refused, saying that the land was not enough. Not wanting to have a long story, he also agreed to transfer for the second time, expanding the area to 33,791 square meters and recognized by the District Land Office and the District Governor Choam Ksan on January 25, 20219.
Despite such expansion, the conflict is not over. Sin Chandun tried to sue again. However, the court ruled that Poch Sokchea had won both the Preah Vihear Provincial Court and the Court of Appeal.
According to Mr. Poch Sokchea, the verdict of the Preah Vihear Provincial Court dated June 10, 2019 decided to drop the charges against him. Separately, the judgment of Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal dated August 10, 2021 decided to reject the appeal against the law. Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal also upheld the Closing Order dated 15 December 2020 of the Investigating Judge of Preah Vihear Provincial Court.
Mr. Poch Sokchea expressed his doubts and did not understand the intent of the online TV broadcast that why try to break the story that he has finished?
Brigadier General Poch Sokchea stated, "It has been about three years since the Preah Vihear Provincial Court and the Court of Appeal ruled in my favor. But recently, an online TV station quoted an old lawsuit filed by one of my parties, which caused a great deal of confusion, especially to the detriment of my honor and my family. "
Mr. Sok Chea expressed his regret that the online TV broadcast was really damaging to his reputation. In particular, confuse the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command and the Army Command.
In order to be clean, Mr. Poch Sokchea sought a lawyer and wrote a written letter to the online television to request that the content be corrected and that his misunderstandings be repeated.
Mr. Poch Sokchea claimed that if the online TV case is not broadcast, he will complain to the court to take action according to the law.
