(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of October 11, 2021, Lieutenant General Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, represented by General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the National Police Chief. National Police Commission. The ceremony was held at the meeting hall of the General Commission of the National Police, in strict accordance with the health rules.
After Major General Chhoeun Bunchon, the newly-appointed Director of the Radio Communication Department, made a commitment to the presidency and the ceremony.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun congratulated the new director of the department, emphasizing that the current change of position is a code of conduct that must not be changed by the change of senior officials in the unit. Part of the reform of the National Police to be a step forward to meet the real needs of the job and also the opportunities and experiences of National Police officers.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun supported and agreed with the commitment of the newly announced director of the department, and what is important is to lead the unit to progress, have sufficient capacity to serve as a commanding officer.
He added that the strengthening of the unit is an effort to strengthen the skills to expand the scope, especially radio communication skills to cover all provinces. He instructed the new director of the radio communication department and the former director of the department to meet and discuss in order to hand over the special work, the remaining work and technical equipment, while having a clear handover record.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police also gave a key recommendation to the new director of the department that as the leader of the unit, he must be a role model and a leader with clear common sense, strengthen discipline, strengthen internal unity, can not touch hand to foot, foot to foot. Emotional, friendly, gentle but firm, especially the division of responsibilities according to skills to be transparent.
As for the technical work, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun also urged the new Director of the Radio Communication Department to strengthen the technical work related to radio frequencies, which in the future, Cambodia will have important national and international events, especially Cambodia will host Organize many important meetings as well.
At the same time, he stressed the need to pay attention to the work of the command, because this work has brought services closer to the people, especially the intervention, rescue, suppression and problem solving quickly, and he also urged the new director of the department. Make internal regulations for the efficiency of the work of the command team as well.
Finally, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, urged the new director of the radio communication department to study the preparation of standards under various laws to strengthen the role in controlling the use of radio communication equipment.
