According to Mr. Su Sunthara, two officials from the Department of Public Works and Transport had previously contracted 19 cases of Kovid, but did not spread the disease to other officials in the department. They received medical treatment until they recovered.
Please also note that after testing the above 94 officials, as a result, none of the officers were positive for Kovid 19.
Former Deputy Governor of Prey Nup District and Former Commune Chief of Bit Trang, as well as 8 members of their party, were arrested for illegal encroachment and clearing in many cases in Preah Sihanouk Province.
(Preah Sihanouk): The specialized police force of the General Commission of Police in cooperation with the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police has launched a search operation to arrest a total of eight ringleaders and their accomplices, including the former Deputy Governor of Prey Nup District and the former Chief of Bit Trang Commune. Many cases of illegal encroachment, clearing and occupation of land in Sihanoukville province.
According to a report obtained by Fresh News on the afternoon of October 11, 2021, these ringleaders and gangs of illegal land grabbers always have brokers and fake document preparation groups lying to the leaders to encroach on their land. And many state lands located in Sihanoukville.
The suspects were subsequently arrested on the orders of Lt. Gen. Di Vichea, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police and Chairman of the Commission for the Collection and Investigation of Land Cases and the Prevention and Suppression of Illegal Land Acquisition. Yim Leang is the Vice President and the team members in cooperation with the relevant professional authorities in Sihanoukville.
As a result, after launching an investigation, the force arrested 8 suspects and was charged with trespassing, occupying and clearing the state land illegally in many cases, including forgery of documents. The public also uses fake public documents and false statements.
According to the report of the Commission for the Collection of Information to Investigate Land Cases and Prevent and Suppress Illegal Invasion of State Land, the eight suspects include:
* Second: Name: Ros Bithol, Male, 39 years old, Born in Tya Ampil Village, Baray Commune, Srey Santhor District, Kampong Cham Province.
* Third: Name: Nhok Kim Tong, Male, 41 years old, Place of Birth: Slap Ktong Village, Chob Commune, Tbong Khmum District, Kampong Cham Province.
5th: Name: Vet Veth, Male, 45 years old, Born in Siem Reap Province, Occupation: Land broker, Role: Fake document
* 6th: Name: Keo Veasna (pseudonym) Real name: Moul Sok Khoeun, Preah Athit journalist
* Seventh: Pheng Sophal is involved in a case of forgery of public documents, theft of real estate, legal ownership of other people's land in Koki village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
* Eighth: Duong Sibunthol is accused of committing the crime of threatening to kill, losing faith in the court's decision, falsifying documents, using violence against righteous property occupants, inciting and causing land riots, causing chaos to the authorities. Province.
It is noteworthy that this arrest is a warning to those in power who are behind the encroachment and seizure of land, whether state or private, to the real landowners. These people will have to act in strict accordance with the law, there are no exceptions.
According to the report, these suspects are skilled in making fake documents, going back in time to pretend that they have land and have been occupying land for many years, which has led to many land disputes in the province. Sihanoukville. Koh Kong Province Announces 19 Infant Deaths Due to Kovid
