Kang Meas District Governor Phok Savuth said that the river bank in the above commune village collapsed about 100 meters, but this case did not endanger the people. However, the landslide affected the homes of five families, one of which was at risk.
The district governor confirmed that after the provincial governor accompanied by relevant professional officials inspected the study, the provincial governor provided oil and instructed the district authorities together with the officials of the provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to cooperate in installing the rainwater pump. Near the house of the people out.
Separately, for a house that is facing collapse, must monitor the situation, that is, if the river bank continues to collapse, the district authorities will help remove the house from the danger area immediately on the instructions of the provincial governor.
