Khmer Civilization Expert: How should the definition of the nation's top leaders be "unique Khmer nationality" reflect the traditional values of Khmer leaders from ancient times?
How does the definition of the nation's top leaders having a single nationality reflect the traditional values of Cambodian leaders since ancient times?
Obviously, as we have seen, during the election campaign or when the top leaders of the nation or politicians take office, each legislature of the National Assembly always swears allegiance to its deities, deities, or ancestors, as loyal to the nation by daring to sacrifice. Everything in the cause of the nation, the motherland and the people.
This shows that the ancient Khmer not only had a nationalist philosophy, loved the motherland and its people while still alive, but also to the next nation, because leadership is nothing superior to the motherland and its people. No. This is what made the Khmer kingdom during the Angkorian Empire strong, glorious, and famous all over the continent.
Finally, Mr. Rath Sandab stated that if this is the case, the top leaders of the nation must have the same nationality when the country is fully peaceful and all this development is able to see clearly that Which politicians are truly loyal to the nation and the people?
