Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh: Government policy to vaccinate Kovid 19 as the first belt to protect people's lives
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers the policy of vaccinating Kovid 19 as a key strategy and the first important protection belt to protect people's lives. People to increase immunity in the community against Kovid 19.
This statement was made by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh during the opening ceremony of the campaign to vaccinate against 19 19 doses of Kovid disease or to encourage people living in Phnom Penh on Monday morning, October 11, 2021.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh said: "The Royal Government considers the policy of vaccinating Kovid 19 as a key strategy and the first and foremost protection belt to protect the lives of the people to increase. "Gain community immunity against Kovid 19 to move towards a full national recovery in all areas and to live with the disease in a new normal way."
At the same time, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh continued that the vaccination of Kovid 19 quickly and timely saved the lives of many Cambodians by reducing the number of cases, cases of serious illness and death of Kovid 19 and Avoid Cambodia from the disaster caused by Kovid 19 and keep the current situation of Kovid 19 outbreak at a manageable level.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh confirmed that in 2021, Kovid 19 will continue to spread to all countries in the world with increasing uncertainty through the transformation of many new Kovid 19 viruses, especially viruses. The new "Delta" transformer, which has a higher transmission capacity and can endanger people's lives even more.
In addition, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh emphasized that in the framework of the new virus zone, some countries that used to control the infection well but still lost their lives have increased significantly. At a time when vaccination rates for the population are still low.
With these measures, the Royal Government has identified vaccination as a key strategic measure aimed at achieving community solicitation, which is a motivating factor in ensuring a rapid return to a "new normal" of life. Daily life of Cambodians in general and socio-economic processes.
The Royal Government is committed to continuing to promote vaccination as soon as possible and achieving the plan to build community resilience and to reopen domestic tourism and the previously stagnant socio-economic sector.
