After the operation from last night until this evening, the water situation on the border of Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province has improved and does not threaten people's homes.
(Phnom Penh): From the night until the evening of October 10, 2021, the working group of the Ministry of Water Resources has been continuing the operation of the water surface at Canal 96 to avoid flooding and affect the homes of people at the border. Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
After the launch of the naval operation under the direct command of Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Honorary General Hing Bun Heang, Commander of the Bodyguard Command, the water situation has improved and is no longer threatening the homes of the people.
Please note that this flood is not a flood of Stung Prek Tnaot, it is a flood of rain, but it is not serious, this is because the natural drainage route is narrow, which is different from the existing natural waterway, causing The release of water through canals, canals and lakes to the Bassac River has been blocked due to the completion or closure and by the construction of roads and some structures do not comply with the proper technical conditions to maintain waterways.
The official confirmed on October 10, "The flood of Stung Prek Tnaot has not happened yet. This water receives water from Laing Chrey in Kampong Speu province, from Nong to Dam 7 Makara, there is no water, the water is declining. In particular, the water under the bridge on January 7 in Sak Sampov, Dangkor district, Kandal province, was flooded a lot because the water came from Kampong Speu, we dropped it to the bottom so that we could resist and fear the flood from Prek Tnaot, Kampong Speu.
"So far, the water in Stung Prek Tnaot has not been a threat to Phnom Penh or the lower provinces such as Kandal and Takeo," he said. "If the weather is good, there will be no flooding." However, the water resources official confirmed that if there is any change, the Ministry of Water Resources will notify.
Although the water situation has not been threatened or reached a state of emergency. But professional officials and local authorities are constantly monitoring and preparing to help people in case of flooding. Cut his wife with two swords, causing serious injuries in Svay Chrum district, her husband jumped into the water to escape, but drowned
(Svay Rieng): A woman was stabbed by her husband with two swords, causing serious injuries, but the authorities and neighbors helped to take Asamin to the emergency room at Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital. He beheaded his wife and jumped into the water to escape, but when he arrived, he drowned.
This incident happened on the night of October 9, 2021 at Angkas Dey village, Ta Suos commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province.
Svay Chrum District Police Inspector Pin An said that the cause of the violence was that the husband was initially drunk and had a verbal dispute with his wife, which led to the murder of his wife. The husband ran to the back of the house, jumped the fence and jumped into the Prek Ta Suos bridge while the water was flowing. The villain disappeared. The woman's family was rushed to Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital.
The police chief said that the body of the husband was found by villagers at 10 am on October 10 at Prek Ta Suos bridge, Ang Keas Dey village, Ta Suos commune, Svay Chrum district.
According to Inspector Pin An, the victim's wife is 42-year-old Peng Bunnary, a factory worker living in Angkas Dey village, Ta Suos commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province. The suspect is Mao Phearun, 37 years old, a farmer living in the above commune.
The inspector confirmed that the suspect who hacked his wife had beaten her several times, but this time to the point of using violence to kill his wife.
Mr. Pin An said that after finding the body of the suspect who killed his wife, the police have set up a commission with the participation of experts and doctors to perform an autopsy, in which the police concluded that the suspect really died. Because of real drowning.
According to villagers, before the incident, the suspect's husband was seen leaving the drinking circle drunk and returned home to find his wife arguing. Later, the husband pulled out a sword and cut his wife with two swords, one in the right ear and one in the left arm, causing serious injuries, causing surprise.
