More than 1,000 Families in Kampong Luong Commune, Krakor District Receive Humanitarian Donations from Pursat Red Cross Branch
(Pursat): A total of 1,025 fishing families living on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake in Kampong Luong commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, who suffered from food shortages during the outbreak of Kovid 19 and during the closed fishing season, received donations. Humanitarian from Pursat Red Cross Branch.
The distribution of Red Cross donations to the above fishermen took place in the presence of Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of Electricite du Cambodge and Honorary President of Pursat Red Cross Branch on October 10, 2021.
On that occasion, Mr. Keo Rattanak brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Mao Thunin, Chairman of the Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee. Take into account the hardships of the people, especially the fishermen who live on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake because they are affected by the spread of Kovid 19 disease and in the closed season can not go out to do business.
He added that through the working group and the provincial authorities have prepared a request to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to provide social land concessions to about 987 families in Kampong Luong commune, with each family receiving agricultural land and residential land. 1.5 hectares at the point "Dambok 100" in Dambok 100 village, Tnaot Chum commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, so that they can move from living on the water to live on land.
At the same time, he urged the people to come and live on the allotted land to work hard to raise animals and grow other crops on this land as much as possible. In case of shortage of raw materials, the team will help to solve according to the actual needs. The important thing is to keep this allotted land for a long time to come, which is the hope of the leaders.
He said that Krakor district is one of the priority districts in Pursat province where the head of the Royal Government as well as the working group have tried to mobilize many investors to develop, create a labor market and improve people's livelihood through the establishment of special economic zones. Garment factory, solar transformer assembly plant ... and recently the most honorable for the province to receive a huge investment in Ford car assembly and assembly.
He urged the fishermen to continue to implement the "3 Do 3 Protect" measures of the Royal Government and the measures of the Ministry of Health to prevent and cut the transmission of Kovid 19 as soon as possible and encourage people as well as nieces and nephews from Children between the ages of 6 and 12 must receive additional doses to get their schools reopened nationwide.
