General knowledge: Has Cambodia ever had a volcanic eruption?
(Phnom Penh): Scientists have discovered that the Earth has been volcanic for billions of years, and until now, there are still volcanic eruptions, especially in countries such as Indonesia, Chile, Japan, Ethiopia, the Philippines, Guatemala. And so on. But did you know that Cambodia has had volcanic eruptions?
If we talk about the period from prehistoric times to the present, Cambodia has never had a volcanic eruption, but if we talk about tens of thousands of years ago, our country has had volcanic eruptions.
Through research and evidence found that Cambodia has had many volcanic eruptions in the past. Yeak Laom Lake in Ratanakkiri Province is one of the largest inert volcanoes in Cambodia. The lake is about 50-70 meters deep, about 800 meters in diameter and is about 700,000 years old.
