Banteay Meanchey Armed Forces Detain 29 Cambodian Workers Intended to Cross Illegally to Thailand
(Banteay Meanchey): In order to prevent illegal border crossings, the Banteay Meanchey Military Operations Area has issued strict orders to all forces to patrol on a regular basis, 24 hours a day, alternating hours and to have good cooperation. With the Joint Forces to ensure the prevention of all illegal cross-border crimes and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in its area of responsibility.
In fact, on the evening of October 7, 2021, Brigadier General Chim Bun An, Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Military Operations Area, ordered Brigadier General Rith Rom, Deputy Commander of the Malay Command, to lead 15 troops on patrol. Along the border in its direction, including cooperation with the Border Police No. 815.
During the geography of Lvea village, Boeung Beng commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province, the above-mentioned joint forces also found 29 workers who intended to cross the border to Thailand and arrested them for interrogation. After educating and interrogating, the force sent all the workers to work as a transistor at the transistor center in Malai district.
It should be noted that since the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Operational Area Forces conducted joint operations with the Joint Task Force to Prevent Cross-Border Workers and Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid-19 Disease, they have been arresting migrant workers and sending them to Chattali Sak Center. Some brokers have sent to the competent authorities to take legal action.
Commander Chim Bun An urged the people, especially those who intend to migrate to work in Thailand, not to be deceived by brokers who often persuade illegal migrant workers, regardless of their safety and money. Subsequent.
