Foreign Ministry announces results of telephone conversation between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Australian Foreign Minister
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation announced on the night of October 08, 2021, the results of a telephone conversation between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Ms. Mariss Pan, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. The Australian Minister for Women's Affairs, who tweeted this morning.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, obtained by Fresh News, the two Foreign Ministers discussed bilateral cooperation and a number of regional and international issues of common interest and concern. Including the recently established Australia-UK-US Trilateral Security Partnership (AUKUS).
Ms Penn reaffirmed Australia's continued support for the ASEAN Middle East and the principles set out in the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Vision (AOIP). She stressed that Australia is committed to adhering to its obligations under the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation (TAC), the South Pacific Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (SPNWFZ) and the Southeast Asian Nuclear-Weapon-Free Zone (SEANWFZ).
The Deputy Prime Minister also encouraged Australia and ASEAN's external partners to further support the four priority areas of cooperation set out in the ASEAN Indo-Pacific Vision (AOIP), including maritime cooperation. Linking the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and cooperation in the economic and other spheres.
