(Phnom Penh): A female weed deer trapped in the Sang Ruk Vorn Wildlife Sanctuary in Oddar Meanchey province was rescued and released back into the wild on October 7, 2021. . This was said by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment on the afternoon of October 8, 2021.
At the same time, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment praised the rangers of the Sangkha Ruk Voan Wildlife Sanctuary of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Environment for rescuing the deer, which is a relatively endangered species and is on the organization's red list. The IUCN was on time.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that rangers have played an important role in protecting and conserving natural resources, not just patrolling to prevent and crack down on natural resource crimes, illegal forest encroachment or illegal logging. But it also plays a role in rescuing wildlife and other biodiversity by removing traps and rescuing wildlife from traps.
According to the report, in the first nine months of 2021, park officials released nearly 30,000 traps, released them from protected areas across the country, and rescued many wildlife.
According to expert studies, deer are relatively endangered species and are listed on the IUCN Red List as Conservation Consistent in specific areas where they live. Deer are present in protected areas in the north-southwest and northeastern regions of Cambodia. It is also found in India, China and Southeast Asia, including Sumatra, Java and Borneo.
Deer like to eat soil, especially deer, which are growing horns, and there is an annual reddening of horn antlers in July and September. During the breeding season, the male deer often fight to control the area and wear up to eight females in the herd. Use only one female at a time after 8 months of gestation.
Once again, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Neth Pheaktra called on people to stop hunting and eating wild animals because they have no health benefits but may pose a health risk and cause diseases because wild animals contain Infected by "saying no to wildlife meat to stop hunting and trapping animals."
In addition, he confirmed that those who continue to violate the ban will face the law in force if the authorities.
