(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, on October 08, 2021, had a telephone conversation with Ms. Mariss Pence, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Minister of Women's Affairs of Australia.
Through his official Facebook page, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon confirmed that the two sides discussed a number of issues, including a trilateral security partnership between Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States called "AUKUS".
He asserted that in a telephone conversation, Australian Foreign Minister and Minister for Women's Affairs Mary Pann stated that AUKUS intends to promote peace and security in the Indo-Pacific region and will respect ASEAN and the ASEAN perspective. Indo-Pacific.
