Statement by Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin: Determining "Unique Khmer Nationality" for the Leaders of the Top National Institutions to Ensure the Standing and Unwavering Commitment to the Nation, Motherland and People
(Phnom Penh): The enactment of the law to determine the "only Khmer nationality" for the leaders of the four top institutions of the nation has a strong purpose to ensure both legal and political guarantees for the position and unwavering commitment to the motherland. And people in all circumstances.
In a statement read by Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, the Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers stressed the purpose of the law: "To ensure both legal and political solemnity to the position and commitment "Unwavering to the motherland and the people of Cambodia in all circumstances and to ensure the protection of the interests of the nation and the people of Cambodia from foreign interference."
Phnom Penh Capital Hall Reminds Parents, Guardians and Child Care Center Managers to Bring Children Aged 6 to Under 12 to Get 19 Kovid Vaccines Before Campaign Closing
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on October 8, 2021 issued a reminder to parents, guardians and managers of child care centers in Phnom Penh to bring children from 6 years old to under 12 years old. Get vaccinated against Kovid 19 before the end of the campaign. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News.
The Ministry of Tourism decided to establish a working group to coordinate the implementation of tourism projects of development partners to mobilize partners to participate in the restoration and development of Cambodia's tourism sector.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism on October 08, 2021 issued a decision to establish a Coordinating Working Group on "Implementation of Tourism Partners' Tourism Project Implementation" to mobilize partners to participate in the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia's tourism sector, coordinate and evaluate project implementation. Tourism of development partners of national and international organizations in Cambodia.
The decision states that the working group is headed by a Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and one Secretary as the Director of the Department of Tourism Development Planning, with the following roles and responsibilities:
* Seek development partners from national and international organizations to provide financial and technical support to promote the development of Cambodia's tourism sector through the implementation of priority development projects of the Ministry of Tourism and the implementation of tourism development master plans in the provinces and major tourism poles. .
Facilitate research, provide information and data to development partners, national and international organizations to study tourism development projects.
Prepare a list of priority projects of the specialized departments under the Ministry of Tourism.
* Work with development partners, national and international organizations to coordinate and orient the implementation of projects in the tourism sector.
* Evaluate the achievements on the main results of the implementation of projects in the tourism sector.
* Organize annual workshops to disseminate the results of project implementation of development partners of national and international organizations and present a list of priority projects of various departments under the Ministry of Tourism to mobilize additional support.
