(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia said that after receiving the notification, the owners of left-hand drive vehicles that take refuge under various license plates and duty-free and right-hand drive vehicles without duty came to fulfill their tax obligations. To avoid fines and other crackdowns. This is according to the announcement of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on October 8, 2021.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has once again called on the owners of left-hand drive vehicles that take refuge under various license plates and duty-free and right-hand drive vehicles without duty to fulfill their tax obligations by December 31, 2021. To receive 10% tax and tax relief.
At the same time, the right-hand drive car must complete the steering wheel from right to left by June 30, 2022.
Please note that from January 1 to June 30, 2022, tax-free left-hand drive vehicles will be taxed in full, with no preferential tax breaks. At the end of the deadline, from July 1, 2022 onwards, duty-free vehicles will be subject to strict and severe crackdowns, and after the crackdown, right-hand drive vehicles will be disassembled or destroyed.
