(Phnom Penh): An old man was stabbed to death by an unknown assailant in bed at 7:30 am on October 08, 2021 at a plot of land on a dirt road in Koh Krabei 1 village. Sangkat Prek Thmey, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
The victim was 71-year-old Ath Soth, a caretaker of a plantation in Koh Krabei 1 village, Sangkat Prek Thmey, Khan Chbar Ampov, and his wife was 43-year-old Nath Ny.
Chbar Ampov District Police Chief Mao Soeuth confirmed that after receiving the information, he immediately led the force to the scene and found a 70-year-old man dead on the bed and the victim was sleeping in the same bed with his wife. Presumably the first step was a murder case.
Chbar Ampov District Inspector confirmed that for this murder case, the local force cooperated with the specialized force of the forensic office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and the medical team to take the body sample first and check for 19 Kovid virus to confirm that the body of the victim Have 19 Kovid's disease or not.
According to the forensic examination of the police, the victim suffered 6 stab wounds on the body, with serious injuries to the head, sprains, right side, and 4 other backs. The suspect used a large knife (possibly a knife). Lion bread). In this case, the Phnom Penh forensic officer concluded that it was a murder case and handed over the body to the family to take to the traditional ceremony at home.
In the case of the above murder, the competent authorities are conducting a very careful investigation to find the killer and bring him to justice.
