General knowledge: When did seawater occur?
About 4,500 million years ago, the earth was different from what it is today, with no oceans and seas. Volcanoes spewed ash and gas all over the planet, at which time the planet was much hotter than it is today.
Volcanic gas, combined with various gases and water vapor, began to form the planet's atmosphere. As the atmosphere evolved, the earth cooled. About 4 billion years ago, the earth cooled enough to cause water vapor to condense and rain.
