Draft amendments to the Constitution and additional constitutions related to the determination of a single Khmer nationality for the leaders of the nation's top institutions have been approved by the Council of Ministers and are ready to be sent to the National Assembly.
The Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers was chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, with the participation of various members of the Royal Government, including four agendas that were discussed and approved as follows:
1: Draft Constitutional Law on the Amendment of Article 19 (new), Article 42 (new), Article 106 (new), Article 119 (new) and Article 13 (new) of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 3 of the Additional Constitution to ensure the normal functioning of national institutions
2: Draft Law on Public-Private Partnership
4: Other issues Requesting the approval of the Council of Ministers to seek the approval of the legislature on the draft law on the approval of the agreement in addition to the agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations regarding the trial. Under Cambodian law, crimes committed during the period of Democratic Kampuchea on arrangements during the transition and termination of the Extraordinary Chambers.
Mr. Phay Siphan, Spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia, stated that the preparation of the draft Constitution on the amendment of Article 19 (new), Article 82, Article 106 (new), Article 119 (new), Article 119 (new) and Article 137 (new) of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 3 and Article 4 Of the supplementary constitutional law aimed at ensuring the normal functioning of national institutions.
