This morning, the Council of Ministers will hold a plenary meeting to discuss and approve the draft amendments to the Constitution and additional constitutions that determine the nationality of the heads of the top institutions.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 8, 2021, the Council of Ministers of Cambodia will hold its plenary session to discuss and approve the draft amendments to the Constitution and the Constitution in relation to the determination of the nationality of Cambodia's top institutions.
The Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers was chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, with the participation of members of the Royal Government. The agenda of the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers on October 8, 2021 is as follows:
1: Draft Constitutional Law on the Amendment of Article 19 (new), Article 42 (new), Article 106 (new), Article 119 (new) and Article 13 (new) of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 3 of the Additional Constitution to ensure the normal functioning of national institutions .
2: Draft Law on Public-Private Partnership.
4: Other issues Requesting the approval of the Council of Ministers to seek the approval of the legislature on the draft law on the approval of the agreement in addition to the agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations regarding the trial. Under Cambodian law, crimes committed during the period of Democratic Kampuchea on the arrangements during the transition and termination of the Extraordinary Chambers.
