On this third holiday, all 25 tourist destinations in the capital and provinces have opened to receive tourists, including Kampong Chhnang, which has previously suspended the first and second holiday resorts.
Meanwhile, the flow of visitors continues to visit until the weekend, while the journey into Phnom Penh is not crowded yet. Accommodation at major tourist destinations is fully booked on both the first and second day. But on the third day, bookings were somewhat reduced as some people returned to Phnom Penh.
As for the special service fee, the price of accommodation and food is not overdue, it is in a reasonable level without any significant incident.
Most of the people participated in implementing measures to prevent Kovid-19, especially wearing masks almost 100%. But keeping the gap is still the main factor that needs to be paid more attention to education, guidance and reminders, especially in some tourist destinations that are very attractive.
At all tourism destinations, the Capital-Provincial Administration and the Department of Tourism have made efforts to inspect, educate, and guide the implementation of the "3-Do and 3-Protection" measures, tourism safety rules, and minimum standard operating procedures (SOPs).
The private sector, from major tourism operators such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and tourist resorts, and local people, especially local traders and tourism communities, are pleased that the Prime Minister has allowed them to travel in This Pchum festival. These create hope for them to continue their business and be ready to welcome more guests on holiday.
