Please listen to the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in February 2019: 3 days off Pchum Ben holiday, traffic accident claimed 14 lives and injured a total of 64 people
(Phnom Penh): During the three-day Pchum Ben holiday from October 5 to 7, 2021, there were 35 traffic accidents across the country, resulting in 14 deaths and 64 injuries. 43 seriously injured). This is according to the report of the General Commission of the National Police.
The number of injuries and deaths from traffic accidents this year is similar to last year.
On October 5, the first day of the Pchum Ben holiday, there were nine road accidents across the country, killing five people and injuring 18 others, according to the National Police. On October 6, there were 11 traffic accidents, killing three people and injuring 22 others. On October 7, there were 15 traffic accidents, resulting in 6 deaths and 24 injuries.
The most common causes of traffic accidents during Pchum Ben are speeding, disrespectful driving, overturning, and drunk driving.
