(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, told the ASEAN Health Minister that people must learn to live in a new environment in the context of the Kovid-19 virus evolving by not getting stuck in Kovid-19 and control Kovid-19 rather than let Kovid-19 control daily life.
This statement was made by Dr. O Vandin on the occasion of attending the Special Ministerial Meeting for ASEAN Digital Public Health on behalf of Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health. The meeting was held under the theme "Collaborating for Better Health and Happiness in the World After the Epidemic" from October 6-7, 2021.
In this special meeting, Ms. O Vandin was selected as one of the keynote speakers on the agenda to discuss the experiences and impacts of health and the economy, as well as the challenges encountered during the response to Outbreaks of Kovid-19 in the region, especially in the country.
Therefore, learning to live with continuing infection prevention is a topic for people to think about and prepare for with risk assessment, mitigation measures, and rapid vaccination promotion. Vaccinated and available in all countries as well. Travel and recognition of vaccination certificates in ASEAN countries is also a point of awareness.
The purpose of the meeting was to discuss topics emerging behind the epidemic and lessons learned from the Kovid-19 epidemic, aimed at investing and providing finance, as well as raising awareness and collaborating. For public health.
