The Royal Government of Cambodia plans to reopen the country later this year after launching a series of measures, especially vaccinating people, including a third dose (boosting dose) as the epidemic decreases. Down one level. As of the night of October 5, 2021, Cambodia has vaccinated 19 Kovid 19 civil servants, the armed forces and a total of 13,456,306 people, while the third dose was nearly 1 million.
Despite facing 19 Kovid, which affected a number of sectors, especially tourism, Cambodia's agriculture and industry are still performing well. The World Bank, IMF and Asian Development Bank (ADB) have forecast that despite facing 19 Kovid, Cambodia's growth in 2021 will be between 1.8 and 2.2 percent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia must strive to grow the Cambodian economy. "If we can open the economy by the end of this year, especially on primary tourism services, our economic growth could exceed 2.2 percent, as assessed in the past nine months," he said.
"This test is a big test between disaster and security. If we do it right, disaster will not happen and it will not lead to the re-opening of the country." This is a further confirmation of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
