Minister of Education: Five jobs have been set up to ensure the sustainability of education and the reopening of schools during the 1940s.
Despite the efforts of the teachers in all forms, the students' learning has experienced many difficulties and losses. This is according to the Minister of Education.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron said that in response to the above challenges, the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has set out and is accelerating the implementation of effective and gentle measures to ensure the sustainability of learning and operation. Re-learning institutions. The five measures include:
* First: Create a safe and secure school environment to protect teachers and students, including mental health counseling and community encouragement to participate in school management.
* Second: Practice multidisciplinary learning, combining classroom learning, digital learning, television learning, paperwork and self-study.
* Third: Implement a flexible curriculum, giving priority to reading and math learning at the primary level in primary school and observation and self-study at the secondary level. Curriculum-based curriculum focuses on key subjects and summarizes lessons for students to learn on their own.
* Fourth: Using digital content created by our outstanding teachers will be able to help solve the shortage of teachers in rural areas, as well as the shortage of qualified teachers.
And 5: Continue to implement school reform to make schools more accountable to parents, students and the community by exchanging school culture and encouraging community participation in school management and support for a positive learning environment. Security.
