Up to 330,000 children have been sexually abused in the Catholic Church in France in 70 years
The report is the result of the first large-scale investigation into a series of child sexual abuse cases occurring in the Catholic Church. Most of the reported violations in the report, about 216,000, were committed by the clergy themselves, while others were committed by individuals associated with the Catholic Church. About 80 percent of the victims were boys.
The commission's findings show that there may have been at least 2,900-3,200 pastors or other members operating in the Catholic Church from 1950 to 2020.
