Koh Rong - Koh Rong Samloem fishing community calls on fishermen not to buy or sell horse crab and tiger crab with eggs outside
In addition, the Koh Rong-Koh Rong Samloem fishing community calls for joint conservation of our marine fisheries resources for sustainable use and natural balance.
Please be informed that recently, experts have announced the ban on the business of horse crabs and tiger crabs with eggs outside to preserve marine fishery resources, especially horse crabs and tiger crabs to thrive in natural waters. In return, it aims to improve the livelihood of fishermen who depend on crab fishing in the coastal areas of the Fisheries Administration.
In case of accidental fishing, please take the horse crab or tiger crab with these eggs on the outside and put them in the crab turn which has been established in 29 places in Sihanoukville, Kampot, Kep and Koh Kong to make the main crab They remove all the eggs first and then sell and trade later.
According to the Fisheries Administration, a single crab can lay more than 1.4 million eggs. So, if you keep these crabs for a short time in the crab until they are hatched, it means that you have helped to protect our fishery resources with the highest sense of responsibility, which is beneficial for healthy fishing. Sustainability and for future generations.
The Fisheries Administration strongly hopes for the responsible spirit of all fishermen to contribute to the maintenance and support of the management of our nation's precious fishery resources, especially the resources of crabs in our own communities to be rich and sustainable. Forever.
