(Phnom Penh): In the last five years, it has been observed that deposits in banking and financial institutions have increased significantly.
In fact, according to the report of the National Bank of Cambodia, as of the first half of 2021, deposit deposits, also known as deposits in the banking and financial system, increased by nearly 20 percent, equivalent to a total of 130 .8 trillion riel or about 32 billion US dollars.
Some Cambodians often think that saving is the only way to save money or spend the rest, but real savings do not mean that. Saving is the process of saving money, which is part of the income, to be used later in an emergency, necessary, or to accomplish a purpose.
In Cambodia, the culture of saving money is beginning to develop remarkably, with the use of home savings methods such as stuffing in piglets, soil under pillows, mats or other places to create accounts in Banking and financial institutions to store savings instead.
Ms. Pen Bopha, Director of Rithipol Company, stated that the savings will enable us to have some budget to achieve our goals as well as our dreams. Saving also helps us prevent some real emergencies, such as the Kovid-19 problem, we can take this savings package to solve.
In particular, Mr. Nget Chou, an expert in the financial sector, said that the banking and microfinance sector is growing, it means to put money in all those institutions, not to put money under. Mats or pillows like in ancient times.
Mr. Men Pheakdey, Director of the Data Management and Macro Analysis Department of the General Department of Supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia, emphasized that Cambodians today have a lot of knowledge related to work, deposits or savings.
He said that the National Bank of Cambodia has launched a national strategy on the financial environment, which was approved by the Royal Government in 2019, and this strategy encourages people to save money. At the same time, the National Bank of Cambodia, the Banking Association of Cambodia, and the Microfinance Association of Cambodia have been paying close attention to this financial environment.
Ms. Peng Liya Ms. Peng Liya, Director of Financial Services for Personal Customers of Prince Bank and a representative of the Banking Association of Cambodia, believes that saving money is very important for everyone, men, women, young and old. The habit of saving money helps us to have a clear plan and prevent any risks that may occur accidentally and also help to achieve any goal that we desire.
"If an individual does not have savings, we could face a financial crisis or some unforeseen risk," she said. When a person is at financial risk, it affects his family, and if many families have financial problems, it causes the whole society to have financial problems that will make the nation suffer. "The problem is getting worse."
