He also pointed out that on the occasion of Pchum Ben, there is a high level of concern about traffic accidents due to heavy traffic on the road. He called on the people to participate in large numbers to ensure that travel is not overcrowded and health measures must be implemented.
Mr. Sam Piseth continued that on the road, please do not overtake each other by driving in the right lane. For motorcycles, please respect the traffic rules, all drivers must be right and must not drive into the center.
In addition, Mr. Sam Piseth said that all vehicles must check the technical specifications before departure to avoid accidents, especially must respect traffic laws and speed limits and drive with great caution. And understanding.
Lt. Gen. Chew Hak emphasized that the main goal is for drivers and passengers to know how to protect their lives from traffic accidents and to protect themselves from Kovid 19. Under the guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, the authorities strictly implement the aim of protecting public safety by strictly controlling the crime of theft, robbery and so on.
Brigadier General Chev Hak confirmed that during this holiday, the police force is ready to prevent congestion as well as traffic accidents in Phnom Penh.
