Please watch the video below: Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Be an official, do not be opportunistic, do not neglect your role or position must adhere to the public interest (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior "As an officer, do not be opportunistic, do not neglect your role or position, and all officials must adhere to the public interest, not to consider partisanship.
On the occasion of presiding over the inauguration ceremony of Stung Treng Provincial Governor on October 4, 2021, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng gave an example that when he was the district governor or got any other position, he signed as he wished. That is leading to problems, so before signing, consult with the relevant institutions as much as possible.
"Our officers, when they received this job, that job," said Prince Kralahom. Of course, our honor has the opportunity to do those jobs, but we must not neglect our role and position.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom also warned officials at all levels not to be opportunistic officials who cause problems to society and themselves, because this opportunism leads to the abuse of power over others. .
Samdech Krala Hom instructed officials at all levels to pay attention and carry out their work consistently, based on accuracy, law and justice.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom advised that all communication between the council and the provincial governor in the general management of the provincial administration, including the development of local development policies, preparation and use of staff management budget, the use of the stamp must be considered. The public interest is paramount, not partisan, family-oriented and self-serving.
Taking this opportunity, Samdech Krala Hom advised the leaders and civil servants at all levels throughout the province to implement the five approaches consistently set by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Sent a Broker to Court Involved in Illegal Migration of Workers to Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): On October 4, 2021, the police sent a woman as a broker to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court to deal with the case related to the case of smuggling people to work in Thailand illegally.
Lt. Col. Sun Saroeun, deputy director of the Anti-Trafficking and Protection of Minors Office, told reporters that the arrested broker was Ren Duong, a 53-year-old female from Kdep Thmor village, Kouk Romiet commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Lt. Col. Sun Saroeun confirmed that before arresting the broker, the police force of Kouk Romiet commune administrative post patrolled and found nine Cambodian male and female workers intending to cross the border into Thailand to work illegally. Kouk Romiet was arrested and brought for questioning at the Kouk Romiet commune administrative post.
In front of the authorities, the broker, Ren Duong, admitted that he had hired Thai employers to find workers to work in Thailand, with each Thai employer paying 500 baht. As for the nine Cambodian workers, after signing the contract, the authorities allowed them to return to their homes.
