(Phnom Penh): The Air Force Command has cooperated with the Lane Air Training Center to train pilots and other related skills. This collaboration aims to increase the human resources of pilots, engineers and aircraft technicians.
The Lanme Training Center opened its pilot training center for pilots, engineers, technicians and flight attendants in Cambodia in 2020. In 2021, Lanme Training Center opened a cooperation with the Air Force to expand this training even better.
Lt. Gen. Kong Mony emphasized, "I understand that the establishment of human resource training cooperation in this area with our Air Force Lanme Company is an appropriate and smart way to support the direction of training expansion." "Domestic human resources in line with current and future needs of the civil aviation market."
Mr. Khan Vanna, Director General of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, stated that the goal of the cooperation between the Lanmy Training Center and the Air Force is not only to train commercial pilots, but also to train human resources in aircraft engineering in Cambodia. There is a lot of demand.
Mr. Khan Vanna said, "Actually, in terms of aircraft repair and maintenance services, many foreign engineers work in our domestic airlines because we still lack human resources." "Therefore, this cooperation is the sharpest priority base to accelerate the development of human resources in all areas to meet the needs of the civil aviation market for now and in the future."
Mr. Chan Chi Seng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Lanmei Company, pointed out that there is a shortage of Cambodian pilots, aircraft engineers and pilots. Seeing this challenge, Lan Me University decided to train human resources in this field to serve the civil aviation sector in Cambodia.
Mr. Chan Chi Seng said that at present, Lanme University has a plane equipped with modern technical equipment for training.
"If we have enough human resources like pilots, engineers, we will be able to expand the economy in Cambodia because we have used local human resources and we will cut," he said. Reduce human resources brought from abroad to work in Cambodia.
According to Chan Chi Seng, the Lanme Training Center currently has nine students studying civil aviation. The nine students were all Cambodian and female Khmer Muslim trainees. The training center is accepting students who want to study civil aviation or aspire to become technicians, pilots and pilots.
