(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on the afternoon of October 4, 2021 issued an appeal to the people, encouraging travelers to use private means of transportation to avoid using public transportation to prevent infection. Kovid 19. This is according to the appeal received by Fresh News.
According to the appeal, the Royal Government has decided to suspend the Kanben and Pchum Ben festivals in order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 by keeping the three-day Pchum Ben holiday according to the public holiday calendar. Civil servants, employees and workers for the year 2021.
During the next three days off, many people will be able to travel to reunite with their families and travel to various resorts, which could put the Kingdom of Cambodia at risk of a large-scale outbreak of Kovid-19. .
