Pediatricians share and exchange experiences and knowledge at the 6th Conference on Pediatric Medicine Updates
(Phnom Penh): Pediatricians, both local and foreign, shared and exchanged experiences as well as new knowledge related to pediatrics through the conference on "The 6th Pediatric Update" online.
The conference was held on September 30, 2021 under the chairmanship of Professor Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, and was attended by more than 700 members of the Cambodian Medical Association.
Even during the Kovit-19 epidemic, the Cambodian Pediatric Association still holds regular conferences, as it does every year, with the aim of providing a forum for local and international pediatricians to share and exchange information. Experience as well as new knowledge related to pediatrics so that all participants can draw on the importance of the care and treatment of Cambodian children.
In the 6th Conference on Pediatric Medicine Update, 5 important topics were presented:
Solve the common problems of upper respiratory tract infections that are most common in Asian children.
* Nutritional characteristics in premature and slow-growing infants and long-term complications
* Introduction of Kovid-19 disease that spreads to severe pneumonia at Kantha Bopha Hospital
Prof. Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, also instructed all pediatricians from various hospitals to bring the latest knowledge to participate in the provision of effective, quality and safe pediatric services and to adhere to. Medical professional ethics to improve the provision of health services to the people.
(Phnom Penh): Ansam cake is a cake that almost all Cambodian families always prepare every year during the Khmer New Year, especially Pchum Ben. In addition to these two ceremonies at weddings, there is also the packaging of Ansam cakes.
* Brahminical beliefs are the cause of the Ansam cake
In Brahmanism, Ansam cake represents the penis of Iso, while Nomkom represents the vagina of Uma, the wife of Iso. That is why we often see this type of cake in the festival accompanied by cakes, which are traditional Khmer cakes as well.
Ansam cake has its origins in ancient Khmer history and has been seen in traditional Khmer festivals such as New Year, Pchum Ben, weddings and other religious ceremonies. The fact that all these cakes are taken to the pagoda on Pchum Ben day comes from this festival as well as other festivals related to Hinduism.
