Algeria recalls ambassador to France over Macrong's comments (Video inside): Algerian government has decided to recall its ambassador to France for advice on the issue. Controversial remarks by French President Emmanuel Macron. This is according to the release by CGTN on Sunday, October 3, 2021.
French and Algerian media reported on Saturday that Macron had addressed a group of Algerian youths whose parents and grandparents had joined forces with the French army in the fight against the revolutionaries. Demanded independence from France in the Algerian War of 1954-1962.
At a meeting on Thursday, McCormack claimed that Algeria was led by a military-political system and described Algeria as having a "completely rewritten" history. According to Makrong, this history is not based on facts, but is intended to incite hatred against France.
However, the Algerian government condemned and dealt with Mr McCormack's remarks, damaging the reputation of Algerian heroes who fought for independence from France and interfering in Algeria's internal affairs. So the Algerian government decided to summon the ambassador to Paris, Mohamed Antar-Daoud, back for advice.
This is the second time Algeria has recalled its ambassador to France, a similar incident that occurred in 2020. The diplomatic row comes at a time when the two countries are already embroiled in tensions over France's decision to reduce the number of visas to Algerian, Moroccan and Tunisian citizens.
