According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on October 2, 2021, Dr. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that the financial literacy video and financial guide will provide Pathways to the general public, financial services users and especially young women entrepreneurs to understand the full process of accessing and using financial services with quality, efficiency and intelligence.
More than 200 participants representing key stakeholders attended the event: US Embassy, National Bank of Cambodia, Cambodian Banking Association, Cambodian Microfinance Association, Wing, Bush K-Capital, C-Investment and Women's Savings Group, as well as partners. Development of NGOs, financial institutions, educational institutions, government institutions and young women entrepreneurs.
Manura Chan, CEO of Wing, also said that women play an important role in the Cambodian economy. They run a small business and are usually responsible for the cash flow for their families. Financial literacy is an important tool for women entrepreneurs because it gives them vital knowledge that allows them to manage their budgets efficiently and effectively.
The Financial Guide is a map to help young women entrepreneurs make effective decisions before concluding what they need to finance and determine the type of finance that best suits their conditions, including business size, level of development, scope of possibilities. Access to finance, climate change and access to financial literacy. This financial guide also links to links that other organizations have produced related to this topic.
Seilaboy, co-founder and director of SeaVesmin, said the project really demonstrates public-private partnerships, focusing on young women entrepreneurs and their voices. We are proud and pleased to have contributed so far and look forward to seeing these resources help women make informed financial decisions in the future.
The 9-episode Financial Literacy Video will raise awareness and increase financial literacy for young women entrepreneurs to strengthen their business. Participants learned about financial access issues and safe financing options for young women entrepreneurs to expand their businesses.
