(Pursat): After serving as the Governor of Pursat Province for about 7 years, Mr. Mao Thunin was transferred by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, to be the Governor of Kampot Province yesterday. September 30, 2021.
Mr. Mao Thunin was appointed by the King to be the Governor of Pursat Province in 2014. During his seven years in Pursat province, Mao Thunin has left behind many achievements in building and developing infrastructure in Pursat province.
In addition to construction and development work in this province, Mr. Mao Thunin also pays attention to serve and solve the difficulties of the people. Before Mao Thunin took office as governor, Pursat was a province with many land disputes.
But after he arrived, he chose the win-win political mechanism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and tried to enter directly to resolve the land dispute until the end of a series of disputes. Also of interest is the monthly or weekly food distribution program for needy people in the province.
In addition to the outstanding achievements mentioned above, Mr. Mao Thunin has created another famous masterpiece in this province, which is the establishment of a congress to solve problems for the people in the province. The Congress Conflict Resolution Program has made Mao Thunin very famous. Through this program, Mr. Mao Thunin helped end many of the people's problems by understanding and avoiding the use of judicial mechanisms.
Mao Thunin's work and emotional leadership and love from his heart made him deeply respected by the people in the province. The people of this province consider Mao Thunin a rare provincial leader.
Before leaving Pursat province, Mr. Mao Thunin on October 1, 2021, took the gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to distribute to the families of veterans in Bun Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung Veal Veng district, Pursat province as well. Providing food to the veterans' families is also his monthly program.
With this food distribution, Mr. Mao Thunin also said goodbye to the people with whom he had been in close contact. The farewell led to the unexpected: the people of the veterans expressed their deepest condolences to him, and some even thanked him for his caring service during Many years ago.
Among them was an old woman who cried and cried and felt sorry for Mr. Mao Thunin. However, Cambodian veterans also wished Mao Thunin success with his new role and happiness, overcoming all obstacles.
After seeing the people miss like this, Mr. Mao Thunin also showed his deep sympathy with the people.
Through all these aspects, it brings to mind the words of advice of the Khmer people, "Let them pity and love them." All these aspects also show that all the actions of the leaders with thoughtful and pious deeds of the leaders always receive loving compensation from the people.
