Cambodia-Thailand trade volume reaches over 5 billion USD, up 11% in 8 months
According to the report, Cambodia's exports to Thailand from January to August totaled 623 million US dollars and imports from Thailand totaled 4.61 billion US dollars, creating a trade deficit between the two countries. Two, $ 3.99 billion.
According to a report from the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand, in August 2021, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand was worth 625 million US dollars. Of that, Cambodia's exports to Thailand were worth 54.5 million US dollars, down about 25% from the same month of 2020, which amounted to 73.1 million US dollars. Imports from Thailand were valued at 571 million US dollars, up 28 percent from 445 million US dollars in the same month in 2020.
Most of Cambodia's exports to Thailand are textiles, agricultural products, gems, precious raw materials, sectors and semi-finished goods, while Cambodia imports back energy, fish, meat, vegetables and finished products such as automobiles, organic fertilizers, cement, foodstuffs. Cosmetics and construction materials.
