Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Issues to Strengthen the Implementation of Health Measures for Passengers and Foreigners Entering Their Provinces
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, on October 1, 2021, issued a guideline on strengthening the implementation of health measures for travelers and people from abroad to Preah Sihanouk Province to Participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19.
In order to prevent the spread of this deadly virus, in order to reopen the socio-economic situation, ensure the normalization of people's lives, maintain the sustainability of the reopening of schools as well as the resumption of work activities. Occupations and businesses, usually within the framework of Sihanoukville, the provincial administration has recommended the implementation of a number of health measures for travelers and citizens from abroad as follows:
* First, continue to patrol the traffic in and out of the border into Sihanoukville, both by land and water. In the event of a passenger or citizen from abroad coming to the provincial or municipal area, the first necessary health measures shall be taken, including the collection of samples for the diagnosis of Kovid 19 virus and the placement of the catheter at the location where the provincial administration Prepared before proceeding with other procedures.
* Second: For passengers arriving at Sihanoukville International Airport, must continue to implement health measures in force through the work system and good cooperation between the provincial international airport and the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration.
