Senior Minister Sun Chanthol welcomes US companies to bid for road construction in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, welcomes US companies to bid for road construction in Cambodia. The desire to see US companies bid for road construction in Cambodia was also informed by Senior Minister Patrick Muffy, US Ambassador to Cambodia.
In a press conference on the progress of the implementation of measures to prevent overweight vehicles on the morning of October 1, 2021, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol presented some of the results of the meeting between him and the US Ambassador on 30 September 2021 as well.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, during the meeting, he requested the United States to provide technical equipment to inspect the road, and to request cooperation, sharing experiences on construction skills training between Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and well-known American universities. . The senior minister also asked the US ambassador to introduce his construction company to bid for road construction in Cambodia.
For the senior minister, such a proposal is to show the United States that the Royal Government of Cambodia has never discriminated against American companies to build roads in Cambodia. On the contrary, the United States itself has never sent a company and blames Cambodia for taking only this country or that country does not take American companies.
"I have asked the United States to introduce its construction company to bid for $ 500 million on National Road 5 and more than $ 100 million for National Road 4, with no US companies bidding," he said. There was no bidding, but it was said that Cambodia only allowed foreign companies, Chinese companies, Korean companies to build the road. "No, because no American company came to bid."
