(Banteay Meanchey): A broker who smuggled five workers on a tricycle to cross the border to work illegally in Thailand was arrested by the Kork Romiet commune administrative police station in Thmar Puok district at a gas station in Vally Breng village. Kok Romiet.
The suspect, Sao Chhada, 33 years old, resident of Trapeang Samrong village, Kouk Romiet commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province, was arrested at 8:30 pm on September 29, 2021.
Lt. Col. Sun Saroeun, deputy director of the Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors Office, said that police from the Kouk Romiet commune administrative post patrolling west of the Boeung Trakoun roundabout found a group of five men and women, including children. Two of them live in Pen village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province, and a tricycle driver came to transport them.
With suspicion, they inquired and found out that the people intended to cross the border to Thailand with a tricycle rider to pick them up. After the interrogation, the authorities sent the people and the tricycle driver to the Thmar Puok District Police Inspectorate for further interrogation and further action.
Lt. Col. Sun Saroeun said that following the order of Major General Sithi Loh, the provincial police chief of Thmar Puok district arrested the suspect, Sao Chhada, and sent him to the provincial police for further action.
In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he really intended to transport the five Cambodian workers, including two children, to Thailand to find work, with a transportation fee of 500 baht per person to cross the road. Nation in Thai territory.
Based on the suspect's confession, the specialized force sent him to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court for processing on the morning of October 1, 2021. Separately, the five workers were educated, instructed and contracted to return to their respective homes.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that he has never received any requests or interventions from overweight transport operators, even if the overweight transporters are in power. Or whatever.
Overcrowding has been found to be one of the main causes of road damage. The transport formula found that one truck over 10 tons, equivalent to 10,000 vehicles, was traveling on the road. If one car weighs more than 30 tons, it is equivalent to 81,000 cars driving on the road.
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport has put in place a number of measures to prevent overweight transportation. The ministry currently has 33 stationary scales on national roads and two additional groups of mobile scales to prevent overweight vehicles. The ministry is also setting up more technology to catch overweight trucks and eliminate corruption between scales station officials and overweight drivers.
In a press conference on the progress of the implementation of measures to prevent overweight vehicles on the morning of October 1, 2021, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the task force to fight overweight. Of course, the results have not been completely improved yet, there are still overweight smugglers.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, in order to prevent overweight, this is only the spirit of the people to respect the law. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized, "Despite the efforts of all relevant authorities, it is not yet 100 percent." "Therefore, the participation of our people in obeying the law is more important than the team working day and night."
The report shows that in the first nine months of 2021, of the 1.8 million vehicles inspected, nearly 580,000 were found to be overweight, accounting for 31 percent. More than 2,000 overweight vehicles from 20 percent.
In connection with the seizure of overweight trucks, the Overweight Transport Crimes Task Force has always proved difficult to carry out its work because the owners of the transport companies are influential. Or have the power to seek intervention or intimidation. But the team, as well as Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, did not surrender to any intervention or intimidation.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "Damage to this road, whether your car is rich or powerful, it is the same. "The road does not know that the car of the big man, the car of the poor, this car of the poor, if the truck is overweight and it damages the road as well."
It should be noted that in order to prevent overweight transportation, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in November 2020 issued a hot measure by deciding to arrest overweight vehicles and keep them for one year in addition to fines. The seized vehicle is a vehicle that is overweight by 20% or more.
From November 2020 to September 2021, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport seized 229 overweight trucks and stored them. With the favor of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, these cars were allowed to be returned to their owners ahead of time to be used for business. But they have to pay the same fine.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol claimed that after the release, which was in favor of Samdech Techo, the working group to prevent overweight is still implementing the same legal measures, and if the next arrest is not favorable. Retail fuel price from today to October 15: regular price of gasoline 4,100 riel and diesel price 3,800 riel per liter
