(Phnom Penh): This morning, October 1, 2021, at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, a press conference was held on the release of 229 overweight vehicles ahead of schedule after the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The press conference was chaired by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on September 30, 2021, yesterday authorized the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to release 229 overweight vehicles ahead of schedule. The vehicles were detained at the weighbridge and the Department of Public Works and Transport in some capitals and provinces.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that vehicles that have not yet paid their fines must first pay their fines in order to be released.
He added that although the Royal Government of Cambodia allows for the release and release of Pchum Ben, vehicle owners and transport business owners should respect and abide by the Law on Roads and the Notification on Strengthening. Strict measures in addition to heavy transport vehicles driving on the road network.
He also urged the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to continue to strictly enforce the legal limit for overweight vehicles, with no exceptions for the second time.
