According to the National Bank of Cambodia, the dollar auction will be announced on the morning of the actual auction day. Commentary: China's achievements in human rights development contribute to China's wisdom and plan for solving humanitarian problems
BEIJING, Sept. 29 (Xinhua) - Institutions such as the China Institute for Human Rights Research released a report on the status of the implementation of the "China National Human Rights Action Plan 2016-2020". This is the first time that China has invited third-party institutions to conduct an honest and comprehensive review of China's human rights development situation.
The report shows that a total of 168 projects and tasks in this action plan have been completed, with many indices and tasks completed ahead of schedule or overdue. Planning and implementing a national human rights action plan is a key theme in the field of human rights protection in the world today.
In July this year, China announced that it had built a prosperous society in all aspects, marking a new beginning in the development of human rights. These results are not only a great achievement of China's human rights cause, but also a significant contribution to global human rights governance and the development of the global human rights cause.
Today, in China, people's lives are more prosperous, people are happier, more prosperous and more satisfied. China's achievements in human rights development have diversified human rights civilization and contributed to China's wisdom and plan for solving humanitarian problems. Human rights are not a slogan, they must be implemented.
The root cause of China's fruitful protection of human rights has always been that the ruling party has always held the people at the core, adhering to the general connection of human rights with the real situation in China. Adhere to the promotion of human rights through development, successfully find a way to develop human rights appropriate to the Chinese situation.
The work of human rights defenders should do better without end. As China enters a new stage of development, the progress of China's human rights cause will have a stronger foundation. China has the ability to better cover human rights issues, and will contribute more to China's efforts to promote global human rights governance and improve human welfare.
The Bar Association and the Intellectual Property Association of Cambodia join hands on cooperation in providing legal education, dissemination and legal protection related to intellectual property.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Ms. Seng Vuoch Hun, President of the Cambodian Intellectual Property Association, signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) aimed at strengthening cooperation in the field of intellectual property promotion and professional development. Lawyers in Cambodia in the field of intellectual property. The MoU signing ceremony took place on the morning of Thursday, September 30, 2021.
The two sides will jointly promote the field of intellectual property and promote the legal profession in Cambodia in the field of intellectual property through:
1: Collaborate to organize joint workshops and training courses to strengthen the professional skills of lawyers, both law students and lawyers who are internship, intellectual property practitioners and the public to have more skills and understanding of intellectual property.
2: Provision of legal protection related to intellectual property and
3. Dissemination of information laws and activities of both institutions related to the field of intellectual property.
