(Ho Chi Minh City): Vietnam's Ho Chi Minh City will begin easing anti-COVID-19 measures after Thursday to allow business and social activities to resume after months of restrictions. Resist the spread of this deadly disease. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, September 30, 2021.
