Exporters claim that fresh mango exports to China will increase from October, while Cambodia just exported 200 tons to China
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's fresh mango exports to China may increase from October 2021 to May 2022 due to the arrival of mango harvest.
Cambodia exported fresh mangoes directly to the Chinese market on May 7, 2021, and so far only 200 tons of mangoes have been exported. But exporters see that from October 2021 onwards, Cambodia will export more mangoes to China.
He added that the export of mangoes so far is only 200 tons, because the agreement to export fresh mangoes from Cambodia to China was officially opened during May 2021, so from May to May. September 2021 is not the mango season, so only 200 tons of mangoes were exported to China. For the exported mangoes, these are mangoes left over from the harvest of the old season.
There is little disruption in mango export in terms of competitive prices because China does not import mangoes from Cambodia alone, but from many other countries, especially from Vietnam, Thailand and India. Another important issue is shipping costs. Cambodia's transportation costs are very high compared to other countries.
"The key factor in exporting this fresh mango more or less depends on the competitive price, but in terms of quality, Cambodian mangoes are widely recognized by the Chinese people as delicious because of the mangoes," he said. "Starchy and sweet and sour taste has made Chinese people very popular in recent years, especially mangoes, turmeric."
Not only the Chinese, the Koreans also like the Cambodian mango and turmeric because Cambodia has a variety of mango, turmeric, which has a special taste, sweet and sour.
Cambodia Fresh Mango is the second fresh fruit after fresh bananas that can be exported directly to China. This is another fruitful achievement born of the excellent cooperation between Cambodia and China.
The Cambodian Gambling Management Commission organizes a consultation forum on the conditions and procedures for fulfilling revenue, licensing obligations and transitional penalties for violations of the Gambling Law.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Gambling Management Commission (SEC) has organized a public consultation forum with casino company representatives nationwide on the terms and procedures of revenue fulfillment, obligations and provisions. Licenses include transactional penalties for violations of the Gambling Regulations Act.
A public consultation meeting was held on the morning of September 30, 2021 through the Zoom system, chaired by Mr. Ros Phirun, Secretary General of the Gambling Commission of Cambodia and Lt. Gen. Seang Sen, Deputy Secretary General of the Gambling Management Commission. Cambodian business, including the participation of the duke, the tycoon, the tycoon and the CEO / CEO / CEO and casino owners across the country.
To begin with, Lt. Gen. Sieng Sen addressed a public consultation forum on the overall content of the draft:
* First: Prakas on the conditions and procedures for fulfilling the obligations from gambling * Second: Prakas on the conditions and procedures for licensing * Third: Sub-decree on transitional penalties for violations of the law on management Commercial gambling is the promotion of good governance based on the laws and regulations in force to prevent all crimes, including the protection of security and social security.
The Deputy Secretary General of the SEC added that in response to the requirements of the Sub-Decree on Minimum Capital for Operations, the first legal document came into force on 26 August 2021. Disseminate together with the Law on the Management of Commercial Gambling on September 13, 2021 within the framework of the preparation of legal documents governing and controlling in the field of commercial gambling.
"This law is being disseminated to ensure the effectiveness of implementation as well as to ensure the sustainability and viability of the business operations of licensed operators before the law comes into force for 2022," he said.
Mr. Ros Phirun said in the forum that in order to keep up with the increasing activity in the field of commercial gambling, the Royal Government has promoted the management of the gambling sector with efficiency and effectiveness based on laws and regulations. Effective.
The Secretary General of the SEC explained the conditions and procedures to the operators participating in the forum to understand the stages and benefits of the law:
Please be informed that the Law on the Management of Commercial Gambling was drafted and approved on October 5, 2020 at the 5th Session of the National Assembly, the 6th Legislature and the Senate. This law was completed on October 26, 2020 at the 6th Plenary Session of the 4th Legislature and was promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1120/031 dated November 14, 2020.
