Kampot International Tourism Port will be another important magnet to attract tourists
(Kampot): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that Kampot International Tourism Port will be an important international gateway for seaborne in ensuring the national transportation system as well as will be another important magnet in Attract national-international tourism.
The Minister said so on the occasion that he and Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province, led a working group and government officials to inspect the construction of "Kampot International Tourism Port" located in Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province on the 29th. September 2021.
The construction of this international tourist port started on August 8, 2018 until now, the work of the whole site has reached about 84% and the work of the passenger building has reached about 73%, scheduled to be completed by the end of 2021. .
The port is an international tourist port that is planned to accommodate about 1 million tourists and passengers. This port is structured according to international standards and is a passenger port (not a cargo port).
The port will be an important international gateway by sea, connecting tourists to the southern islands and connecting Kampot province of Cambodia to the world. Through this port, it will further promote the development of tourism and related sectors in Kampot province, Bokor mountain resort and Cambodia's coastal tourist destinations.
Minister Thong Khon and Governor Chiao Tai also attended the inauguration of a small infrastructure project in Peam Krasop Ecotourism Resort, Koh Kong Province, Wat Phnom Sor Sear Resort, Kep Province and Phnom Kampong Trach Tourism Resort, Kampot Province. :
* Peam Krasop Tourism Community, Koh Kong Province, has received information on public toilets, production and sales centers for community products, as well as equipments for production and an incinerator with a capacity of 2-4 tons of garbage per day.
* Wat Phnom Sor Sear tourism community in Kep province has received information center, public toilet, 227-meter-long receipt and two 13-meter-long stairs in the cave.
