Ms. Men Sam An: Promoting children's rights and protecting children is our job together
(Phnom Penh): "National Policy Implementation Plan on Child Protection System 2019-2029" was officially launched on September 29, 2021 through the Zoom system under the chairmanship of Mrs. Kattisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Social Affairs, Ms. Men Sam An said, "Promoting children's rights and protecting children is our common task, which requires us to work together in a multi-sectoral, interconnected way."
In addition, she added that the protection of children is also the world is paying attention and working together to prevent and respond to all forms of abuse, and Cambodia is a country that is moving forward to participate. This work actively aims to improve the promotion of child protection for the benefit of all children.
The National Policy on Child Protection System is a strategy that demonstrates the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to the systematic implementation of child protection in Cambodia and is a set of rules designed to promote and enhance protection. Children from all forms of abuse and exploitation based on three pillars: (1) prevention, (2) intervention, (3) the provision of services and responses that we need to respond systematically.
Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and President of the Cambodian National Council for Children, said that despite the attention of the Royal Government, many mechanisms have been established to manage and provide services to children in general and However, there are still some children living in difficult situations who need support and intervention.
The Child Protection System is a concrete commitment to the systematic implementation of child protection in Cambodia, including:
1. The need to invest more in sub-national social officials or social workers to promote effective, efficient, consistent and timely child care services for children and families in the community.
2. Continuing to ensure that children have access to legal and social equity services by providing a minimum package of social services for children and families in need of protection.
3. Response to children and their families affected by the disaster.
4: Continuing to concentrate, strengthen and expand existing programs for child protection to increase efficiency, transparency and stability.
5. Ensuring the integrity of existing procedures, measures and mechanisms to solve children's problems to meet the needs and ensure the protection of children, family environment, love, caring, child-friendly and ensure the best interests of children.
She added: "Plan International Cambodia and I believe that many other development partners are ready to support the Royal Government of Cambodia to make the next 10-year national action plan a success for millions of children, especially girls. In Cambodia. ”
