(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Ngin Nel, Mayor of Banlung City, on September 29, 2021, confirmed that the authorities have given two weeks to the business people to sell on the public side to earn money to support their families after the security around Banlung Market. Arrange for vendors to return to the market to avoid the risk of transmission of Kovid 19.
"Because every day, 19 positive Kovid cases are still found in Banlung, as well as in some areas throughout Ratanakkiri province, and Banlung market is being beautified according to the standard," Ngin Nel said. To avoid the spread of Kovid 19 disease in Banlung market, he gave them two more weeks to sell normally on the public square to earn money to support their families.
Vendors selling on the public side of the street say that their daily seating is better and safer because the stalls are spacious, spaced from one place to another, and access to the Banlung Market is now The stalls have not been set up 100% yet, and positive cases of Kovid 19 are still being discovered, which is also a concern.
Vendors said that although the Banlung municipal authorities allowed them to re-enter the market in Banlung, it was now better to sell on public sidewalks because the market was cramped and the area outside the market was more crowded. The wider the safety gap, the lower the risk in the market, however, they adhere to the "3 do not and 3 prevent" health rules.
The vendors added that the public sidewalks were organized by the city hall, and they paid 2,000 riel per day to Banlung City Hall and 500 riel to the sanitation department. .
