Lt. Gen. Rath Srang assigned a team to bring money and relics to the monks at Wat Preah Barami Vong Borei Kabel Phosto!
Due to the Kovid 19 issue, this year's Kanben ceremony at the pagoda was restricted without a meeting based on the principle of "3 protect and 3 do not", so Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang did not go to the pagoda to hold the Ben directly. Only assign a team to bring money and relics to the monks. China considers negative listings for cross-border trade in FTA trade
BEIJING: China will consider creating a negative list for cross-border trade in services in the superpower's free trade area (FTZs) to further promote trade liberalization of services. According to the release of Xinhua.
China will continue to work to raise the level of China's openness, a Chinese state-run newspaper quoted Commerce Ministry official Chen Hong as saying at a press conference on Tuesday. Innovative Chinese institutions will strive to build various FTZs with global influence.
At the China International Services Trade Fair, which ended in early September, China announced that it would promote the implementation of a negative list for trade in services across the country.
In July, the Chinese Ministry of Commerce released a negative list for cross-border trade in services in Hainan, the first negative list for trade in services in the country.
The list, which came into force on August 26, 2021 and is officially titled "Special Administrative Measures for Transboundary Services Trade at Hainan Free Trade Port", includes 70 regulatory measures targeting providers. Foreign services in 11 sectors.
Under the negative list for cross-border trade in Hainan Province, foreign service providers are not allowed to provide services that are prohibited by this list. Unlisted economic activity is allowed and domestic and foreign service providers can enjoy fair competition and fair market entry in the non-listed sectors.
Cambodia-Australia cooperation to boost investment in agriculture-food, by August, nearly 10 billion USD investment project in agriculture and agro-industry approved
