The MoU Signing Ceremony is a milestone in reaffirming our commitment to prioritize investment in agro-food sector to contribute to food security, poverty reduction through job creation and growth. Economy and environmental sustainability.
This Memorandum of Understanding will be an important tool in contributing to the promotion of investment and promoting development in the agro-food sector, as well as improving competitiveness in the agricultural sector.
The implementation of the Agro-Food Investment Desk at the Council for the Development of Cambodia will strengthen the solid foundation of the agri-food sector to become more resilient in Cambodia through the diversification of resources and forms of investment that use technology and innovation in the sector. This is while creating more value-added jobs for Cambodians in the agro-food sector.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the CDC, thanked the Australian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade through the Australian Embassy in Cambodia for providing technical assistance to the Council for the Development of Cambodia and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. To promote investment activities under the Cambodia-Australia Agricultural Price Chain (CAVAC II).
The Minister highly appreciated the Australian Embassy in Cambodia for its role in providing technical assistance to accelerate the recovery of the Cambodian economy in a new normal direction after the Kovid-19 crisis.
"Meanwhile, the new Cambodian Investment Law will provide smart incentives for sectoral investment, while investment in agriculture and agro-food has been identified as a priority sector to boost and enhance productivity," he added. "To ensure that these sectors are resilient and sustainable in contributing to economic stabilization in response to the Kovid 19 crisis."
The Australian Ambassador to Cambodia underscored the Australian Government's commitment to supporting the Cambodian economic development process, especially to increase productivity in the agricultural sector by jointly promoting investment in the agro-food sector.
He said that the financing of the Council for the Development of the Cambodian Food and Agriculture Investment Table is now an additional Australian contribution to complement the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to promote and Maintain investment in agriculture, agribusiness and agro-food.
