National Minimum Wage Council supports and applauds $ 194 minimum wage for workers by 2022
(Phnom Penh): The National Minimum Wage Council has expressed strong support and admiration for setting the minimum wage for workers at $ 194 for 2022. Congratulations and support after the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training issued a press release on the increase in wages for workers in the garment and footwear sector by an additional $ 2 for 2022, which is officially set at $ 194 Per month.
According to Mr. Sam Soeun, a full member of the National Council of Minimum Wages and a representative of the National Union Council of Cambodia (CCNU), he expressed his gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has always cared for the welfare of workers and the people. People across the country are allowed to hold meetings to discuss the minimum wage of $ 194.
Mr. Sam Soeun also thanked Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor, Training and Vocational Training, for taking care of the well-being of the workers by directing the meeting to set the minimum wage for workers on behalf of unions and groups. The National Council of Cambodian Trade Unions (CCNU) will support a $ 194 wage increase for 2022.
After three rounds of negotiations, in which no figures were agreed, the minimum wage for workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector has finally reached the polls, with employers setting the figure at $ 188. The union side has a figure of $ 204 and the government side has a figure of $ 192.
According to the latest statement from the Ministry of Labor today, citing the reasons for the Kovid-19 crisis, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to pay $ 2 in addition to the $ 192 workers' wages, which makes garment workers Receive the minimum wage for 2022 of $ 194 per month and effective from January 1, 2022 onwards.
Although some union representatives were dissatisfied with the figures, the Ministry of Labor confirmed that the benefits that workers had received in the past were retained, allowing the average worker to receive an average salary. From $ 211 to $ 222 per month.
