Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, once pointed out that including the vaccine that arrived tomorrow, Cambodia will receive a total of 35.5 million doses of vaccine. She also said that the vaccine that Cambodia has ordered and delivered tomorrow is for vaccination of children aged 6 to 12 years.
Vaccination against Kovid 19 is very important to help people have a strong immune system to fight Kovid 19, reduce mortality due to the virus and reduce the spread of the disease. The Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has vaccinated Kovid 19 as a strategy on the battlefield with Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's strict order has made the vaccination rate of Cambodia significantly faster. As of September 26, 2021, Cambodia has vaccinated 13.1 million people aged 6 years and over, equivalent to more than 82% of the total population of 16 million.
As a result of Cambodia's vaccination efforts, Cambodia has been able to control the spread of 19 cases of Kovid in the country, especially in reducing the number of deaths from the effects of 19 cases of Kovid.
Cambodia's achievements in both vaccination and control of Kovid 19 have spread Cambodia's reputation regionally and globally, and have been praised by the World Health Organization, friendly countries and international development partners. Well.
There are many factors that lead Cambodia to decide on a vaccination plan. But Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Supreme Commander-in-Chief of the Battle of Kovid 19, is still the key to deciding on a vaccination plan, as the country's leader decides on plans and strategies. If the leader decides wrongly or late, it is clear that the vaccination plan will not be successful.
