Minister Mam Bunheng Visits Banteay Meanchey Province to Strengthen Health Implementation of Health Measures
(Banteay Meanchey): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, and his team on September 27, 2021, visited Banteay Meanchey province with the participation of Mr. Oum Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province.
The purpose of this mission is to discuss the strengthening of the implementation of health and administrative rules to control the spread of Kovid-19 throughout the province.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bun Heng inspected the services of Preah Net Preah Referral Hospital and visited 33 health workers infected with 19 Kovid 19 who are being treated at Preah Net Preah District Referral Hospital.
Minister Mam Bunheng also inspected the implementation of health rules and administrative measures at Poipet International Border Crossing and then inspected the laboratory of Poipet Referral Hospital equipped with PCR with the assistance of the Thai International Cooperation Agency (TICA). Test 200 to 300 samples per day.
Afterwards, the Minister of Health visited the flood victims at the safe haven of Serei Sophorn City and instructed the people to keep clean regularly to avoid diarrhea and other infectious diseases including Kovid 19. Distributed antiseptics, antiperspirants, mosquito nets, soaps and soaps.
The Department of Health of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration also received 1 million Chinese traditional medicine tablets, 150 bottles of snake bite medicine and some essential medicines.
At the same time, the Minister brought high praise from Samdech Techo Prime Minister to health officials, local authorities at all levels, armed forces of all kinds in Banteay Meanchey province who have done their best to provide services to the people. With a high sense of responsibility.
