The announcement was made in a press release on the results of the celebration of "World Tourism Day 2021" held on September 27, 2021.
The Ministry of Tourism claims that "Cambodia is now recognized as an advanced country in terms of vaccination, which is considered by the world to be a key strategy for fully reopening domestic and international tourism." In this context, the Ministry of Tourism will focus on safety as a key message to promote national and international tourism.
The Ministry also requested the relevant parties, especially the private sector, to participate in organizing its dissemination, focusing on the content "Cambodia Safe-Cambodia Safe" and called on the relevant operators to participate in the implementation of tourism safety rules to achieve "Label Tourism Safety Rules". Which the Ministry of Tourism has already submitted.
"If in the future there is no native Kovid-19 vaccine, the tourism sector must be prepared to innovate, from aircraft production to air filters in tourism businesses to prevent transmission," the ministry said in a statement.
However, the Ministry of Tourism, as well as other national and international institutions, expressed hope that "people always find solutions, crises always end."
