The Minister requested that the Ambassador consider providing opportunities for as many Cambodian workers to work in Australia as Cambodia has sent to the Republic of Korea, and if possible, in addition to agriculture, the Australian side may consider providing opportunities for Cambodian workers also go to work in construction, services and industry so that they can earn a high income to support their families as well as gain new experiences from Australia.
The two sides discussed work and shared information on procedures, mechanisms and labor management systems, both in recruitment, transfer and management mechanisms that can ensure risk-taking or deception, labor exploitation, human trafficking and so on. The Australian side is afraid that opportunists will use this information to distort the truth and deceive Cambodian workers, while Australia has not yet officially allowed Cambodia to send them.
The Embassy is also pleased that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notice to prevent the fraud of Cambodian workers, saying that Australia has granted work visas to work in agriculture, with both sides in the process of negotiating to Open this job opportunity.
The Australian Embassy in Cambodia will continue to work with the General Department of Labor of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to obtain all-inclusive information for applications to Canberra for review.
The Minister did not forget to thank the Government of Australia for its continued support, both financial assistance and human resource training, as well as building physical infrastructure for the people as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia, and hoped that the relationship between the two countries Both Cambodia and Australia will continue to work closely together in the long run.
At the same time, the Minister expressed his strong hope that the Australian side will provide this job opportunity to the people of Cambodia, because Cambodia has well prepared documents, policies and clear mechanisms, which is a good management system to ensure. Recruit, send and manage workers to ensure that their rights and interests are not violated and that they can prevent labor exploitation and human trafficking.
General knowledge: "Nobel Prize" was initiated by whom and for what?
While some called him a "merchant of death" because of all these explosives, Nobel was, in fact, a pacifist and later began to worry deeply about the impact of his discovery. To the world as well.
After his death in San Remo, Italy, on December 10, 1896, most of Nobel Prize's wealth was turned into an annual awards program in physics and chemistry. Literature, medicine and peace according to his word.
In doing so, Nobel stated that in doing so, he would like to encourage outstanding individuals in these areas to make discoveries that can be used for the benefit of mankind as a whole and for the promotion of peace. Just five years after Nobel's death, the first Nobel Prize ceremony was held.
The first Nobel Prize ceremony was held in Stockholm, Sweden, the birthplace of Nobel in Physics, Chemistry, Medicine, Literature and Peace. The ceremony marks the fifth anniversary of the death of Alfred Nobel.
Leaders and organizations sometimes receive the Nobel Peace Prize, while researchers often receive the Nobel Prize in science for their joint discoveries. In 1968, another Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences was established by the National Bank of Sweden and was awarded to the first winner in 1969.
