Commentary: The lies surrounding Xinjiang of Western anti-China forces can not mislead the international community.
BEIJING, Sept. 26 (Xinhua) - China released a white paper on the "population growth of Xinjiang" on September 26, which outlined the situation of population growth in Xinjiang through detailed data. Hold the world a good example in promoting the growth of a strong ethnic minority in China, a unified and multi-ethnic country.
At the same time, the population of Weiwei has maintained a high growth rate, from 8,345,600 in 2020 to 11,624,300 in 2022, an average increase of 1. At 67 percent a year, this figure is higher than the growth rate of ethnic minorities across China. In addition, the White Paper states that in the near future, the population of Xinjiang, especially ethnic minorities, will maintain steady growth.
In addition, in accordance with the United Nations Human Development Index, the UN standard for assessing the level of human development, the growing number of Xinjiang ethnic minorities has made good progress in all three areas. Expected life expectancy, education level and quality of life.
Lies cannot hide the truth. The data show that the population growth situation of Xinjiang is better than at any time in history. The lies concerning Xinjiang, which Western anti-China forces could not mislead the international community, could not undermine Xinjiang's modernization process and impede China's development and progress.
