Crack Down on Drug Trafficking, Arrest a Cambodian and Seize Nearly 1kg of Drugs in Takeo Province
(Takeo): Special forces of the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on drug trafficking, arrested a Cambodian and confiscated nearly 1 kg of drugs in Takeo province. This is according to the report of the Anti-Crime Department, which was received by Fresh News on September 26, 2021.
The operation was carried out on the orders of Brigadier General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and Brigadier General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes. .
The report states that on September 24, 2021 at 11:30 AM, the specialized force of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes (A4) led by Major General Kheng Sarath, Deputy Director of the Department, with the coordination of Mr. Chiv Chantara Prosecutors of the Takeo Provincial Prosecutor's Office are investigating and cracking down on drug trafficking at the intersection of Street 3 in Kraing Tbal Village, Kraing Leav Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province.
During the crackdown, the police detained one suspect, Lin Toch, male, 47 years old, a Cambodian, and confiscated 854.36 grams of methamphetamine (ICE) powder.
Currently, the suspect and the above exhibits are being processed and sent to the Takeo Provincial Court according to the procedure.
(Kampong Speu): A baby bear was handed over to the park rangers at the Cardamom Mountain National Park Office in Kampong Speu province on the night of September 25, 2021 for further protection and conservation. This is the statement of Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment on September 26, 2021.
The Ministry of Environment thanked the people who saved the wildlife and handed over the bear cub, a rare species, to the ranger of the Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Environment.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, a ranger, took the cubs to the Oral Mountain Wildlife Sanctuary for safekeeping and released them back into the wild.
In Cambodia, the polar bear is present in some protected areas in the northeastern, eastern, northern and southwestern regions of Cambodia. Big bears are a diverse species of predators, including plants and animals.
Big bears can start to breed at the age of 4 to 5 years, usually breeding between June-July and breeding during November-March and usually giving birth to one or two cubs at a time. Bears can live up to 30 years. Bears are threatened by a number of factors, including habitat loss, poaching and illegal wildlife trade, gallstones and rearing.
Mr. Pheaktra said that the number of big bears was declining due to habitat loss, lack of foraging sites and hunting for commercial specimens. Big bears are found in Cambodia in suitable habitats for dense and semi-dense forest species.
At the same time, the Secretary of State asked a small number of people who are engaged in trapping animals to stop their activities because it is against the law and if law enforcement officers are caught, they will face the law in force.
He also called on people who like to eat wild animals and believe that eating wild animals or wild animals for good health should abandon this belief because it not only does not help health but harm health because of wildlife. Abundant with viruses to stop poaching and trapping illegally.
Mr. Neth Pheakda said that in the past eight months, more than ten thousand traps have been removed from the protected area to save many wildlife.
