(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he will try to address regional challenges when Cambodia chairs ASEAN in 2022.
The confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made in his speech at the United Nations General Assembly on the night of September 25, 2021.
In that speech, the Prime Minister stated that "As the chair of ASEAN next year, Cambodia will try to address common challenges in the region. With strong solidarity between ASEAN member countries and support from external partners, Cambodia will continue to accelerate the process of building the ASEAN Community and maintain the role of ASEAN as an important region for global trade, investment and supply chain. "
Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia will continue to promote the building of a vibrant and harmonious ASEAN community with protection for migrant workers, a green and environmentally friendly development agenda, digital revolution, handicraft development. And small and medium enterprises (MSMEs), as well as the promotion of entrepreneurship of women and youth.
Full Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the United Nations General Assembly (5 pages)
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at 10:30 pm on September 25, 2021, addressed the 76th General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly. Made via video system.
The 76th UN General Assembly High-Level Dialogue will be held under the theme "Building Resilience through Hope - to Rehabilitate Kovid-19 Sustainable Reconstruction Response". "To the needs of the planet, respect for the rights of citizens and the activation of the United Nations."
In his speech, the Prime Minister focused on a number of key issues, including: Socio-economic recovery in the wake of the 19-Kovid crisis as a top priority, continued pressure on international peace and security, the importance of multilateralism and cooperation. International transactions based on law.
Samdech Techo also highlighted the successful national vaccination campaign, economic recovery plan after the Kovid-19 crisis for sustainable development, efforts to address climate change and preparedness. Chair of the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM13) and the 2022 ASEAN Summit of Cambodia.
