(Phnom Penh): Hundreds of families who bought plots of land from Borey Kaing Meng have fulfilled their contract obligations, but so far it has been more than 10 years. The title deed (hard copy) has not been handed over to the buyer yet, making it very difficult for the customer to use the land he bought.
The lawyer representing the client who bought the plot of land in Borey Kaing Meng stated that the client had signed an agreement to buy the plot of land from Borey Kaing Meng since 2007, which was previously located in Kandal Steung district, Kandal province, and now part of the location The Borey is cut into Phnom Penh, with the Borey side promising that when customers pay all the money, the Borey will run the transfer of ownership to the customer without any problems.
All of this has resulted in countless losses to customers, both in terms of time and benefits, including the failure to fulfill various tax obligations to the state.
Unable to bear it any longer, they decided to rely on a lawyer to make a final letter of notification to demand that the Kaing Meng Borey owners fulfill their obligation to transfer ownership to them, leaving 15 days otherwise. They will continue to take legal action.
