The meeting was co-chaired by the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Indonesia, Retino Marsudi, who facilitated the ASEAN-US Dialogue Partnership, and the US Secretary of State, Anthony Blinken.
The ASEAN and US Foreign Ministers agreed to strengthen ASEAN-US cooperation to combat the Kovid-19 pandemic and its devastating effects and ensure a strong economic recovery. .
ASEAN commends US commitment to comprehensive action toward ending global pandemic, as well as providing more than 23 million doses of vaccine and nearly $ 160 million in relief aid Health and Humanitarian Emergency to ASEAN Member States and USAID Efforts to Assist ASEAN in Developing the ASEAN Public Health Emergency Coordination System.
At the meeting, the ASEAN and US Foreign Ministers shared the view that vaccines should not be used as a political tool and the importance of promoting equitable access to vaccines and vaccinating the surrounding population. The world as fast as possible.
The Meeting expressed support for the ASEAN-US Leaders' Declaration on Digital Development to be adopted at the 9th ASEAN-US Summit in October 2021, which may Strengthen ASEAN's readiness for the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) and support ASEAN's efforts to integrate digital communications and the ICT development gap in ASEAN.
