Samdech Heng Samrin: For 28 years, the National Assembly has always fulfilled its role in accordance with the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, said this morning, September 24, 2021, that for the past 28 years, the National Assembly has always fulfilled its role in accordance with the Constitution in contributing to the improvement of living standards. Of the people and the development of the nation.
Remarks by the President of the National Assembly on the 28th anniversary (September 24, 1993 - September 24, 2021) of the day of promulgation of the Constitution, which is the supreme law and the foundation of the legal framework to lead the nation's development.
Samdech Heng Samrin continued that the Constitution of 1993 made our country return to the "Kingdom of Cambodia" again after we ended the civil war and had the first free general election in 1993 and brought peace, national unity and progress in our society to this day.
Samdech Heng Samrin added that let the compatriots respect, protect and abide by the Constitution in order to build and promote the rule of law in the Kingdom of Cambodia, we unite to strengthen national unity, protect the territory of Cambodia, sovereignty and the beloved Angkor civilization of our nation. In leading the motherland towards an island of peace, prosperity and prosperity forever.
Constitution born after the fire crisis is 28 years old
(Phnom Penh): The Constitution is the supreme law for a democratic Cambodia. The Constitution governs the sovereignty, role and status of the King, the fundamental rights of the Cambodian people, the economy, education, culture and social affairs, the functioning of the National Assembly, the Senate, the Congress and the Royal Government, the functioning of the judiciary, the Constitutional Council, the administration and the National Assembly.
In particular, the Constitution is also a line of decree to guide Cambodians to live according to the law. In addition, all laws and legal documents of the Kingdom of Cambodia must be in accordance with the Constitution, otherwise those laws and legal documents will be unconstitutional.
The Constitution that Cambodia is currently using has been revived after decades of endless war ended under the Paris Peace Accords of October 23, 1991. This Constitution is also a message of the spirit of unity of the Cambodian leaders, including Samdech Preah Borom Ratanakoth, Norodom Sihanouk, the leader of the resistance movement, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Cambodian government.
Mr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, stated that the current Constitution is the supreme law born of the common will of the Cambodian people of all political persuasions, has become a strong legal basis for building a peaceful, stable and progressive Cambodia. By sustainability.
The President of the Constitutional Council also stated that the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia is a historic achievement after the Cambodian people reached an agreement on a common political solution to the Cambodian conflict at the Paris Conference on Cambodia on October 23, 1991.
* Third Constitution: is the Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which has only 21 articles, divided into 16 chapters, and was adopted on January 5, 1976. The Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which transformed the regime in Cambodia from a republic to a communist dictatorship, massacred its own people for three years, eight months and 20 days.
