Minister of Commerce encourages consumers to report fraudulent activities of businesses or business owners
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce and the German Cooperation Agency on September 23, 2021 jointly organized a national workshop to disseminate the Law on Consumer Protection under the theme "Ethical Doing Business: Welfare". Of your customers and your business. ”
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and was attended by Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, and Frank Jattke, Chairman of the ASEAN Working Group of the German Cooperation Agency (GIZ). ) In Cambodia, as well as representatives of the private sector and many other development partners, about 150 people.
Speaking at the seminar, Mr. Pan Sosak called on business people who have not yet fulfilled their consumer protection obligations to pay attention to implementing those obligations in accordance with the laws and regulations in force to contribute to the institution. Authorities and consumers in building a harmonious and sustainable society.
On that occasion, the Minister of Commerce also encouraged consumers to report any business ventures and business owners who commit dishonest activities in business to the Ministry of Commerce or the National Committee for Consumer Protection through the General Department of Consumer Protection. Compete and crack down on fraud (KPR) to find common solutions in a timely manner.
"Effective consumer protection requires businesses to be informed of their obligations to consumers and to avoid any actions that could distort, misrepresent or harm consumers, both inside and outside the country," he said. "Operations are traditional or in e-commerce."
"Protecting the interests and rights of consumers should not be seen as an obstacle to business," he added. In contrast, businesses that sell products or services honestly and serve their customers fairly, for example, by adhering to product warranties and guarantees, can expand their customer base and competitiveness. "Representatives from the business community can also act as trusted partners for the government in supporting consumer protection."
Frank Jattke, Head of the ASEAN Working Group of the German Cooperation Agency (GIZ) in Cambodia, said that fair business, both online and offline, is the key to success. In business, a company that enjoys the full support of its customers or consumers can expand its customer base.
Mr Francois Kerr announced that the code of conduct was expected to be disseminated across all ASEAN member countries and was part of efforts to rebuild the country after the epidemic.
Please be informed that Cambodia has the youngest consumer protection regime in ASEAN and the Law on Consumer Protection was promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1119/016 dated November 2, 2019. . In that, the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPF) acts as an important enforcement agency and is assigned duties related to consumer protection in accordance with the provisions of this law.
