Samdech Techo Advisor Asks Thai Education Minister to Provide Opportunity for Cambodian Workers' Children
(Bangkok, Thailand): Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism, requested the Thai Minister of Education to consider and provide opportunities for the children of Cambodian workers working in Thailand to receive an education in schools. Thai teaching.
Dr. Sok Sokretya's request was made during a courtesy call and discussion with Dr. Treenuch Thienthong, Minister of Education of Thailand. In this meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya and Dr. Minister of Education of Thailand discussed a lot of education issues, including the provision of scholarships for Cambodian students, as well as vocational training in Cambodia under the noble sponsorship of the Queen. Chakrey Sirindhorn.
In addition, Dr. Sok Sokretya also expressed concern for the children of Cambodian workers who missed the opportunity to study. In front of the Thai Minister of Education, Dr. Sok Sokretya asked the Thai government to support and take care of Cambodian children so that they have the same access to education as other children.
Responding to the request, the Thai Minister of Education emphasized that the Royal Government of Thailand pays close attention to Cambodian children who come with their parents to work in Thailand. At the same time, the Royal Government of Thailand has provided them with the opportunity to study in public schools and child care centers, just like Thai children.
Although Yana, the Minister promised to bring the above proposal to the Thai Cabinet to find ways to help children who are in need of basic rights to education and the right to development.
During the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya also asked the Thai Minister of Education to help train tourism professionals, as limited human resources in tourism may face shortages in the future when Cambodia welcomes international and world tourism. He reopened.
Dr. Sok Sokretya and Dr. Minister of Education of Thailand also discussed the Kampong Speu Institute of Technology under the auspices of Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn, who is currently on a mission to provide technical training to Cambodian students. Many to strengthen human resources to meet the current job needs in Cambodia.
Through the Minister of Education of Thailand, Dr. Sok Sokretya also expressed his gratitude to Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn for her attention in training human resources and the quality of education in Cambodia. The Prime Minister's personal adviser also thanked the Thai Ministry of Education for taking care of the Cambodian students who were studying in Thailand during Kovid-19.
In the above meeting, the Minister of Education of Thailand also expressed his congratulations and appreciation for the success of vaccination and control against tuberculosis 19 of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. She also expressed her appreciation for the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, which has brought full peace to Cambodia and rapid development in all areas.
