Chinese Foreign Minister calls on G20 to increase humanitarian aid to Afghanistan
BEIJING: Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi on Thursday called on the G20 to step up its efforts to provide aid to Afghanistan. This was released by the news agency CGTN on Thursday, September 23, 2021.
The Chinese diplomat made the call at the G20 foreign ministers' meeting on Afghanistan, which was held on video. Wang said any sanctions or restrictions imposed on Afghanistan should be lifted as soon as possible.
In addition, emphasizing the uncertainty of Afghanistan's future, Wang Yi also called on the G20 to play a constructive role in promoting peace, development and national reconciliation in the South Asian country.
In September, Beijing announced it would provide 200 million yuan ($ 31 million) in emergency aid, including food, winter supplies, vaccines and medicines to Afghanistan.
