(Phnom Penh): An accused military officer was released on bail by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court after the authorities sent him to court in connection with a case of "money fraud".
Chhon Amnat, a 41-year-old male military officer, was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on November 27 following a court arrest warrant. 2020.
After being sent to court on 22 September 2021, Mr. Sin Sovannaroth, Trial Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, with Mr. Lim Bunheng as the Prosecutor and Ms. Ith Lundy as the Trial Clerk, tried the accused. Chhon Amnat was charged with fraud in Phnom Penh on May 18, 2018 in accordance with Articles 377 and 378 of the Penal Code.
Following the hearing, Trial Judge Sin Sovannaroth decided to release Chhun Amnat, that is, without detention, despite the request of Lim Bunheng.
During the hearing, Mr. Lim Bunheng, on behalf of the Prosecution, stated that the accused, Chhon Amnath, did not appear and testify twice before the investigating judge on the summons, so the investigating judge issued an order. To arrest the accused.
Mr. Lim Bunheng added that the accused, Chhon Amnath, refused to appear during the summons hearing until the arrest warrant was issued by the investigating judge, so the court could try him, so the court should consider detaining him. Temporarily charged.
However, the request of the Prosecutor was not considered by Trial Judge Sin Sovannarot, who decided to release the accused Chhon Amnath. Mr. M. Chhun Lim: The 1993 Constitution is the longest-lived Constitution compared to the five constitutions of Cambodia in the past.
(Phnom Penh): The Constitution of Cambodia, promulgated in 1993 after more than two decades of war, will turn 28 years old on September 24, 2021 tomorrow. Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council of Cambodia, stated that the Constitution of the Second Kingdom of Cambodia has become the oldest and longest-lasting Constitution compared to the five constitutions of Cambodia in the past.
The Constitution is the supreme law for a democratic Cambodia. The Constitution governs the sovereignty, role and status of the King, the fundamental rights of the Cambodian people, the economy, education, culture and social affairs, the functioning of the National Assembly, the Senate, the Congress and the Royal Government, the functioning of the judiciary, the Constitutional Council, the administration and the National Assembly.
Cambodia first drafted its constitution in 1947. The Constitution of Cambodia has changed five times in a row due to the change of leadership in line with the evolving political situation in Cambodia. The first changes in the Khmer Republic, the second in Democratic Kampuchea, the third in Democratic Kampuchea, the fourth in the Democratic Republic of Kampuchea, and the fifth in the current constitution.
Please be informed that Cambodia first had a constitution in 1947 and the current constitution is a constitution established in 1993. The six constitutions that Cambodia has had include the following:
* First Constitution: The first Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia was adopted on May 6, 1947. The 1947 constitution is a constitutional one, but this constitution does not change the form of leadership, only some changes according to the actual situation.
* Second Constitution: The Constitution of the Khmer Republic was adopted on May 10, 1972. This constitution changed the political system from a constitutional monarchy to a US-style republic.
* Third Constitution: The Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea was adopted on January 5, 1976. The Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which transformed the regime in Cambodia from a republic to a communist dictatorship, massacred its own people for three years, eight months and 20 days.
* Fourth Constitution: The Constitution of the People's Republic of Democratic Kampuchea was promulgated by Decree No. 01, dated June 25, 1981.
5th Constitution: On April 30, 1989, the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Kampuchea amended this Constitution by changing the name of Cambodia from the People's Republic of Cambodia to the State of Cambodia in Article 4 of the Constitution states: Implement a multi-party political regime.
* Sixth Constitution: is a constitution born after the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991. On May 23-28, 1993, Cambodians across the country went to the polls to elect 120 Constituencies across the country through a proportional system in which 20 parties participated. Grab the ballot.
