Banteay Srei District Administration Prepares New Temporary Stalls after Banteay Srei Market Closes
(Siem Reap): The Banteay Srei District Administration has set up a new temporary stall for people selling vegetables, fish, meat and some other daily necessities instead of the Banteay Srei Market, which has been temporarily closed.
Banteay Srei District Governor Khim Finang wrote on his Facebook page on the evening of September 22 that the market would be reopened on Friday, September 24, replacing the two-week-suspended Banteay Srei Market. .
Mr. Khim Finang described that the new location is on the section of Rubber Road No. 67 at the pig nose of the "Triangle Garden" in front of Srey Kulen Restaurant, about 200 meters from the old location of Banteay Srei Market. The team has prepared a temporary detour as shown in the diagram below to ensure that traffic on National Road 67 will continue to function normally during the two weeks.
Mr. Khim Finang said that these temporary stalls were set up with proper security gaps and were located on a large open space, selling only in the morning and required to be dismantled at noon in the form of a wax market. It has already been organized in Preah Dak village.
Each stall must have no more than two vendors, and each vendor must wear a mask, face mask, identification tag, and be tested for negative results before being allowed to sell in the new location. Absolutely must not be directly involved with the positive.
The district governor hopes that the provision of temporary stalls will be able to meet the basic needs of the people in the community, as well as open the door for some traders to continue to earn money to support their livelihood during the market is closed to prevent infection. Outbreak of Kovid-19 disease.
