Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Seafood duck beak is present at Macro Shopping Mall as part of supporting the conservation of mangrove trees and increasing income for the community
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, is optimistic that the support for processed food from duck beak shells originating from Koh Kong is to support the conservation of mangrove trees and increase income for the community.
Neth Pheaktra's expression of optimism was made on the occasion of attending the Dissemination Ceremony of Peam Krasop Duck Beak Community in Koh Kong Province at Macro Shopping Mall in Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh on the evening of September 22. This 2021.
"Duck beak is a local product that is abundant in the Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary in Koh Kong Province and symbolizes the sustainability of natural resources, born of a harmonious balance between economic activity and conservation, especially forest conservation," he said. "Mangoes are starting to appear in the macro market to join as a new food option for seafood lovers."
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that the duck beak shell, which is a product of Koh Kong province and also a delicious kind of shellfish, brought to be distributed at Macro Market is another new step to expand the market of duck beak shells. In the local market and as part of the efforts of the General Department of Local Communities of the Ministry of Environment to help improve the livelihood and family economy of the protected area community.
At the same time, he thanked the Masterpiece Market and Macro Market for cooperating with the Ministry of Environment to bring this local product to market. This is part of marketing for local products and also part of marine conservation, especially in the protection of mangrove forests in Koh Kong province, which is an important source of food security for local people. That.
It should be noted that the introduction of beak shells for sale at Macro Market was made in collaboration with the Cambodian Sustainable Landscape and Ecotourism Project of the Ministry of Environment with Macro Market in both Phnom Penh and Siem Reap. Special price from September 22 to October 5, 2021.
The senior official said that duck beak shells are famous abroad because of their delicious taste, but for Cambodians, people do not seem to know much about this type of shell. For the sale of Koh Kong duck beak at Macro Market now is a demonstration of the expansion of the community product market to promote local products and the community family economy, as well as participate in the protection and conservation of resources. Nature.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated: "When you support these products, it means that you join the Ministry of Environment to protect our natural resources, increase employment to local people in the community, which means community "He has a job, he has an income, and the other part is involved in protecting mangroves."
He added that the announcement of Koh Kong duck beak sale at Macro Market is also part of the aim to make Koh Kong duck beak products get community support from restaurant owners, hotels and the general public. . In addition, it also encourages the community to collect duck beak shells to participate in outreach activities and increase knowledge on product development and food processing.
In addition, by promoting the sale of duck beak at Macro Market, HE hopes to help promote this seafood product to more Cambodians and turn to eat more of this food.
He said that in order to achieve these goals, the CSLEP project will work with development partners and the private sector to create a favorable environment for investment in conservation-friendly economic activities. At the same time, the development of a policy on the export of duck beak products is also a priority for the CSLEP project to improve the overseas market situation.
Currently, the project has collaborated with the parent company and Macro Cambodia to organize the process of processing quality and hygienic products for supply to the market in Cambodia, as well as widely disseminated to the people of Cambodia.
Ms. Phal Chakrya, Executive Director of Samneang Me Market, said that after the indication of the Ministry of Environment and the attention of Macro Market itself, which wants to promote local products, the company took the duck beak shell, which is a food. But famous to sell ads now.
She said that in the past, the market for selling duck beak was not yet widespread, so the company advertised and hoped that the Cambodian people would support the revival because in addition to promoting local products, it also helps livelihoods. The community that grows this kind of shellfish.
The executive director of the Mother Market added that from now on, Cambodians can buy duck beak shells in the supermarket in all provinces and cities because there is a wide range of sales.
It should be noted that the community of Peam Krasop Protected Area in Koh Kong Province can produce about 3,210 tons of duck beak to supply the market per season, and the community can usually harvest duck beak from November to March or there is a delay. Little based on factors of market demand.
It should be noted that in the past, the Ministry of Environment has encouraged communities to increase duck beak raising, while high market demand can help improve livelihoods and the family economy.
