(Phnom Penh): The Youth Forum for Environmental Dialogue 2021, organized by the Ministry of Environment in collaboration with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, found the winners of this competition on Thursday, September 22, 2021.
As a result of the competition, Chbar Ampov High School of Phnom Penh won the first prize, Hun Sen Borey High School 100 won the second prize, and Russey Keo High School and Hun Sen Chak Angre High School won the third prize.
Mr. Chuob Paris, Director General of the General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information of the Ministry of Environment, said that the Youth Forum on Environmental Dialogue 2021 is the 41st and first time of the online organization, which started in August 2021. And divided into three stages: Introductory, First and Final.
He added that the forum provided an opportunity for young people to study, research and find new scientific arguments, support their position, exchange knowledge and experiences from speakers and environmental experts, and share that knowledge with the public. More general and helped to provide more knowledge to young people and as well as helping other young people to learn about the environment.
At the same time, the Secretary of State stated that Cambodia is moving forward to make progress in line with the vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which will transform Cambodia from a low middle income country to a high middle income country by 2030. Become a high-income country by 2050.
In line with this vision, the Royal Government has also considered sustainable development, which refers to economic growth, social development and a greater focus on environmental friendliness. Therefore, the Environmental Youth Forum is a way to share environmental information and love for the environment to other citizens, in addition to other mechanisms that the Ministry of Environment has set up to mainstream and disseminate environmental knowledge among the people.
At the same time, the Secretary of State encouraged young people to do more research on the environmental sector in order to become more knowledgeable in participating in the protection of the environment of Cambodia better in the future.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra thanked the leadership of the General Department of Environmental Knowledge and Information and especially the Department of Environmental Education for its efforts to develop a comprehensive program of environmental knowledge to encourage young people to take the initiative. Environmental protection, management of natural resources, biodiversity conservation and sustainable living.
It should be noted that this forum has 8 high school students participating in the competition, including: Hun Sen Chak Angre High School, Chbar Ampov High School, Russey Keo High School, Hun Sen Borey High School 100, Hun Sen Chumpouvorn High School, Wat Koh High School, Chea Sim Samaki High School, Chea Sim High School Santhor Mok.
