Jean Malin: Non-professional analysis and scientific research base could face legal liability
Mr. Malin's remarks came after a number of civil society groups called on the Royal Government of Cambodia to "stop threatening analysts."
Regarding the appeal of the civil society group, the spokesman of the Ministry of Justice, Mr. Chin Malin, made the following four points:
First: "Analysis, which is considered a right to freedom of expression and opinion protected by law, is a professional analysis, meaning a scientific analysis based on a clear method of research. Based on theoretical aspects, general principles, interviews and practical applications, etc.
Second, some of the analyzes in Cambodia that their group has branded and referred to as independent analysts for criticizing the government are not professional and scientific analysis, but emotional analysis. These include love, hate, and resentment, as well as political tendencies.
Thirdly, do not be an analyst following some foreign interviewers and radio stations that have anti-government political tendencies and national interests, because what they want is the views of analysts that match their goals to comment. Release, publish, and publish only to attack, denigrate, and criticize the government for defamation.
