The accident happened on National Road 8 in Prek Tamak village, Prek Tamak commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province on September 20, 2021, caused by a truck driving down the Prek Tamak bridge at high speed, unable to control the steering wheel. Three people were killed and six others were seriously injured when a motorcycle, a car and a shop near a bridge collided.
