Ministry of Tourism: Cambodia, India are planning to boost tourism after Kovid 19 crisis
(Phnom Penh): Leaders and working groups of the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia and India have agreed on a plan to revitalize tourism after the Kovid-19 crisis. This is according to Mr. Try Chhiv, Director of the Department of International and ASEAN Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism.
Mr. Try Chhiv confirmed that the bilateral agreement was made during the third meeting of the Cambodia-India Tourism Working Group via video conferencing on September 22, 2021.
Mr. Try Chhiv added that the meeting discussed and agreed on topics such as:
1. Expansion of tourism cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of India after the Kovid-19 crisis.
2. Promote the promotion of tourism destinations, especially cultural and natural tourism of the two countries.
3. Exchanging experiences in promoting, developing and managing tourist destinations, exchanging tour packages of tour operators of the two countries.
4. Promoting cooperation between stakeholders in the tourism sector and promoting cooperation in human resource development.
Mr. Thong Rathsak also informed the meeting about the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022, which is hosted by Cambodia and will take place from 16 to 22 January 2022 in Sihanoukville. The 9th ASEAN-India Tourism Ministerial Meeting will also be held at the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022. After that, Cambodia will host the fourth Cambodia-India Working Group Meeting during May 2022.
