According to the Ministry of Tourism, tour guides who have not been vaccinated against Kovid-19 for any health reason must be certified by their local health authority.
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the difficulties that people often suffer in the context of the epidemic of Kovid 19, the Cambodian Red Cross continues to help and give gifts to all the most vulnerable people across the country. In fact, on the morning of September 22, 2021, 17 poor families in Phnom Penh received donations in the form of food, supplies and equipment to prevent Kovid 19, as well as some funds.
The handover ceremony was held at the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters in the presence of Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross and some associates of the Cambodian Red Cross.
On that occasion, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak had a talk with the people in connection with the speech of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who sent a message of condolences to the people who came today. In particular, encouraged good health care and continue to work together to overcome difficulties for themselves and their families.
In addition, in the context of the spread of Kovid 19, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak called on all citizens to adhere to the health rules and guidelines of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, 3 protection and 3 must not learn Live a normal life in a new way to participate in the fight against Kovid 19 responsibly.
Ms. Men Neary Sopheak continued, "After receiving the information that our 17 families, some of them work as sanitation workers, run motodups such as motorbikes, tricycles and people with various chronic health problems. In short supply, the Cambodian Red Cross immediately arranged to give them gifts. "And our team continues to carry out this humanitarian action to rescue our citizens on time and to their destination, even during the Kovid 19 season."
At the same time, Ms. Thor Sary, over 50 years old and physically ill, who came to receive humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross, said with tears and excitement, "I am very happy that Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Has continued to help his children so far. I respectfully wish Samdech Kittipritthbandit a long life to be a shadow for all his children.
