(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, told Fresh News on September 22 that Darasakor International Airport in Koh Kong Province will be completed in October. The trial run, scheduled for December 2021, may be postponed until early 2022.
The delay in launching the test was due to a recent review by the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, which found that there was still some work that the company needed more time to complete, such as providing information and safety-related documents prior to Civil Aviation. Officially published.
