Cambodia focuses more on rice exports to China after declining total rice exports (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia is focusing more on rice exports to China after exports Rice exports to European markets and some countries are declining. The problem of decline due to rising shipping costs combined with a lack of shipping containers.
He added, however, that Cambodia still needs all markets, including the European Union, ASEAN, Australia, Gabon, the United States, etc., because Cambodian rice leads to fragrant rice that needs a specific market.
He stressed that not only Cambodia is looking at the Chinese market, Cambodia's neighboring countries are also turning to the Chinese market, because in general, other countries produce cheap rice, currently the average price is only $ 380. Per tonne, while Cambodia produces fragrant rice as a priority, which costs between $ 650-800 per tonne.
He noted that the decline in rice exports to the European market was due to transportation problems, limited supply of services and high demand, while the influx of containers to the EU was greater than the inflows. There is congestion of container hulls at ports and container terminals in the European Union.
He added that currently Cambodia needs to ship about 400 containers per week to the European Union, but the amount is not allowed only 100 to 150 containers.
"This challenge is only a global and transitional one for the EU market. As long as shipping and sea shipments are back to normal, the journey will return to normal," he said. The rice that Cambodia exports to the European Union is fragrant rice and organic rice.
It should be noted that the total volume of exports in the first eight months of 2021 was 342,447 tons, valued at 248.35 million US dollars. Exports have declined in both volume and volume.
