The following is the decision of Preah Vihear Administration: Pailin Provincial Customs and Excise Branch informs car owners duty free and import duty to pay tax from today until June 30, 2022
The announcement of Pailin Provincial Customs and Excise Branch, obtained by Fresh News this morning, states that Pailin Customs and Excise will collect taxes and import duties on existing tax-free vehicles in those districts in accordance with the policy. And the following mechanisms:
* First: Vehicle owners will receive a tax deduction of 10% of the total tax payable. This mitigation has a deadline of December 31, 2021 and does not cover vehicles with a production year of 2021. After this period, vehicle owners will not receive a discount.
* Second: For right-hand drive vehicles, car owners must make a deposit equal to the total tax and duty minus 10% and must take the car to repair the steering wheel from right to left until June 30, 2022. . After steering, the car owner can come and get the tax receipt and license from the customs officer.
* Third: From July 1, 2022 onwards (tax-free vehicles that are cracked down will be required to pay taxes and duties, including fines according to the regulations in force. For right-hand drive vehicles, which are prohibited in the case. Cracked will be destroyed or disassembled as spare parts.
* Fourth: Tax-free vehicle owners can come to fulfill their tax and duty obligations at the Customs and Excise Branch of Pailin Province, located at National Road 57, Dey Krahorm Village, Sangkat Otavao, Pailin City, Pailin Province. Contact telephone number 097 464 73 66, 096 58 72 902.
Pailin Customs and Excise Branch would like to call on all duty-free vehicle owners to voluntarily come to fulfill their tax and import duties in a timely manner in accordance with the principles and mechanisms as stated in the notice.
