(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), emphasized that the new investment law is in line with the Free Trade Agreement on the opening of the Cambodian market and Attract more investment.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea made this remark during the 7th session of the 4th Senate to approve the new investment law.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea stated that "this new investment law is part of the economic recovery This law will allow Cambodia to take advantage of the FTA agreement with friends. "China and other free trade partners, including the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (AEC-RCEP)."
He stressed that the signing of all forms of free trade is an opening of the Cambodian market, letting investors know that when they come to produce in Cambodia, they will be able to export to those countries.
He added that the new investment law is very important in the context that Cambodia is currently facing the problem of the spread of Kovid-19.
In addition, the CDC Secretary-General claimed that the new investment law was attractive, so he hoped that the implementation of the new law would attract more investors and encourage more local investors to participate.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea stated that the new investment law has many points that help the local industry by attracting investment and job creation.
The priorities are:
* Modernization, increasing the productivity of local industries, strengthening connectivity to regional and global supply chains by promoting the growth of capital inflows, technology transfer, knowledge and know-how.
Increasing Cambodia's competitiveness to make its economic structure more diversified and resilient to regional and global crises. Providing protection of legitimate rights and interests to investors in the Kingdom of Cambodia through the establishment of a comprehensive and balanced legal framework in line with national interests.
This draft law consists of 12 chapters and 42 articles and was approved by the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia for the first time by 92 votes out of the total number of members of the National Assembly on September 9, 2021 at the 6th session of the National Assembly. 6 and was the 7th session of the 4th Senate for approval on September 20, 2021.
