Bar Association Condemns Lawyer Phan Chansak for Violation of Lawyer Law and Election Campaign
In the same statement, the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia condemned the actions of lawyer Phan Chansak, ID 253, who posted a public message in the telegram group "CLO-Opinion of Cambodian Lawyers" on September 18-19, 2021. "Sell one ballot for $ 1,000 while the candidate is campaigning."
The Bar Association claims that this act is a violation of the Code of Conduct for Lawyers and the Decision on the Election Campaign for the 10th Mandate Bar Council (2021-2024) with the intent to seriously damage the honor, reputation and Dignity of the Bar Association, Candidates and Members of the Bar Association.
According to Article 50 of the Code of Conduct for Lawyers: "By their conduct, each lawyer must be responsible for the reputation of the Bar Association." In Article 10 of the Decision on the Campaign for the Election of Members of the Bar Council of the 10th Mandate (2021-2024), Article 5 prohibits the provision of money or materials to voters by any means.
The Bar Association has stated that it will take strict action against lawyer Phan Chansak for violating the Code of Conduct for Lawyers and the Decision on the 10th Mandate Bar Association Election Campaign (2021-2024).
The Bar Association would like to remind the candidates and supporters that all campaign activities must adhere to the principles of the election campaign set out in the decision on the election campaign to elect members of the Bar Council.
