Mr. Theng Sothol said that all monasteries must implement the strictest health safety measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, including the new mutated virus that Delta, including the appointment of a thermometer. Alcohol dispensers containing alcohol or gel provide hand washing facilities at all entrances.
Take care to clean regularly in the bathroom and the place where there is a lot of exposure, put up signs indicating the wearing of masks and keep safety gaps, advise the pagoda committee at all levels and Buddhists to wear masks or face masks. In particular, keep the principle of social safety distance of at least 1.5 meters apart, avoid standing in close proximity or close to each other by limiting the number of participants in proportion to the location of the celebration.
On that occasion, the Chamkar Mon District Administration also donated some materials to the 4 pagodas, in which 1 pagoda received 1 thermometer, 1 can of alcohol equal to 30 liters and 1 case equal to 2000 mass.
