TOKYO: The Japanese government on Monday decided to convene an extraordinary session of parliament on October 4, 2021 to determine a new prime minister ahead of the November general election. This was released by the Xinhua News Agency on Tuesday, September 21, 2021.
However, the election of the chairman of Japan's ruling "Democratic Party (LDP)", which will take place on September 29, 2021, is expected to determine who will be the next prime minister. Caretaker Minister Yoshihide Suga will resign later this month because the LDP is the party that controls the majority in Japan's parliament.
It should be noted that the general election in Japan is likely to be held on November 7 or 14, 2021.
