Philippines announces support for Australia over US-UK submarine technology
MANILA: The Philippines has announced its support for the AUKUS trilateral security agreement between the United States, the United Kingdom and Australia, in particular the provision of nuclear submarine technology to Australia. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday afternoon, September 21, 2021.
The AUKUS (A-UK-US) tripartite security agreement and its pledge to help Australia build nuclear-submarines have been the subject of much controversy and condemnation, not just by one Chinese giant. The United States' stalemate allies in the European Union are also protesting, with France being considered the biggest loser.
In contrast to Indonesia and Malaysia, which last week issued "reminds Australia" of security responsibilities in the Indo-Pacific region and fear of instability in Southeast Asia due to submarine-nuclear competition. The Philippines, meanwhile, has announced its support for what the United States, Britain and Australia have decided.
