Message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of International Peace Day, September 21, 2021
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, issued a congratulatory message on the occasion of the International Day of Peace on September 21, 2021.
Samdech Techo's message received by Fresh News this morning (September 21) states that the United Nations has adopted September 21 every year for the world to celebrate International Day of Peace dedicated to strengthening Peace of mind for people and countries all over the world.
For 2021, in the context of the world being severely affected by the Kovid-19 pandemic, the International Day of Peace is organized under the theme "Rebuilding the World for Equitable and Sustainable". Give priority to peace, which is the foundation of a concerted effort to save the world from the catastrophe caused by this epidemic.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo is pleased to join the international community in celebrating this glorious International Day of Peace to raise global awareness of the unique values of peace and demonstrate Cambodia's unwavering commitment to In continuing to build and maintain peace, stability and long-term stability.
