Currently, 19 positive Kovid monks have been sent to a low-level treatment center at Puok High School in Siem Reap. As for the other monks, as well as their grandfathers, abbots, grandmothers and disciples, they were ordained in the pagoda.
After that, Minister Mam Bunheng and the working group of the Ministry of Health and Local Administration as well as the Health Department of Siem Reap Provincial Administration proceeded to Sambour village, Nokorpheas commune, Angkor Chum district with positive case Kovid-19. Local authorities have designated the village as a red zone and closed it down.
At the same time, Minister Mam Bunheng also inspected the sales activities of the people in Angkor Chum Market for education and inspection and inspected the activities of vaccination campaign against Kovid-19 to children from 6 years old to under 12 years old and from 12 to under 18 years old at Angkor Chum District Referral Hospital.
The Minister of Health also continued his visit to Varin village, Varin commune, Varin district, which had positive cases of Kovid-19, but no serious cases and no deaths. Local authorities have already decided to close the Warren village. The team then inspected the Kovid-19 Mental Illness Center at Sre Noi High School, where patients were being treated but there were no serious cases and no deaths.
At all locations where Minister Mam Bunheng and his team visited, they distributed health education materials, leaflets and explained prevention methods, including Rule 3, Prevention 3, and advised that if there were any suspicious symptoms, they should immediately report to the doctors or authorities. Local or by phone 115 and dial 4.
At the same time, the Minister of Health brought high praise from Samdech Techo Prime Minister to health officials, local authorities at all levels, armed forces of all kinds in Siem Reap, who have done their best to provide services to the people. Citizens with a high sense of responsibility. Indonesia sees record 19-day low Kovid infection in more than a year
