Mondulkiri Airport Construction Procedures Delayed due to Kovid 19 Crisis
(Phnom Penh): The Mondulkiri Airport project is in the process of preparing a proposal from the company that received the investment right to build the airport. Proposal processing has been slow due to the Kovid 19 crisis, which has hampered the entry and exit of foreign experts.
Construction of Mondulkiri Airport is scheduled to begin in 2022, but due to delays in the study process, plans may be delayed.
Mondulkiri Airport is planned to be built on a 300-hectare site about 20 kilometers from Sen Monorom, with an estimated investment of more than $ 80 million.
Mondulkiri is considered the fourth economic pole after Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap. Mondulkiri is considered to be a natural eco-tourism destination with a cool area with rich blue nature.
Mr. Chak Mengheang, Deputy Governor of Mondulkiri Province, said that Mondulkiri Province is the fourth pillar of the economy and tourism and the airport construction project will help raise the province's image even further. Currently, the construction of hotels, resorts, entertainment venues, restaurants is getting a lot of attention.
In particular, experts in the field of real estate have seen the potential of Mondulkiri ecotourism, especially planning to build an airport.
Mr. Chrek Soknim said that the land sector in Mondulkiri will be better when the airport construction project starts due to the airport, more time travel, more travelers, more passengers, the need for accommodation. There is also a lot of food, so the growth of the real estate sector increases and so does the price.
"Once the airport is built, land prices will rise sharply because only a handful of land in Mondulkiri province is being affected by prices," he said. "So when the airport starts construction, real estate prices will go up."
