(Kep): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, stated that the incinerator of solid waste incineration, which is the Ministry of Environment's offer to the Kep Provincial Administration, is not only a new achievement on the territory of Kep, but also the consideration of the Royal The Cambodian government provides additional means of support to sub-national administrations to take ownership of urban waste management more effectively.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this statement on September 20, 2021, during the inauguration ceremony of the incinerator of solid waste, hazardous waste from Chattalysak Center, Kovid 19 Hospital or medical waste from the hospital. And health centers in Kep province.
He emphasized that this new achievement will help to clean up the environment in Kep province and especially to give the trust of the people in the provincial administration to manage well the waste from the center and the Kovid 19 treatment center.
The senior official of the Ministry of Environment also praised and highly appreciated the Provincial Administration and the Department of Environment of Kep Province for facilitating and arranging the location for the installation of solid waste incinerators with the capacity to burn between 5 tons and 7 tons of solid waste. Per day to serve urban solid waste management.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, the incinerators that have been installed have been involved in the incineration of medical waste from Kovid 19 Medical Center and Cataractic Center, as these are in addition to the existing medical incinerators. In hospitals and health centers throughout Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that the management and packaging of solid waste from Chattalysak Center and Kovid 19 Hospital and from home care patients, including the spraying of disinfected alcohol will contribute to prevention. Epidemic of Kovid 19 disease.
The Secretary of State stated that if medical waste is not properly managed, it will become a virus that destroys people's health.
According to Som Piseth, Kep Provincial Governor thanked Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and the leadership of the Ministry of Environment for taking care of the provincial administration to strengthen the ownership of environmental sanitation management.
He said that this achievement is due to the joint efforts between the provincial administration and the leadership of the Ministry of Environment in charge of Kep province, especially Secretary of State Neth Pheaktra, who has worked diligently to effectively manage solid waste from the center and Kovid 19 Hospital and other medical waste.
Welcoming the new achievement, the provincial governor said that the solid waste incinerator was absolutely necessary for Kep to use to incinerate medical waste and waste from Chattalysak and Kovid 19 treatment centers without disposal. In the open field. He said the provincial administration has paid close attention to the management of these wastes.
At the same time, the Governor of Kep Province requested the Kep City Administration, which is responsible for the management of the incinerator, to pay close attention to maintaining this achievement for a long time and use it for cleaning. Environmental hygiene.
On behalf of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra thanked the Kep Provincial Administration, the Department of Environment and the specialized departments under Kep Province, as well as the relevant authorities for participating in the implementation of the Urban Solid Waste Management Policy submitted by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
At the same time, apply Kovid 19 antiseptic on the inside and outside of the bag and leave the rubbish separate before releasing it. With the official launch of the solid waste incinerator, Mr. Neth Pheaktra believes that this incinerator will effectively participate in the management of solid waste, medical waste in Kep.
