Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The bitter experience and lessons that Cambodia learned from the flames of war and the genocidal regime made the Cambodian people clearly understand the value of peace and stability
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that the bitter experience and lessons that Cambodia has learned in the more than two decades of war and genocide have made all Cambodians We clearly understand the values of peace and stability that are fundamental to the development of the nation.
In a message on the occasion of the International Day of Peace on September 21, 2021, Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that for almost 23 years since December 29, 1998, the end of the war on the motherland of Cambodia. Samdech's "win-win politics" brought complete peace and true national unity for the first time in Cambodian history.
Through the same message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that this precious and precious period has provided an opportunity for the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to work hard to restore and rebuild the nation, as well as to take strong steps on the path of development and achievement. Progress in all areas should be proud of the motto "Peace, Development".
Taking this opportunity, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen solemnly announces the strong commitment of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to protect, at all costs, the peace and stability that Cambodia has hardly achieved. Develop the nation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that due to the values of peace that Cambodia has achieved so hard, which has made the country progress in all areas remarkably and has encouraged Cambodia to strive to develop itself into a country that has Actively contribute to the cause of world peace.
