Phnom Penh Governor Introduces Security Forces to Protect Citizens, Especially Kovid 19 in Upcoming Pchum Ben Ceremony
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, urged the competent forces to protect the safety and security of the people in the upcoming Dak Ben and Pchum Ben ceremonies to be extremely careful to protect the safety of the people. In particular, to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in public places and to protect oneself, even with previous experience.
Mr. Khuong Sreng introduced this on September 20, 2021 in the video meeting from the distance of the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command at the Phnom Penh Capital Hall to discuss security, order and the strictest implementation of measures. Prevent Kovid-19 infection in Dak Ben and Pchum Ben ceremonies to achieve good security, safety and no risk of Kovid-19 infection.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also stated that after vaccinating the people in Phnom Penh and currently vaccinating children between the ages of 6 and under 12, Kovid-19 infection has decreased significantly in Phnom Penh, making it possible for us to walk. Steps will be taken to reopen the traffic of the people, reopen the factory, and recently reopened secondary and high schools.
