Kandal Provincial Governor successfully facilitates between Khmer Muslims, goats and slaughterhouse owners, agrees on the price of 4,000 Riels per animal and asks for understanding of the animal cleaning service fee of 2,000 Riels per animal
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophorn, Governor of Kandal Province, successfully mediated the dispute between Cambodian Muslim traders and goat owners on the price of 4,000 Riels per head and asked for an understanding of 2,000 Riels for animal hygiene services. On a goat. This compromise has been widely applauded by a large number of Cambodian Muslims.
The successful mediation took place in a coordination meeting at Ponhea Leu District Hall, presided over by Kong Sophorn, about 30 Cambodian Muslims and other relevant officials on the 20th. This September 2021.
Mr. Kong Sophoan mediated with a high level of psychological satisfaction that both parties could accept with a happy face, as the dispute has been going on for a long time, leading to verbal conflicts in the past.
Mr. Kong Sophoan spoke about the high attention of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has taken into account the well-being of people from all walks of life, and he also pays high attention to all the business of Citizens by making it easier for people to do business, especially to make it easier for citizens during the 19th Kovid era.
The governor of Kandal province explained the heroic ways surrounding the legitimacy of the goat business and the ease with which animals can be slaughtered at slaughterhouses.
Regarding this mediation, Mr. Him Mat and Ms. Sacharoh, representatives of goat farmers in Prek Ta Prohm village, Kampong Os commune, Ponhea Leu district, expressed their happiness and satisfaction that the provincial governor was satisfied with the long-standing dispute. In the past.
In this regard, Mr. Santhy, the owner of the slaughterhouse in the village above, also agreed to accept this mediation and that this is one of the greatest mediations made under the mediation of the provincial governor and that without the presence to participate in resolving. From the provincial governor, this story is still protracted, I do not know when it will end.
It should be informed that this compromise has decided to agree on the price of 4,000 Riel per head for one year and the next year to increase the price of 5,000 Riel until the end of the license, while the provincial governor will ask the Ministry of Agriculture to understand the service fee. Sanitation of 2,000 riel per goat, because the business has a low income due to Kovid 19 disease, and this is the basis for resolving the dispute can reach a decision acceptable to both parties.
