Takeo Provincial Customs and Excise Branch informs tax-free vehicle owners to take refuge until June 30, 2022
(Takeo): Takeo Provincial Customs and Excise Office has issued a notification to the owners of vehicles under various existing license plates in the district, no tax and import duty to pay tax from the date of this notice until the 30th June 2022.
Takeo Customs and Excise Branch will accept import tax or all kinds of vehicles, both right-hand drive and left-hand drive, which have not yet fulfilled their import tax obligations.
According to the announcement, the public who are using vehicles without import tax, please hurry to fulfill the obligation to pay import tax with incentives, including:
* First: Vehicle owners will receive a tax deduction of 10% of the total tax payable. This mitigation has a deadline of December 31, 2021 and does not cover vehicles with a production year of 2021. After this period, vehicle owners will not receive a discount.
* Second: For right-hand drive cars, car owners must make a deposit equal to the total tax and deduction of 1% and must take the car to change the steering wheel from right to left until June 30, 2022. . After adjusting the steering wheel, the car owner can come and get the receipt and diploma from the customs officer.
* Third: From July 1, 2022 onwards, tax-free vehicles that have been cracked down on will be required to pay taxes, including fines, according to the regulations in force. Right-hand drive vehicles, which are prohibited from being imported in the event of a crackdown, will be demolished or dismantled as spare parts.
