In modern times, astronomers have explained that the morning star, or thief, is Venus, the second planet in our solar system, between Mercury and Earth.
Astronomers have observed that every 584 days, Earth and Venus return to each other, averaging 40 million kilometers, and the nearest distance between the two is about 38 million kilometers. Due to the close proximity, Venus is the brightest planet in the sky after the moon.
