Please read the newsletter and flood forecast of the Ministry of Water Resources about the water level at the following hydrological stations: Education experts applaud the Royal Government on the vaccination campaign for children aged 6-12 years.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, September 17, 2021, announced the launch of a new campaign to vaccinate 19 children from 6 to 12 years old. Considered a highly responsible campaign to protect the lives of children from Kovid 19. The opening ceremony of the 19 Kovid vaccination campaign for children aged 6 to 12 took place at the Peace Palace.
According to Samdech Techo, vaccinating children between the ages of 6 and 12 is to create greater social resilience, which can lead to a wider social activity. In addition, the main goal of this vaccination is so that young children can return to school.
Individuals in the field of education have similarly said that all children are like vines to be inherited, that is, they must be educated to be the next generation to help develop the nation. Both public and private institutions have applauded the Royal Government for the recent vaccination campaign for children between the ages of 6 and 12, launched by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
"On behalf of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, I would like to thank and support the strategic decision of the head of government to vaccinate 6-12 year olds," he said.
Mr. Dim Virak Rith, Principal of Chaktomuk Secondary School, considered that the vaccination campaign for children aged 6-12 years old is the wisdom of the Royal Government and it is a serious consideration for young people who are the age to receive a thorough education. .
"Children need education and learning, which is the foundation," he said. "If our seeds or foundations are weak, then it will be difficult to get to the big level, so the Royal Government is very smart."
Speaking at the same time, Mr. Tip Naren, Director General and Founding President of ASEAN Heritage School, expressed his great pleasure that the Royal Government has sought vaccines for the compatriots, especially now focusing on children. He also urged parents and guardians to get their children vaccinated so that they can return to school directly.
"So we are happy and hopeful and hope that all parents and guardians will bring their children to be vaccinated as instructed by our government so that they can come to school," he said.
The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of South Korea are set to formally sign a Free Trade Agreement (FTA) in October 2021, with negotiations between the two sides closing in February 2021.
Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News this morning, September 20, 2021, that Minister Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, may be invited to sign the FTA. Go sign in person in Korea if the situation is better, or go online if the situation is still not good.
"Like the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement is another new effort and success of the Ministry of Commerce in opening markets for Cambodian exports," he said. "To the world market."
He said that the Korean market that Cambodia has decided to open now will increase opportunities for agricultural products, processed agricultural products, textiles, clothing, footwear, travel bags, rubber products, spare parts, electronic components, light industrial products, And a large number of other products produced by investors in and outside the SEZ may be exported duty-free to the Korean market.
At the same time, it facilitates the re-importation of electronic goods, pharmaceuticals, auto parts, and equipment that are raw materials and machinery for our production, which will lead to an increase. Increase production productivity as well as product quality for export.
At the same time, trade facilitation will be fully implemented, various non-tariff barriers, including sanitary and phytosanitary conditions, rules of origin, mutual recognition of standards assessment, production standards, quality of goods and Other technical barriers are also facilitated and exempted for the free flow of goods.
The free trade agreement will also bring about economic cooperation, technical exchanges and capacity building in partnership. Separately, negotiations on investment and services will be made after this agreement enters into force. This could further attract foreign investment to Cambodia and lead to the introduction and exchange of new technologies. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Pen Sovicheat.
Please be informed that in 2020, the trade volume between Cambodia and Korea reached a total of 729.13 million US dollars, an increase of 17.31 percent compared to 2019 of 881.76 million US dollars. The free trade agreement is expected to boost trade ties between the two countries to more than $ 1 billion.
