Senior Minister Kun Kim tells rescue teams to be ready to help people from the floods (Video inside) (Siem Reap): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, told rescue teams in all units to be ready. It came out to save people from the floods at a time when Cambodia will be affected by bad weather, leading to heavy rains at the end of September.
Senior Minister Kun Kim's remarks were made during a visit and conversation with Disaster Search and Rescue Operations 720 of Intervention Division 2 on Sunday, September 19, 2021.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister conveyed the greetings and memories of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all forces.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim mentioned Cambodia's risk of some adverse weather effects that could lead to strong winds and moderate to heavy rainfall across the country. According to the senior minister, this effect could lead to Cambodia being hit by heavy rains, flooding of the Mekong River in the provinces along the Mekong River and the northwestern provinces as well.
Faced with such a situation, Senior Minister Kun Kim reminded the rescue force to be ready to go to the rescue. In particular, check and prepare enough materials and equipment for rescue operations.
"The first thing to consider when a disaster strikes, especially floods, is to save the lives of the people, not to endanger the lives of the people without our rescue," he said. Therefore, our rescue force must be regularly equipped with both force and tactics for rescue operations. "When there is a disaster, our forces must leave immediately, not delay."
During the ceremony, the Senior Minister also said that in order to prepare for the disaster, liberate the lives of the people, the National Committee for Disaster Management has set up a clear relief structure in the six military zones and some units and opened training. Increase the rescue capacity and equip the necessary equipment and tools in this rescue operation.
The senior minister also called on people in flood-prone areas, especially fishermen, to be very careful about the dangers that may occur during the rainy season. Follow up on weather warnings and other announcements of the Ministry of Expertise and the media of the National Committee for Disaster Management to be prepared in advance.
The senior minister also reminded all local authorities, all of which are members of the National Committee for Disaster Management, to work closely together to disseminate disaster information to the people and to be prepared to help. They are when disaster strikes.
