Interior Ministry Spokesman: 69 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on September 18
(Phnom Penh): At least 69 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on September 18, 2021 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News this morning, September 19.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 69 suspects, 19 were arrested in 11 criminal cases and 50 were arrested in 17 drug cases.
Ministry of Water Resources: The effects of low pressure valleys and storms will cause moderate to heavy rainfall in Cambodia, some capitals and provinces face flooding
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a statement on the weather situation in Cambodia, stating that after regular monitoring and monitoring of the weather situation, it shows that Cambodia is currently suffering. The effects of the Indian low pressure valleys and the weak southwest monsoon kept the rain to moderate to low.
From September 20 to 23, 2021, the weather will change drastically, with the low pressure system re-emerging, coupled with the active low pressure currently in the South China Sea, which will drag across the northern part of Cambodia. May cause moderate to heavy rainfall.
Meanwhile, on September 24, 2021, there will be a depression in the South China Sea and will increase its influence to the 15th typhoon on September 25, 2021, heading towards Vietnam. Which will have a significant impact on the northeastern part of Cambodia.
According to the forecast, the weather in Cambodia from September 20 to 23, 2021 will be as follows:
1: Lowland area: Cloudy with scattered to moderate to heavy rain, which may cause flooding in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu, Pursat, Battambang, Pailin and Banteay Meanchey provinces.
2: Upland areas: Dangrek mountain range and Cardamom mountain range: cloudy, cloudy, haze and moderate to heavy rain in Pursat (Veal Veng district), Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom provinces. Through Stung Sen, which could cause floods.
3: Coastal areas: Cloudy skies, heavy fog, scattered to moderate to heavy rain mixed with moderate gusts, which may cause flooding in Koh Kong province, especially national roads. Number 4 can be threatened by flooding. On the sea surface, there will be rain, wind and waves of medium height.
In light of the above-mentioned weather conditions, the public should be informed and increase their vigilance to avoid any possible accidents.
Mr. Rofi Osman, Member of the National Assembly and his associates visited to provide houses for the elderly and distribute gifts to the people in Prey Chhor District, Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province.
(Kampong Cham): This morning, September 18, 2021, Mr. Rofi Osman, Member of the National Assembly and colleagues from the Secretariat of the Islamic Movement of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) visited and handed over houses to the elderly with gifts to the people. Shortage in Prey Chhor and Kang Meas districts, Kampong Cham province.
The donations included for Prek Khchay village, Prey Chhor district, including food packages for 70 families, each family received 15 kg of rice, 1 fishing rod, 1 liter of cooking oil, 2 kg of sugar, 2 kg of salt. They also donated $ 1,450 to build a house for the elderly and the disabled and organized a solidarity meal.
Meanwhile, in Angkor Ban 1 village, Kang Meas district distributed food packages to 60 families in each family: 15 kg of rice, 1 stick of fish, 1 liter of oil, 2 kg of sugar, 2 kg of salt. In addition, $ 1,000 was donated to the village committee for the construction of the grave fence, $ 300 was donated to the Cambodian Muslim Youth League, and $ 300 was purchased for fishing equipment and $ 200 for the elderly.
On behalf of the Muslim Movement, he also mentioned that these gifts are a contribution to solve the difficulties and concerns of the Muslim Movement of the Cambodian People's Party, which always cares about your well-being.
Mr. Rofi Osman reminded people of voting age to be responsible and make sure they have the correct name on the voter list and to be ready to check or re-register for those who have just reached voting age or who have just been elected. The relocation will start from October 12 to November 30, 2021, according to the announcement of the National Election Committee.
Launched an enterprise to produce glass, paper and straws made from Khmer rice, corn and potatoes, invested more than 5 million USD in Krakor district, Pursat province
(Pursat): TK & D has invested more than US $ 5 million in Takeo Krom village, Boeung Kantuot commune, Krakor district, Pursat province to produce paper cups and straws made from Khmer rice, corn and potatoes. Come (edible) without harming health and the environment, especially reducing plastic waste in society.
The enterprise was officially inaugurated on September 19, 2021 under the chairmanship of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province.
She added that TK & D will produce glass cups, paper and straws made from rice flour, corn flour and potato flour that can be consumed to supply the local market without the use of chemicals that are harmful to health and the environment, especially to reduce waste. Plastic creates greenery in Cambodia.
She said that this enterprise has also cooperated to invest more than 5 million US dollars in an area of more than 2 hectares in Takeo Krom village, Boeung Kantuot commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, which can absorb the labor market. Our population is more than 100 people.
On the occasion of cutting the ribbon to officially launch and inspect the operation of the TK & D enterprise chain, Mr. Mao Thunin expressed his full support for this investment and asked the enterprise to buy the original products. Farmers in the province can grow and harvest to supply the demand for the production of paper cups and straws made from Khmer rice, corn and potatoes.
At the same time, the provincial governor requested that this enterprise receive more support from customers to contribute to support the economy in the province as well as the Cambodian economy to be recognized internationally.
