This hotline, even if your phone does not have money, can still call. Experts on Khmer civilization: Khmer descendants should not be inspired to reject the ancient tradition of "throwing Ben in the Pchum Ben festival"
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert Rath Sandab said that in the tradition of the Khmer kingdom, when it comes to Pchum Ben festival, it is the longest festival among the traditional Khmer festivals or other traditional festivals. In the world, because it lasts for 15 days, from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach, which the Khmer people always celebrate this festival without interruption since ancient times, except for the Khmer Rouge dictatorship from 1975 to 1979 only.
Mr. Rath Sandab further stated that in this Khmer belief system, the word "ghost" has a negative meaning or causes the most serious shame to his family. Therefore, no one wants to confuse the spirits of their ancestors with such insults.
