(Phnom Penh): The heads of two major banking institutions in Cambodia explain to entrepreneurs as well as owners of small and medium enterprises about some ways to easily get credit from banks or microfinance institutions to expand business.
Preparing business financial statements is essential for easy access to credit from banks.
Dr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia (ABC) and Chief Executive Officer of ACLEDA Bank, stated, “To facilitate access to financial services from banks or microfinance institutions (entrepreneurs as well as small and medium enterprises). "Medium) to have a properly audited financial statement."
First, the declining business activities of SMEs that affect their income make it difficult for banks to provide additional loans when requested by banks as well as microfinance institutions.
Second, the history of repayments shows that in the banking sector as a whole, there are up to $ 30 billion in refinancing loans, equivalent to 15% of total loans in Cambodia. In applying for a new loan or applying for an additional loan, the bank as well as the microfinance institution see that the repayment history is slow.
Third, the lack of preparation for the filing of documents of SMEs found that when applying for a loan, some enterprises are not properly registered or financial documents are not clear.
Dr. In Channy pointed out that as of July 2021, banking institutions that are members of the Banking Association of Cambodia have provided nearly 36 billion US dollars in loans and nearly 44 billion US dollars in savings, which makes cash. In the banking sector, there are many vacancies.
The President of the Association of Banks in Cambodia said that the cash flow in the banking sector as a whole is large due to the demand for credit is not as high as before because traders are struggling.
He said the bank has weighed on the risk of lending, so the bank's prudence and low customer demand have increased the amount of cash available in the banking sector.
Dr. In Channy said that for traders who have difficulty doing business, they use the rest of their funds to deposit in the bank, which makes the cash in the bank more free.
Dr. In Channy added that the Bank's prudence is to keep the banking sector strong, as the banking sector must be strong to play an important role and be the backbone of the national economy.
