BEIJING: On September 17, France was scheduled to join the United States in celebrating the 240th anniversary of the war in the Gulf of Chesapeak. But on September 16, the three countries, the United States, Britain and Australia, announced the establishment of an Indo-Pacific security alliance and signed an agreement on the sharing of technology and production of nuclear submarines in order to counter China.
This has led to the annulment of the huge submarine agreement that France signed with Australia. Outraged, France canceled the previously scheduled celebrations. As the saying goes, when betraying the American allies, there is no hesitation. "The knife was stabbed in the back," French President Macron said angrily.
Under the guise of "America as a priority", the United States viewed the Allies as a tool for personal political gain, further weakening the US Alliance system. After all, what both Britain and Australia should consider is that the United States, as an ally, always abandons the alliance for personal gain, should it not harm its own interests?
As a nuclear-armed country, the United States has aligned itself with Britain, providing unwavering support for the development of military nuclear technology to Australia, a country without a nuclear weapon. Seriously negative to address external issues such as the nuclear issue on the Korean Peninsula and the Iran nuclear issue, as well as to undermine international peace.
