This is according to the official report from the Ministry of Health, which was received by Fresh News tonight. Below is the summary list of Kovid vaccination 19: Mission Day 1: 4 more elderly people over 100 years old in Ratanakkiri and Stung Treng provinces received a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen after volunteering for Kovid vaccination
(Ratanakkiri-Stung Treng): Four more 100-year-old grandparents in Ratanakkiri and Stung Treng provinces receive humanitarian donations from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, after they volunteered to be vaccinated. Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's humanitarian donation was handed over to her back on September 18, 2021 by Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the National Committee for the Kovid 19 Vaccination.
Grandparents 100 years and older who received gifts from Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Ratanakkiri include:
After the handing over ceremony of gifts to grandparents in Ratanakkiri province and the closing ceremony of the first round of 19 Kovid vaccination campaign for people aged 18 and over in Ratanakkiri province, Ms. O Vandin led the working group Travel to Stung Treng to give a gift to another 101-year-old grandmother in Siem Pang district.
The team, led by O Vandin, had to travel for hours to reach her home, crossing a long road, especially along the Cambodia-Laos border ring road, where the Cambodian-Lao army clashed in 2017. Just arrived at the house of the grandmother above.
On the occasion of handing over the gifts, Ms. O Vandin always brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to visit them and also asked about the health condition after vaccination against Kovid 19 and why. That prompted them to get vaccinated.
The four vaccinated grandparents thanked the Prime Minister for allowing him to be vaccinated and given him a gift on this occasion.
They expressed the view that the Kovid 19 vaccine is very important for them, even though they are old, but the vaccine can protect them from Kovid 19 even if they are infected. Neither did he get seriously ill.
Please be informed that according to the planned plan, Ms. O Vandin will lead the team to travel to Preah Vihear province on the morning of September 19, 2021 tomorrow to continue handing over Samdech Techo Hun Sen's humanitarian donation to the 100-year-old elderly. Another year up there. After finishing in Preah Vihear, Ms. O Vandin's team will continue to Kampong Cham to deliver more gifts there.
