Khmer Muslims selling goat meat caught by veterinarians asking Samdech Techo Hun Sen to solve three points and accuse veterinarians of oppressing people without understanding
(Kandal): Twenty-five Cambodian Muslim families living in Prek Ta Prohm village, Kampong Os commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, who are engaged in goat herding as a small family, are upset because the veterinary officials of Kandal province have confiscated and put pressure on the people. Enter the slaughterhouse by paying a lot of money and make various legal threats against them.
Residents added that they were upset and angry with Ol Dorin because he threatened, accused people of committing crimes (stealing) and raided their goats all night while negotiations were underway. Doing so causes citizens to become angry and provoke conflicts.
People's representatives respectfully request Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help solve the following points:
1: Eliminate the pressure for them to enter the kiosk (slaughterhouse) for those who have a small business Not much 3: Request the Governor of Kandal Province and the Minister to reconsider Mr. Ol Dorin's behavior, which caused a great deal of emotional distress, while the Cambodian Muslims here support and vote for the Cambodian People's Party 100%.
Separately, Mr. Santhy, the owner of the slaughterhouse, confirmed to Fresh News Agency in Kandal province that he would agree to the request of the people of 4,000 riel per head for two months, and if the situation of Kovid 19 still affects the livelihood of the people, he may Consider further delays as well.
Mr. Thorn Sovanna, Governor of Ponhea Leu District and Mr. Bun Toun Simonath, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kandal Province, in the evening of September 18, 2021 at the above slaughterhouse, confirmed that this matter should be raised. Settlement will be held at Ponhea Leu District Hall on the first Monday of next week.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of September 18, 2021, ordered Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, to chair a meeting to address the framework of policies, laws and regulations. Involved in the case of people killing goats in their homes.
The Prime Minister's order came after the Prime Minister on the morning of September 18, 2021, posted a video of a veterinarian in Kandal province catching goat meat of people who have been killed, which caused a lot of criticism. Strong.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that "the stage we are in is the agro-commercial stage where our farmers not only grow or raise animals to supply their families, but also to supply the market." At the same time, consider public health issues, infectious diseases from animals circulating in the market, hygiene issues, etc. I would like to thank you for your input, which has become an input for improvement. ”
The case of catching goat meat, which people have already killed, was found to have occurred in Prek Ta Prohm village, Kampong Os commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province. Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Inspects Work Progress of YLP Association in Banteay Meanchey Province
