Senior Minister Kun Kim: The army is ready to save the people from the flood disaster
(Battambang): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, emphasized that in accordance with the orders and instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Army and Disaster Management Officers have prepared their forces and qualifications in Rescue people from possible flood disasters this year.
Speaking at the handing over of relief materials and equipment to the 5th Military Command for use in disaster relief operations on September 17, 2021, Senior Minister Kun Kim said that natural disasters, especially disasters Floods are a disaster that has had a devastating effect on Cambodia every year on the lives and crops of its people.
The Senior Minister added that although Cambodia could not prevent this natural disaster, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, always pays close attention and consideration to address the impact and The difficulties arise from this disaster, especially to protect the lives of the people and try to save the lives of the people as a result of the disaster.
During the ceremony, the Senior Minister also said that in order to prepare for the disaster, liberate the lives of the people, the National Committee for Disaster Management has set up a clear relief structure in the six military zones and some units and opened more training. Rescue capacity as well as equip the necessary equipment and tools in this rescue operation.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, during the first eight months of 2021, there were 179 gusts in 25 provincial capitals. Caused collapse and severe damage to 837 houses, injuring 67 people and killing 5 people. There were 85 lightning strikes, killing 67 people, injuring 42 people and killing 40 animals.
In response to these issues, the Capital-Provincial Disaster Management Committee, in cooperation with the Cambodian Red Cross, national teams, organizations, including the Armed Forces, helped to restore the lives of the people in a timely manner. Cambodian-Chinese Buddhist Association Donates 10,000 Masks to Sports Spirit
