JAKARTA: The Indonesian government has reminded its neighbor Australia of its obligation to maintain peace, stability and security in the region after announcing a decision to equip a nuclear-powered submarine as part of an agreement. "A-UK-US" tripartite security with the United States and the United Kingdom. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Saturday afternoon, September 18, 2021.
In a statement posted on the Indonesian Foreign Ministry's website on Friday, the Indonesian government cautiously noted Australia's decision to equip a nuclear-powered submarine. .
"Indonesia is deeply concerned about the continuation of the arms race and the balance of power in the region," the statement said. The largest Southeast Asian nation also stressed the importance of Australia's commitment to continue its commitment to non-proliferation.
The archipelago has encouraged Australia and other stakeholders to push for dialogue to resolve issues peacefully. "In this regard, Indonesia emphasizes respect for international law, including the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS 1982), in maintaining peace and security in the region," the statement added.
Strong reactions have already taken place and in various forms surrounding the establishment of the "A-UK-US" trilateral security alliance and the sharing of nuclear-powered submarine technology from US and British to Australia
China has condemned the move as "extremely irresponsible for regional security", while France has expressed outrage over the $ 40 billion deal between the three countries. Nuclear submarine deal with Australia sunk
Senior Minister Meas Sophea continues to remind people not to forget to protect themselves from Kovid 19 even after vaccination
(Preah Vihear): Senior Minister Meas Sophea, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Preah Vihear Province, called on all citizens to continue to implement the "3 Do and 3 Protect" measures on a regular basis. And do not forget about Kovid 19 infection, even if everyone is vaccinated.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea made this call on the occasion that the Senior Minister chaired the meeting of the Provincial Party Committee, the meeting to assign and disseminate the instructions on the election campaign to the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election. Of the Provincial Party on the morning of September 18, 2021, with the participation of working groups at all levels.
Senior Minister Meas Sophea said that by implementing credible and realistic step-by-step measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in the country, one hand has actively fought against Kovid 19 and implemented the strategy. The three main ones are: prevention, treatment and vaccination, and on the other hand, the implementation of policies to balance people's lives and business in all sectors to maintain socio-economic balance.
The Senior Minister also called on the people to continue to implement the plan set for efficiency and success for the upcoming Commune / Sangkat Council elections of the 5th mandate 2022 and jointly implement measures to combat Kovid 19. By continuing to implement three or three preventive measures on a regular basis, even if we have been vaccinated or can be said to have a cure.
In addition, Senior Minister Meas Sophea also congratulated Mr. Muong Khim and Dr. Hun Vathana on their appointment as Deputy Chairmen of the Central Working Group to assist Preah Vihear Province and other working groups. Also. ARDB Director General Concludes Three-Day Mission to Monitor Rice Mills in Rice Procurement and Farming
In fact, Mr. Kao Thach, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of ARDB, led his officials to inspect the condition of rice mills and farmers in 5 provinces, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey. And Pailin for 3 days from 15 to 17 September 2021.
The visit to the rice mills is to check the effectiveness of the use of credit under the special government financing scheme provided through the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank to those mills.
With the heavy rice harvest approaching, Mr. Kao Thach encouraged all mill owners to continue to buy rice from farmers as much as possible and respect the market price.
In addition, he urged all rice millers to participate in the effective implementation of agricultural contracts to ensure the price of rice and the stability of the rice market to farmers.
In addition to inspecting rice mills, the Director General inspected the cultivation of safe vegetables at Tasei Samaki Agricultural Community in Thmor Kol District, Battambang Province.
During the visit, he encouraged the community to continue to expand the cultivation of safe vegetables and continue to organize and expand its membership in connection with existing markets. He also continued to visit the wholesale vegetable market in Bor Vil district, Battambang province and had a conversation with the traders who are selling there.
While the grower was facing market problems, Mr. Kao Thach invited a group of representatives of the Mien Pailin community, who are clients of the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank, to listen to the problems that the association is facing and raise issues. Requests to the bank to help solve, especially on additional loan issues.
At the same time, the Director General inspected the process of setting up a beef cattle farm in Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province. The farm is currently in the process of installing a modern large-scale watering machine with a length of 600 meters and is preparing to plant grass on the cleared land.
On the first day of the vaccination campaign, 19 people in Mondulkiri province rushed to bring their children between the ages of 6 and 12 to get the vaccine.
(Mondulkiri): The first day of the campaign to vaccinate 19 children against 6 to 12 years old for Mondulkiri province, people and parents rushed to bring their children to get the vaccine that the provincial authorities have prepared. At locations organized at health centers throughout the province.
Vaccination of 19 children against 6 to 12 years of age is considered a highly responsible campaign by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to protect the lives of children from serious diseases. Fierce and the reopening of the school.
