China calls on international community to support Afghan people on path to development, counter-terrorism and humanitarian aid
(UN) - A Chinese envoy said this Friday (New York time) urging the international community to support the Afghan people on the path to their chosen development, fight terrorism and provide humanitarian assistance. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Saturday evening, September 18, 2021.
Dai Bing, China's Deputy Permanent Representative to the United Nations (UN), said the international community should stand on the basis of respect for Afghanistan's sovereignty, independence and territorial integrity in accordance with "Afghan-led" principles and Support the people of Afghanistan in choosing their own development path.
During a post-election comment by the United Nations Security Council (UNSC) to extend the mandate of the UN aid mission in Afghanistan, Dai also called on the international community to improve the overall political structure in Afghanistan. Afghanistan implements prudent domestic and foreign policies, maintains friendly relations and close ties with neighboring countries, and respects the rights of minorities, women and children.
China also reiterated the Taliban authorities' commitment to building security and stability by not allowing Afghan territory to be used to abuse or undermine the security of other countries. China hopes the Taliban-led government will abide by its commitment by severing ties with all terrorist groups and eradicating all acts of terrorism from Afghanistan.
