Commentary: China-ASEAN Dialogue Established for 30 Years to Start a New Process
BEIJING, Sept. 15 (Xinhua) - Wang Yi, a member of the State Council and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China (PRC), concluded a visit to four neighboring countries, including Vietnam, Cambodia and Singapore. Get special attention from the outside world.
This year marks the 30th anniversary of the establishment of China-ASEAN dialogue relations. Therefore, this year is a special year that summarizes past achievements and paves the way for the future. During his visit, Wang Yi brought with it the sincere intentions of the countries, which are expected to join hands with Southeast Asian countries to fight Kovid 19 and deepen practical cooperation.
As for the South China Sea issue, which is of great concern to the outside world, China has clearly expressed its willingness to cooperate with ASEAN countries to expedite discussions on the "South China Sea Code of Conduct" and hopes that during With Cambodia taking over the rotating chairmanship of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) next year, it is possible to achieve a dialogue on the "Code of Conduct for the South China Sea" with ASEAN countries.
