Samdech Techo Hun Sen, through an audio message released on September 15, pointed out that the vaccine used to vaccinate children between the ages of 6 and 12 is Sinovak, a vaccine manufactured by a Chinese company.
Samdech Techo emphasized in the message that there are about 1.8 million children between the ages of 6 and 12. According to Samdech Techo, vaccinating children between the ages of 6 and 12 is to create greater social resilience, which can lead to a wider social activity. In addition, the main goal of this vaccination is so that young children can return to school.
The Prime Minister emphasized in the message that "so that children can go to primary school can go to primary school without fear because they have been vaccinated. Otherwise, we are in the range of 6 to 12 years, which we previously required for secondary school, but we follow the steps, and the next step, we are also thinking of children in kindergarten between the ages of 3 and 6, which is considered "The next step."
In addition to this voicemail, Samdech Techo Hun Sen further confirmed on his Facebook page that the future of their lives, health and education is the most important work to be done, and the decision to vaccinate children is aimed at ensuring The right to life, the right to health care and the right to their education, etc.
In addition to launching a vaccination campaign for children between the ages of 6 and 12, the Prime Minister will also hold a press conference to present the social situation and work to fight the 19-Kovid War.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has already launched two vaccination campaigns. The first one was held on February 10 for people aged 18 and over. As of Sept. 15, 9.7 million people over the age of 18 had been vaccinated against Kovid 19, or 97.88 percent. Of those, the second dose was more than 8.7 million.
In this mission to protect the lives of people from harassment by Kovid 19 virus, the Royal Government of Cambodia has reached the Kovid 19 vaccine, the third dose, or a dose to encourage people. As of September 15, a total of nearly 800,000 front-line and priority personnel had been vaccinated with the third dose. The Royal Government plans to launch the third dose campaign for the general public during October.
Khmer Civilization Expert: How does the Techo Heritage National Stadium, designed in the shape of a "ship", reflect the traditional values of Khmer-Chinese friendship?
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, said that September 12, 2021 is a day of victory in the Kingdom of Cambodia, which has emerged as a great achievement in history, another is the Techo Yang National Stadium. Beautiful, designed in the shape of a "ship", strong, vibrant, floating on the land of Suvarnabhumi, Phnom Penh, and the most beautiful in ASEAN, with the help of China.
Because the meaning of "ship" reflects the connection between diplomacy, trade and noble relations since ancient times, because the ship is connected from one port to another or from one country to another. This means that the Techo Heritage National Stadium, which was designed in the shape of a "ship" in the Techo era, reflects the traditional values of the Khmer-Chinese friendship, connecting from the past to the present and into the future.
Mr. Rath Sandab continued that in this sense, the Moradok Techo National Stadium, which is designed in the shape of a "ship", reflects the values of the Khmer people of all generations, so that "ship" is a means of transportation. Connect diplomatic relations, prosperity ahead of business smoothly, which leads to greater success. Because in ancient times, ships were replaced by ships today for traveling or doing business from one country to another.
If you look at the journey on the surface of the water or on the surface of the sea, the ship itself has overcome all obstacles, storms, rain, thunder, sea waves are protecting our lives and lead us to the destination we want to go for freedom and independence. For example, in the Chinese shrine, each of the householders in each house, restaurant, hotel, or company, there is always a display or offering of gold, silver, or diamonds in the shape of a ship.
Mr. Rath Sandab stated that in terms of the traditional background of the Khmer-Chinese friendly relations, there have been diplomatic relations with each other for a long time, since the time of the Phnom Kingdom, while in the past, the two countries also had borders. Through this relationship, the landscape and the presence of the Chinese in the Khmer Empire in some of the sculptures of the Khmer temples are evident.
Among them, the Bayon temple sculpture tells us about the Chinese in two different aspects: the first aspect is the Chinese army in Jayavarman VII's military convoy, showing the diplomatic relations and the second aspect is the Chinese. Usually a community businessman among the Khmer people living in Angkor in the 12th-13th centuries.
