Comment: China has the ability to continue to contribute its strength to the global economic recovery
Due to a number of factors, such as macro policy interests continue to grow and the business environment needs to be continuously improved, the innovation role of the Chinese market is growing rapidly. Technological innovations seem to be the "ignition engine" that works relentlessly to drive the continuous development of China's economy.
At the same time, domestic demand remains strong support for China's economy. Although partly affected by Kovid 19 and floods, the growth of Chinese consumption in August slowed, but the employment situation, which is supportive of consumption, remained generally stable. This trend to promote China's consumption class has not diminished.
On the other hand, while improving the economic efficiency of enterprises, China's real economic unit development support policy continues to be effective, and the vitality of investment continues to grow. The domestic demand of the large-scale Chinese market has great potential, which is the basis for the Chinese economy to recover and grow to a continuous high-quality development.
In the context of the continued spread of Kovid 19, China's sharp opening-up has boosted the global economy. China's total foreign trade volume in August set a new record for the same period in history, whether import or export growth far exceeded market estimates. As China's international openness continues to expand, China will continue to become a popular destination for foreign investors.
The United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) in Afghanistan announced on Thursday that more than 634,000 Afghans will be displaced by the conflict in 2021. This. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday evening, September 16, 2021.
A total of 634,800 Afghans have been displaced by the conflict as of September 12, 2021, of which 282,246 have already received necessary assistance. Meanwhile, according to figures provided by the OCHA, more than 28,000 Afghans will be affected by natural disasters across the country in 2021.
On this issue, Afghan officials and humanitarian agencies have expressed grave concern over the living conditions of displaced families in the country since the Taliban came to power in mid-August. To the lives of many women and children because they do not have access to health centers and schools.
