(Phnom Penh): Mango, Kirirom and Mango farming communities in Cambodia are urging Cambodian mango farmers to return to their supply of mangoes to meet domestic demand, as mangoes are more expensive than large mangoes and are in high demand. Spicy shops in Cambodia are about 90% imported.
Ms. Chhin Chamroeun, Executive Director of Svay Keo Romiet Kirirom Agricultural Community, told Fresh News on September 16 that according to the research of Svay Keo Romiet Kirirom Agricultural Community in the past, Cambodia consumes about 10 tons of mango pods per day. Imported for sale in Cambodia costs between 2,000 riel and 5,000 riel per kilogram. Thailand is the largest importer of mangoes to Cambodia.
She said that it takes only 35 days to get a sale, which saves growers time, capital in production, and can be done several times a year without worrying about the risk of falling prices. Like big mangoes. It takes more than two and a half months to store the fruit in large quantities and has to deal with erratic prices.
She added that mango growers should pick out a handful of mangoes for sale, keeping only a small quantity per stalk for packaging so that the mangoes are large, good quality and expensive.
It should be noted that Cambodia has 131,890 hectares of mango plantations, of which more than 90,000 hectares have been collected. In the first eight months of 2021, Cambodia exported 163,828.55 tons of fresh mangoes, an increase of 251.03%, exporting to Thailand, China, Hong Kong, Korea, Singapore and Kuwait. Kambol District Land Office made public the results of the plot of land for the people in Phum Phea, Sangkat Preah Lang to come and inspect
