The following is the full text of the instructions of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration: The Cambodian Red Cross attends the 18th National Meeting of the Red Cross Red Crescent Society of Southeast Asia on video
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Red Cross on the afternoon of September 16, 2021 participated in the 18th National Meeting of the Red Cross Society of Southeast Asia, which took place on September 16-17, 2021. Video hosted by the Thai National Red Cross.
The Cambodian Red Cross was also joined by Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General, Mr. Yulana, Second Deputy Secretary General and many other Cambodian Red Cross officials.
According to Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, the meeting focused on:
1. The challenge of the global epidemic of Kovid-19, which is infected and dies every day due to the protracted Kovid-19 crisis, armed conflict, natural disasters and man-made disasters.
2: Continuing to strengthen the national and international solidarity of the National Red Cross, Red Crescent Society, Southeast Asia to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease and save human life.
3. Promoting its values of strengthening community resilience and mobilizing volunteers and youth in the Kovid-19 response campaign to address key global issues such as climate change, technology and climate change. Strive to raise funds for the sustainability of the National Association as well as for humanitarian cooperation.
4: Considering the capacity building of each association as well as the Red Cross Red Crescent Movement in the restoration of the status of Kovid-19 to date, we can not conclude when it will end. Not yet.
