Police officer who shot and killed a barber in Tuol Kork district was sentenced in absentia to 13 years in prison and ordered to pay the victim $ 150,000, but the perpetrator has not yet been arrested.
(Phnom Penh): A police officer who shot and killed a barber in Phnom Penh's Toul Kork district in September 2020 has been sentenced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to 13 years in prison and fined. $ 150,000. This is according to the court's verdict announced in early August 2021. However, the perpetrators have not been arrested yet.
According to the spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Mr. San Sok Seiha confirmed that the authorities continue to investigate this case without giving up. "Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, has ordered the police force to search and arrest the perpetrators, not to release them," he said.
The assailant was named Ly Thary, 30 years old and a former Daun Penh district police officer. Later, because of misconduct, he was taken to the Phnom Penh Police Station. The victim, Sok Soken, was over 30 years old and had a haircut.
It should be noted that at more than 10 pm on September 26, 2020, a man, a hairdresser, was shot by a neighbor, causing his sudden death in front of his house next to Tuol Kork School in Boeung Kak Ty commune. 2 Khan Toul Kork.
The victim's wife said that after a fight, the assailant pulled out a gun and fired at her husband, killing him in a pool of blood. After the shooting, the assailant escaped.
The victims' deaths left four young daughters orphaned for their lives. The first daughter is 11 years old, the second daughter is 9 years old, the third daughter is 5 years old, the fourth daughter is 1 year old.
