Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Continues to Suspend the Sale of All Kinds of Alcohol for an Additional 14 Days to Prevent Kovid 19
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, issued an instruction on the continuation of the sale of all kinds of alcohol for another 14 days from September 17 to September 30, 2021 in the province. .
According to the announcement received by Fresh News on September 16, 2021, due to the situation of the outbreak of Kovid 19 in the "February 20 community event" in Sihanoukville has not yet Completely prevented and the next outbreak to ensure the protection of the lives of the people, public health, as well as social order, the provincial administration recommends the following:
* Continue to suspend the sale of all kinds of alcohol in Sihanoukville from September 17 to September 30, 2021
* All public markets, private markets and marts, as well as alcohol distribution depots in Sihanoukville must continue to suspend the sale and distribution of all types of alcohol.
* All restaurants, cafeterias, food stalls, cafes, beverage outlets, food and beverage businesses and vendors of all kinds of alcohol distributors shall continue to temporarily suspend all alcohol service to guests for an additional 14 days.
In addition, the provincial administration stated that in the case of citizens, market managers, company managers or distributors, shop owners, stall owners, as well as: business owners involved in the sale of alcohol as described above, do not follow this instruction. Administrative measures and legal measures without exception.
The following is a statement from the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration: The government of Rodrigo Duterte has announced that it will not cooperate with the ICC in investigating the war on drugs in the Philippines.
MANILA: The Philippine government will not cooperate with the International Criminal Court (ICC) over its investigation into allegations of crimes against humanity committed in President Rodrigo Duterte's war on drugs. This was released by Reuters in the morning of Thursday, September 16, 2021.
The announcement by Salvador Panelo, a spokesman for the Philippine presidential palace, came after a judge at the International Criminal Court (ICC) on Wednesday approved a formal investigation into the allegations. Crimes against humanity committed in Rodrigo Duterte's war on drugs.
The approval of the ICC probe comes as Duterte, now 76, will end his presidency in June 2022, but is scheduled to run for vice president. Will be able to help maintain his power in the Philippines.
