General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Staff of the Ministry of National Defense's Vaccination Task Force, said the army's vaccination task was almost complete and little was left. According to General Ith Sarath, the remaining amount will be handed over to the provincial authorities for further management.
To complete the vaccination campaign, more than 3,000 military personnel from various units across the country worked tirelessly.
Vaccination against Kovid 19 is not an easy task and requires a great deal of patience and commitment on the part of the team. During the Kovid 19 vaccination campaign, doctors were exposed to Kovid 19 infection, wearing Kovid 19 vaccine and wearing a mask, which caused the team to sweat and sweat every day.
Their mission is also unknown Saturday, Sunday or holidays. Despite the concerns of Kovid 19 infection and the above-mentioned difficulties, the vaccination team worked diligently to ensure that people were vaccinated against Kovid 19.
