(Phnom Penh): Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, stated that in order to achieve a successful re-opening of tourists, it is necessary to rely on psychological factors and the tendency of tourists to decide on tourist destinations and activities. Excursions and the preparation of the tourism business along the new normal trajectory.
Dr. Thong Khon stated this this morning, September 15, 2021, in the meeting to review the internal tourism work for the first 9 months of 2021 and the direction of implementation, which was made by video at the Ministry of Tourism. With the participation of the Capital-Provincial Administration and the 25 Capital-Provincial Tourism Departments, the private sector and stakeholders.
Dr. Thong Khon said, "In order to achieve a successful reopening, we need to rely on two main determinants: external factors: the psychological factors and the tendency of the main decision of the guests. Tourists in choosing tourist destinations and excursions, that is, giving high value to cleanliness, hygiene and safety.
Internal factors: Refers to the readiness of the tourism business along the new normal path in all production lines of the tourism sector, with the key priority is to think from the beginning to the end of the line, including infrastructure, transportation, fitness, tourism, human resources in tourism. "Implementing tourism safety rules and implementation of standard operating guidelines (SOPs) to diversify tourism products in line with the new context of demand and supply."
