(Phnom Penh): Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vintian highlighted that Cambodian and Chinese stakeholders are negotiating on Cambodia's longan exports to the Chinese market.
This information was highlighted in an article on helping buy lentils in Battambang by the Chinese Embassy and the Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia.
The article expressed the expectation that Cambodian longan would be the third fresh fruit to be licensed for export to China, after bananas and mangoes.
It should be noted that in a working meeting with Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of China on September 12, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, requested the Chinese government to help open the market for longan. Cambodia.
In response to this request, Minister Wang Yi warmly welcomed and promised to speed up the relevant work so that Cambodian longan can enter the Chinese market. The Minister expressed the hope that opening the market for Cambodian longan will help Cambodian farmers to have a better life and not face a lack of market.
