(Siem Reap): Kan Ben, Pchum Ben and Kathina festivals are one of the largest and most important traditional Buddhist ceremonies for Buddhists, and are celebrated annually at the end of September.
In the context of the ongoing 19 Kovid disease, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration has instructed all departments, units, municipalities and districts to disseminate the content of the above festival widely and encourage the convenience of civil servants under the auspices of Buddhists to participate. Perform traditional rituals at pagodas or in their units and meet parents, siblings, grandparents as desired.
The provincial administration also recommends decorating national flags, banners, banners, slogans and lighting colored lights in parks, public places and people's homes.
In particular, the Department of Information must instruct national and private national and private radio and television stations in the province for reporters to follow and research the history of the activities of the traditional festival and the dress code, as well as the polite attitude to be observed during the festival. Especially in the pagoda as well as widely disseminated during the two festivals.
The letter also stated that the Department of Cults and Religions must take care to create better conditions for the monks to participate in the Kan Ben, Pchum Ben and Kathina ceremonies in the Buddhist tradition and national tradition with generosity in time. Set. All monasteries must strictly implement the "3 do not 3 protection" measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the community.
