Minister of Commerce defends three important draft laws with the 9th Senate Commission
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, on Tuesday, September 14, led a delegation to defend three important draft laws related to foreign trade with the Ninth Committee of the Senate.
The draft law, which was reviewed by the Ninth Committee of the Senate and defended by the Minister, includes: Draft Law on the Approval of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (APEC), Draft Law on Approval Agree on a free trade agreement between Cambodia and China and a draft law on competition.
The meeting to review the three draft laws was televised, chaired by Kong Sarach, a member of the Standing Committee and chairman of the Ninth Committee of the Senate.
Mr. Pan Sosak informed the meeting about the main points and benefits that Cambodia will receive when these agreements and laws come into force. The Minister also answered questions from the Senate Commission.
The Minister of Commerce briefed the meeting on the Ministry of Commerce's efforts to develop trade laws and regulations aimed at improving the business environment as well as market diversification and finding additional markets through negotiation agreements. Bilateral and multilateral free trade with key trading partners to promote exports in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's fourth phase of the Rectangular Policy.
As a result, after much deliberation, the Ninth Committee of the Senate fully approved to submit the draft law to the upcoming plenary session of the Senate for approval.
