Hun Many Inaugurates Center for Cambodian Development's "Discovering the Fourth Industrial Revolution"
(Phnom Penh): The Center for the Development of Cambodia organized the launch of the book "Understanding the Fourth Industrial Revolution" which took place on the morning of September 14, 2021 through the Zoom Forum under the chairmanship of Mr. HUN Many, Chairman of the Education, Youth, Sports, Cult and Affairs Committee. Religion, Culture and Tourism of the National Assembly and Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Center 4.0.
Under the theme "Achieving the Complete Vision of Cambodia 4.0, Starting from Raising People's Awareness", the book launch program was organized with the aim of providing a forum for knowledge sharing and discussion on the book "Understanding the Industrial Revolution". Fourth, ”published by the Cambodian Development Center.
In a keynote address on the program, Mr. HUN Many stated that raising people's awareness is an important foundation for achieving an environmentally and sustainable Cambodian society in the context of the revolution. Industry 4.
He said that a large number of developed countries have succeeded in promoting the digital revolution by building their foundations by reforming education systems in line with the context of digitalization, focusing on science, technology, engineering and mathematics. STEM). The development of human resources along the path of technology and innovation with clarity is an important factor in achieving the development of a society that is innovative and innovative.
In his keynote address, Mr. Hun Many made some recommendations for the effective and fruitful use of the technologies of the Fourth Industrial Revolution of the Cambodian people, including:
* First: Absorption and Adaptation: Inspire all citizens who are socio-economic cells and indispensable actors to absorb and adapt to new technologies as well as to cultivate Innovation, talent, innovation through continuous monitoring of new developments and trends in technology at the Cambodian, regional and global levels.
* Second: Responsibility: Inspire the youth to be the driving force in disseminating and integrating the understanding of the 4.0 era by sharing it with family, friends and the community. At the same time, young people must be careful by using technology to target and use for the benefit of themselves as well as society and not affect the public interest.
Encourage the use of responsible technology that contributes to the development of the national economy, increases efficiency in the workplace, helps study, helps solve social problems and so on.
* Third: Digital security and security management: We need to think about security in the use of technology, especially the fight against crime or cybercrime. Good cyber security and safety management is strategically important for national security, as well as contributing to increasing the trust and confidence of digital users.
In addition, the launching ceremony of the book "Understanding the Fourth Industrial Revolution" also included a welcome speech by Mr. Dao Ansan, Executive Director of the Cambodian Development Center and a speech of thanks by Mr. Soeng Reth, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Member of the Supreme National Economic Council and a representative of the Board of the Center for the Development of Cambodia.
