Court Detains Foreigner, Two Cambodian Women After Fraud and Money Laundering
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tith Sothy Borachat, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on September 14, 2021, remanded in custody three suspects, including a 38-year-old Nigerian man and a Cambodian woman. Two for "fraud and money laundering."
According to Colonel San Sok Seiha, Spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, confirmed to Fresh News on the night of September 14, 2021 that the decision to issue a temporary detention order of the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Two Nigerian men and a Cambodian woman were arrested by the Anti-Technology Bureau of the Security Action Plan.
Colonel San Sok Seiha said that the perpetrator contacted the victim's wife via WhatsApp in early 2020, asking the victim's wife to send money from Canada to a bank account in Cambodia subsequently reported that the victim, CHEN STEVEN, was arrested and detained by the Cambodian immigration police for overstaying his visa and had to be sent money to them for mediation.
According to the confession of the perpetrator's wife, she actually received money from abroad by transferring money into her bank account several times without a clear source. Overseas, $ 237,142 to ABA Bank, $ 1,600 to ABA Bank Transfer and $ 9,866 transfer from Wing Ver Account to each other.
The spokesman confirmed that the authorities then continued to detain the Nigerian man and his wife after conducting interrogation, and all the suspects admitted that they had indeed received money and transferred money abroad. Without clear source, the total amount transferred from the bank was $ 73,141.
Colonel San Sok Seiha, on behalf of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, would like to call on all citizens to be very careful and to consider all aspects, do not quickly believe the persuasion of others, especially people we do not know a clear history.
