Princess Norodom Mary Visits "Samdech Mey Library"
(Phnom Penh): Princess Norodom Marie, President of the Women's Foundation, Samdech Raksmey Sophoan, led an honorary delegation, including Princess Norodom Ratana Devi, Prince Norodom Siharith, Prince Sisowath Teso and Pok Bopha Yeang. Samdech Mey Library ”of the Documentation Center of Cambodia in the morning of Tuesday, September 14, 2021.
Princess Norodom Mary, President of the Women's Foundation, Samdech Raksmey Sophoan, was born in Phnom Penh on December 21, 1948 and studied in Cambodia and France. In 1985, the Princess established the Cambodian Women's Association, first located in a refugee camp along the Cambodian-Thai border operated by FUNCINPEC.
After the Paris Peace Treaty, the Cambodian Women's Association changed its name to the Samdech Raksmey Sophoan Women's Foundation, after Princess Norodom Raksmey Sophoan, the younger brother of King Norodom Suramarit. The Foundation is headquartered in Phnom Penh and is recognized as an NGO that assists Cambodian women in the areas of education, health and training.
The Samdech Raksmey Sophoan Women's Foundation was established as a leading organization in promoting the renewal of Khmer silk, which has played an important role in the nation's artistic survival, rehabilitation and economy.
At the end of the ceremony, the Honorary Delegates expressed their gratitude for the cordial welcome of the leaders of the Documentation Center of Cambodia. Princess Norodom Mary would like to donate a collection of historically valuable documents to be kept at the "Samdech Mey Library" to serve research and education for the next generation of Cambodia. Khmer Breweries sponsors 69 seats to Banteay Meanchey
