International Analysis: "American hegemony is the source of the world war"
In fact, this trial will be a window for the world to understand the origins of the US-inspired war and the American-style hegemony, as well as the failure of the plan to "transfer its democracy to other countries."
As a country with a history of just over 240 years, the wars that the United States has instigated and participated in more than 200 times. Just after the end of World War II from 1945 to 2001, of the 248 armed clashes in 153 regions of the world, the United States instigated 201 incidents, accounting for 81 percent of the total. Undoubtedly, the United States is the most war-addicted country in the world.
In addition, US war addiction is also economically viable. In 2019, Philippine President Duterte said in a speech that the United States hopes for a lasting war because the war will force other countries to buy planes, warships and ammunition from the United States once the war is over. Many will lose their jobs. It is safe to say that Duterte was right.
At the same time, the United States has tried to reform other countries through its will to force the transfer of its democracy to other countries, but without exception, all have failed and caused great suffering to the people of the region. .
