General knowledge: Light travels at how many kilometers per second?
(Phnom Penh): Light travels so fast that we can not see it with the naked eye, but scientists have used various instruments to measure its speed, they found that it has a speed of up to 300 , 000 kilometers per second and the slowest is only 61 kilometers per hour.
Recently, scientists have recorded new discoveries that when light travels through sodium at a temperature of -272 degrees Celsius, it can travel at a speed of only 61 kilometers per hour. Thus, we can assess whether light travels fast or slow depending on the object it passes through.
