(Kampong Thom): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, assigned the President of the Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association, Major General Som Sun, together with local authorities this morning. On September 13, 2021, a new house was handed over to the family of a veteran who was engulfed in fire in Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province.
The newly built house, handed over to the families of the victims, is now the back of the 198th house, which is 4 meters by 6 meters, built high above the ground, concrete pillars, steel bones, floorboards, corrugated iron roofs and corrugated stairs. Built by the working group of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association, Kampong Thom Province.
After the fire engulfed the house, Mr. San Sim took refuge with his neighbor's house and was homeless and unable to rebuild his house. Today, he received a new house, a precious gift from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen through Senior Minister General Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
The family of 69-year-old San Sim, a martyr, has six dependent children who were affected by the fire. Recently, in Trapeang Chambok village, Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province.
On that occasion, Major General Som Sun also brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who both always thought about the well-being and living conditions of the veterans in Anywhere and anytime.
It should be noted that because the veterans have contributed greatly with Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the implementation of the win-win policy that has brought complete peace as today, without all the sacrifices of our veterans for our nation and motherland. No, we do not have everything today.
During the handover ceremony, Lt. Gen. Som Sun brought the gifts of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Pich Chanmony to give him an additional 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 1 can of fish sauce, 2 portable water bottles and some budget.
Local authorities, people and families of victims in Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province are excited to find something that can help solve their difficulties now and would like to express our deep gratitude. Finally, to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Mr. Hun Manet and Mrs. and the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province, please meet only the five blessings of the Buddha, do not starve.
