Cambodian-Chinese Volunteers Continue to Donate $ 1,688 to a Chinese Family in Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): After seeing a group of Cambodian-Chinese volunteers post information on Wechat about the financial support to the families of 19 victims of Kovid in Svay Rieng province, a Chinese man sympathetically through the group Cambodian-Chinese volunteers donated $ 1,688 to the families of the victims to alleviate their suffering.
Mao Sienghor, a 68-year-old woman living with her daughter Seng Chanthou in Boeung Ray Cheung village, Kraol Kor commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province, died on August 11, 2021.
$ 1,688 was handed over to his daughter, Seng Chanthou. Ms. Seng Chanthou, the son, described that her family consisted of six members, including her, her husband, mother (died by Kovid 19) and three children.
She said her husband helped build the house for her daily needs, and that her one-and-a-half-year-old youngest son died of asphyxiation and was rushed to hospital. Soon after, her mother fell ill and she borrowed money to pay for his treatment. She later learned that her mother, 19-year-old Kovid, had died one day after 19 Kovids.
Ms. Chanthou continued, "I have been suffering again and again. Now my family has been out of Chattalysak for a week, but I have not been able to find a job yet, and I have to spend my daily life. "There is another serious financial crisis."
Representatives of the Cambodian-Chinese volunteer group claim that the Chinese help comes from their association, which regularly conducts humanitarian activities, donating $ 150 per family to 19 family members who have died of Kovid.
Excited and sympathetic to the victims, a Chinese man donated $ 1,688 to the family in order to alleviate the burden and provide a small amount of capital to continue the small business for the needy family.
This activity shows the kindness of the Chinese people to the people of Cambodia, and also to promote the relationship between Cambodia and China, strengthen the relationship between the two peoples.
