Western nations support Libya's presidential election scheduled for late 2021
The embassies of France, Germany, Italy, Britain and the United States have joined forces to urge all parties in Libya to secure parliamentary and presidential elections scheduled for May 24. The coming December 2021 is going smoothly. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday afternoon, September 13, 2021.
A joint statement from the Western embassies in Libya said: "All political parties (in Libya) should recognize that now is the time for trade. "Connect with each other and complete mechanisms in the run-up to the election in response to the concerns of all Libyans."
The statement from the West was a reaffirmation of the United Nations (UN)-sponsored Libya Political Dialogue Forum held in November 2020 and the declaration of Resolution 2570 of the United Nations Security Council (UNSC). These are key steps that the international community has pioneered for the reunification of Libya, and these results should be respected by all parties.
