Kampong Chhnang Provincial Authority Launches Campaign to vaccinate cattle against foot-and-mouth disease in Prey Moul commune, Rolea Bier district
(Kampong Chhnang): Veterinary officers of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture this morning, September 13, 2021, launched a campaign to vaccinate cattle against foot-and-mouth disease and foot-and-mouth disease in Trapeang Ta Sok village, commune. Prey Moul, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
The opening ceremony of the vaccination campaign for cattle was led by Mrs. Born Sophy, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, Director of Agriculture and Mr. Kreung Sam Ath, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Veterinary Office, along with officials of the Provincial Department of Agriculture and many people. .
During the ceremony, Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, reported that in Kampong Chhnang, there were a total of more than 200,000 head of cattle, of which about 4,000 were sick and 33 died. More than 2,000 have been cured and more than 2,000 are being treated. Separately, today, 200 head of cattle were vaccinated in Trapeang Ta Sok village.
On that occasion, Ms. Born Sophy, Deputy Governor, called on all farmers to bring cattle to be vaccinated in this campaign in a timely manner and to take care of cattle disease as instructed by experts. And if a cow dies, do not eat the meat of the sick animal, which can lead to the spread of other diseases to humans and animals locally.
In addition, the Deputy Governor also instructed the people to join together to prevent and prevent Kovid 19 disease is to implement the "3 do not and 3 prevent" measures.
During the ceremony, officials also distributed medicine and equipment for the treatment of cattle to district veterinary officers, commune veterinarians and village veterinarians. After that, the professional officers also sprayed pesticides on the cattle barns of the people in Trapeang Ta Sok village.
