Laws and regulations have been enacted in the past, including:
* Gambling suppression law * Decisions and directives of the Royal Government, inter-ministerial prakas and charge books, etc. * Seeing the gaps as well as to fill the components in the legal framework to be complete and valid to Ensure the management and promotion of the Integrated Business Gambling and Trade Gaming Sector to operate more transparently and effectively by taking refuge under the roof of the full range of laws and regulations in force.
The Secretary-General further said that the Law on the Management of Commercial Gambling was drafted and approved on October 5, 2020 at the 5th Session of the National Assembly, the 6th Legislature and the Senate. This law was fully adopted on October 26, 2020 at the 6th Plenary Session of the 4th Legislature and was promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1120/031 dated 14 November 2020 .
The law allows for more efficient management of casinos and other commercial games by setting minimum investment amounts for the casino business, determining which areas should or may not allow commercial gambling, and capacity building. Institutions and equipments of appropriate technology to regularly monitor the operations of commercial gaming operators.
In conjunction with the above law, paved the way for the preparation of a sub-decree on setting the minimum capital for casino gambling operations and came into force on 26 August 2021 to determine the minimum capital for casino gambling operations in the Kingdom. Cambodia.
