According to the official Facebook page on September 13, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said: Today, I would like to inform my compatriots about the results of the operation to crack down on drug crimes in August 2021, which is in During this month, our authorities cracked down on a total of 440 drug crimes, an increase of 111 cases, equivalent to 33.7 percent compared to July 2021.
The cases that were suppressed include: 355 cases of storage, trafficking and storage, 84 cases of use and 1 case of synthesis.
Last August, police arrested 861 suspects. The number of suspects involved in these drug offenses increased by 12 from 1.4% in July 2021. Among the suspects were 650 suspects in trafficking and storage cases, 210 suspects in drug use cases and one suspect in synthetic processing. Twenty-one foreigners were among the suspects.
Although the number of drug cases and the number of suspects arrested and detained by the police increased compared to July, during the August operation, the number of drugs seized by the police decreased by 161 kilograms and 548.17 grams decreased. 73.6 percent, that is, our authorities seized a total of 57 kilograms of drugs and 912.54 grams, compared to July, which seized nearly 220 kilograms of drugs. "The increase in July is due to our authorities cracking down on big cases."
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and on behalf of the Ministry of Interior, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, I would like to once again send my sincere appreciation and encouragement to all relevant leaders and officials, including civilians, police and police. The Armed Forces, which has worked hard to cooperate well in the operation to crack down on drug crimes to contribute to the protection of security, public order and social security for our nation and people.
On this occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng would also like to send a message to all compatriots from all walks of life and all law enforcement forces to support and implement the three national slogans, 1 defense, report as follows:
First, do not get involved: do not trade, do not distribute, do not be a backbone, do not conspire and do not use drugs. Second, do not intervene: Do not obstruct the law enforcement of drug offenders, even family, relatives or friends. Third: Do not exempt: Do not relax the law enforcement of drug offenders. All relevant authorities must enforce the law strictly and honestly in their profession, and everyone must respect and enforce the law.
One report: To report to the authorities on the subject of trafficking, distribution, use, processing and illegal drug storage sites to the authorities so that we can continue to join forces with the National Solidarity Against Drugs, which is the enemy of socio-economic development and human resources. Especially youth resources, which are the pillars of the nation.
