WASHINGTON (Reuters) - North Korea's missile test over the weekend was a threat to neighboring countries and the international community as a whole, the US military said. This was released by Reuters on Monday morning, September 13, 2021.
In a statement issued on Sunday, September 12 (Washington time), the US Indo-Pacific Regional Military Command stated, "This action clearly shows that North Korea continues to focus on program development. "The military will pose a threat to its neighbors and the entire international community."
