Taliban to allow women to study at university, but to study separately from men
Kabul: The new Taliban education minister has said that all Afghan women will be allowed to go to university, but their classes cannot be mixed. From men. This was released by Reuters on Monday, September 13, 2021.
In early August, the Taliban government announced that women would still be allowed to continue their studies up to university if they wore proper body clothing, such as niqab. Which is a kind of clothing that covers almost all women's bodies, leaving only the space between the eyes, and is divided into classrooms between men and women, or separated by a curtain in the same classroom.
The Taliban has also promised to allow Afghan women to work under Islamic law, but they have not yet clarified the details.
