Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed to the media that the vaccine for the third dose has reached 2 million doses and will reach another 3 million doses, a total of 5 million doses, plus the help of this new Chinese friend. Another 3 million doses and the previous injection of nearly 1 million doses, we will have 9 million doses. If we need another 12 million doses, we only need another 3 million doses.
With substantial assistance to Cambodia's development, China has become a major supplier of vaccines to Cambodia. To date, Cambodia has received 26.8 million doses of Kovid-19 vaccine from the Government of the People's Republic of China and the Chinese population. This is the confirmation of Mr. Prak Sokhon.
The presence of aid, including vaccines against Kovid 19, Chinese equipment and budget to the Cambodian government clearly demonstrates the spirit of steel friendship between China and Cambodia, a spirit of mutual support in the face of adversity. In particular, it shows the strong Chinese spirit of participation in helping to fight Kovid 19 in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this announcement on the occasion of Samdech and Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, presiding over the official handover ceremony of the Techo Heritage National Stadium in This afternoon, September 12, 2021.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia announced: "And we continue to welcome all foreign friends who have donated to help us, I do not reject, I thank all the countries that have provided vaccines to Cambodia in the past. "Through Kovak, bilaterally."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also confirmed that this evening, Samdech will meet with Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, because Cambodia needs 19 Kovid vaccine for the third dose at present. This Cambodia has been in the process of injecting civil servants, the armed forces and so on.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in the next 10 months will launch a campaign to vaccinate against measles 19 doses 3 to maintain immunity in the community to reopen schools to reopen the economy and we need to learn And lived with Kovid 19 for many more years, requiring a new way of life, because Kovid 19 destroyed traditions and changed existing attitudes.
So far, Cambodia has received 26.8 million doses of Kovid-19 vaccine from the Government of the People's Republic of China and the Chinese population.
At the same time, Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi added that in the future, the Chinese government will provide an additional 3 million doses of Kovid-19 vaccine to the Royal Government of Cambodia.
It should be informed that as of the night of September 11, 2021, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of National Defense have vaccinated 11,429,835 Kovid-19 vaccines to civil servants, citizens and the armed forces throughout the country. .
