(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie sent a suspect to court on the afternoon of September 10, 2021 to be punished according to the law related to domestic violence and intentional detention. The villain aims to extort money from his wife, illegally possesses a weapon and rapes his stepdaughter, threatening to kill her.
In addition, this suspect is also a person who is famous for many endless cases in the past, both in the provinces and the capital.
Suddenly, when the wife went to court, she found out that her husband was filing for divorce, not a criminal case to be arrested and imprisoned as her husband had threatened, so the wife refused to accept the agreement to divide the property and pay the suspect. Afterwards, the suspect, who was the husband, called his wife and threatened her with a gun on the table, threatening that if the agreement was not taken to court, beware of orphans without mothers.
However, since they were living together without civil status, the court dismissed the plaintiff's request to stop living as a minor, but to implement the agreement that the husband forced his wife to do before going to court.
On September 7, 2021, the police received a request for intervention from the plaintiff, adding that his two children were detained by the suspect in the house, asking the police to help release his child.
Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie Officers conducted a search operation at 49, Trapeang Chhouk Village, Sangkat O Bek Kam, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. The suspect (one of them was a minor) was right and the suspect escaped when he saw the police. Authorities and village authorities intervened by locking the house to free the two children.
