WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The FBI on Saturday released documents related to its investigation into the September 11, 2001 terrorist attacks and allegations that the Saudi government provided support to the terrorists. Hijack the plane. This was released by Reuters on Sunday, September 12, 2021.
Of the 19 hijackers, 15 were from Saudi Arabia. However, US authorities have so far found no evidence that the Saudi government was directly supporting al Qaeda, which was then given refuge in Afghanistan by the Taliban. But it leaves suspicions that a Saudi official may have done so.
Relatives of the victims of the "September 11" terrorist attacks, as well as businesses and insurance companies in the United States, are suing Saudi Arabia for billions of dollars in damages.
