(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has stated that other countries can not play a substitute role in building peace, and only "national ownership" is the key to success and complete peace. By sustainability. This was stated by Samdech Techo during his participation in the 7th General Assembly of Hope under the theme of Peace in the Asia-Pacific Region this morning, September 12, 2021.
Samdech added that obviously Cambodia is an example that should be considered for experience. The complete peace that we have now is being built with the participation of all stakeholders in the country. He added that in the early 1990s, Cambodia could not achieve complete peace, despite the international community spending about $ 2 billion.
