The United States has 750 military bases around the world.
US military presence in the Middle East
The US military presence in the Middle East was enhanced by the invasion of the Taliban and al Qaeda in Afghanistan in 2001 and the war in Iraq in 2003, when former President George W. Bush blamed Iraq for Saddam Hussein. There are nuclear weapons. There were 170,000 US troops stationed in Iraq in 2007 and now number 2,500.
