* US military deployment since 1950
For more than 70 years, US troops have been deployed to more than 200 countries and territories, and their deployment has steadily increased since World War II:
1955-1975: After the Korean War, tensions between the United States and the Soviet Union escalate, and ideological rivalries between the two powers spread to Southeast Asia in the 1950s and 1960s, first emerging from Vietnam War until it penetrated into Khmer and Lao territory as well. A total of 3.4 million US troops have been deployed to Southeast Asia, and more than 3 million people, including 58,000 US troops, have been killed.
On March 29, 1973, the last US troops left Vietnam, and two years later, on April 30, 1975, South Vietnam completely fell into North Vietnam, ending the Vietnam War. But the victory of the communist bloc in Indochina caused a brutal tragedy, such as the emergence of the Khmer Rouge regime in Cambodia.
