(Pursat): All public and private educational institutions at the secondary and high school levels in Pursat province will be re-opened for students to re-enroll from September 15, 2021.
During the reopening of schools, all educational institutions must implement the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Samdech Techo's "3 Do Not 3 Protective" measures, as well as the Ministry of Health's health measures.
This is according to some working meetings to prepare for the re-opening of students, led by Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Commission for Combating Kovid 19 on September 11, 2021. At the forum in the provincial hall after the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the instructions of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
