The following is the announcement of the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration: Today is the "20th anniversary" of the "September 11, 2001" terrorist events in the United States.
WASHINGTON, Sept. 11 (Xinhua) - Today marks the 20th anniversary of the September 11, 2001, terrorist attacks by al-Qaeda in the United States. The terrorist attack is considered one of the most significant and bitter turning points in the history of the United States and the world, killing 2,996 people and injuring more than 6,000 others.
Here are the details of this incident:
After the incident, in 2004, the terrorist leader revealed that he had recalled the idea of an attack on a twin tower in the United States after witnessing a bombing on a skyscraper. One during the war in Lebanon in 1982.
Some of the key individuals were recruited as team leaders for the hijacking activities, and some were only appointed as assistants due to their lack of English proficiency, which made it difficult to train pilots.
Hani Hanjour already has a pilot's license and has taught other terrorists how to live, order food and dress Westernly. After the recruitment, the hijackers went to a training course to become more proficient pilots and traveled to the United States, some of them using illegal passports.
He also called on the FBI and the State Department to warn embassies, police stations and the Department of Defense after discovering that al-Qaeda terrorists had entered the United States and, strangely, they were Attend a pilot school. More importantly, they can know even the details of each terrorist. Unfortunately, the United States still could not prevent this tragedy in time.
Attack: On the morning of September 11, 2001, 19 terrorists began hijacking a large passenger plane with long-range destinations due to its high fuel content. More devastation than usual. The four aircraft include:
The North Twin Towers collapsed at 9:59 a.m. after a 56-minute fire due to massive flames caused by the plane's fuel explosion. The southern twin towers collapsed at 10:28 a.m. after a 102-minute fire.
According to the investigation, the thieves had bought some tools and knives that were not banned from air travel at the time. Some passengers and crew said the robbers were armed with a bomb, but some said the bomb was fake.
The FBI did not find any explosives at the crash site. Therefore, it was concluded that the bomb was indeed a fake. All media outlets across the United States and around the world reported the incident immediately after the first attack.
Factors that led to the attack: The motive for al-Qaeda leader bin Laden's plot to assassinate the United States has been linked to a number of factors, investigators said in a statement. Signed by himself. Those factors include:
1: The United States supports Israel, a Muslim adversary
2: United States supports anti-Muslim attacks in Somalia
3: US government expresses anti-Muslim stance
US support India for persecution of Muslims in Kashmir
5: US military presence in Saudi Arabia
6: Sanctions on Iraq
According to an analysis, without the US military presence in Saudi Arabia, the homeland of Osama bin Laden, he would not have been able to persuade people to carry out such a massacre.
Al-Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden initially denied any involvement in the attack, but later admitted in 2004 that he had planned the attack. Despite trying to escape capture for nearly a decade, the world's top terrorist leader was finally found and killed by the United States in May 2011.
Muslim organizations in the United States strongly condemn the September 11, 2001 attacks and call on American-Muslims to use their skills and resources to help victims and their families through blood, medicine and food aid. And shelter for victims. The attack was also strongly denied and condemned by the media and governments around the world.
