(Phnom Penh): The Moradok Techo National Stadium is divided into three phases in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, 12 km from Wat Phnom and built on an area of more than 85 hectares under a project cost of about 200 million Dollars.
The first phase of construction started on April 12, 2013 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, including swimming pool, indoor sports center, basketball court, volleyball court and athletes' accommodation. The first phase was completed and inaugurated on April 4, 20217 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
Along with the inauguration of the achievements of the first phase of the Moradok Techo National Stadium, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also officially opened the construction site of the second phase, the construction of the Main Stadium of the Moradok Techo National Stadium on On April 4, 2017, the construction of this international standard stadium was a grant from the Chinese government in the amount of about 160 million dollars.
The third phase is the construction of sports villages and some remaining outdoor sports fields. The sports village is currently under construction by a local company to welcome about 10,000 delegates and athletes to the 2023 SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia. The sports village construction company has promised in front of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, chairman of the CAMSOC National Committee, that the construction will be completed by the end of 2022.
This great achievement was built to welcome the opening and closing ceremonies and the 32nd SEA Games, which was scheduled by the Royal Government to be held on May 5 and closed on May 17, 2023 and the 12th ASEAN Para Games, which will open on June 1 and close on June 10, 2023.
