(Phnom Penh): In general, human beings often build shelters or build villages or cities near water sources such as rivers and streams, because this idea has existed since prehistoric times. Therefore, some questions have been raised as to why our humanity is so popular.
The simple answer is that water is needed in daily life. On the other hand, wherever there is water, it is possible to grow crops. Most of the best cultivable areas are along the rivers, because the rivers have enough water to supply agriculture, and what is special is that the rivers are flooded every season. This flood brought with it fertile sediments.
On the other hand, rivers, seas, etc., are a network of national and international trade routes near and far, the best means of transportation and travel, because in the old days it was not easy to have long roads that were easier to travel than waterways. No. The fact that one human society is connected to another human society also has this waterway network, which is the first and foremost means.
