(Phnom Penh): Prosecutors of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the evening of September 10, 2021 decided to charge a police officer in Khan 7 Makara for beating a woman who violated the traffic law on the head for "aggravated intentional violence" Separately, the driver was charged with "driving a vehicle and refusing to stop a vehicle on the orders of a road traffic police officer", which is punishable under Article 76 of the Road Traffic Law.
A Phnom Penh Municipal Court official told Fresh News that the charges against the two men were made by Deputy Prosecutor Chhay Hong of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
On the morning of September 10, 2021, the police inspectorate of Khan 7 Makara sent the police officer who caused the accident to a woman to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to proceed with the procedure.
Please be informed that at around 8:20 pm on September 08, 2021, there was a violent incident between the police officer of Khan 7 Makara and the motorcyclist not wearing a helmet in Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh.
According to the report, before the incident, the two victims were riding a motorbike without wearing a helmet when they reached the checkpoint, they tried to ride back and were beaten by the police officer, who hit the woman on the side. After breaking his head and falling off the motorcycle as well.
The victim was Ngon Srey Nich, 22, and the driver was Ngon Seila, 18. Separately, the violent police officer is known as Mat Pisey.
