BEIJING: A telephone conversation between Chinese President Xi Jinping and US President Joe Biden has caught the world's attention, especially at a time when the two economies are facing major problems. Which is extremely difficult to solve. This is according to the release by the Chinese newspaper CGTN on Friday afternoon, September 10, 2021.
However, the 90-minute telephone meeting, which was announced on Friday, both sides seemed to show a soft attitude and wanted to move towards a positive return to their relationship to suit the context. Varies around the world. Chinese President Xi Jinping has urged the United States under Zhou Biden to work for a return to normal relations between the two countries.
In that conversation, Xi Jinping expressed his condolences to Joe Biden over the loss of American lives and the economic damage caused by Hurricane Ida last week. Zhou Biden also received sympathy from the Chinese president.
As a follow-up, Xi spoke of US policies toward China, which have sometimes made Sino-US relations extremely difficult. Xi stressed that the seriousness surrounding the issue not only affects the interests of the people of the two countries, but also the common interests of the countries of the world.
Xi Jinping explained during a 90-minute conversation with Zhou Biden that the United States and China are now the world's two largest economies, so how can the two countries maintain relations? Demonstrate responsibility for the future of the world?
Chinese President Xi Jinping has urged incumbent US President Joe Biden to work for a return to normal relations between the two countries, and this is not an option, but something that China will America must do and improve.
Turning to climate change and COVID-19, Xi Jinping expressed China's unwavering commitment to strengthening ties with the international community to address these issues. China supports green development and is committed to pursuing a carbon reduction plan in the international arena. For COVID-19, China is pushing for international cooperation to address common issues.
In response, Joe Biden made a similar remark. The US president acknowledged that the world is changing rapidly. "US-China relations are the most complex in the world, and the future of the whole world depends on how the United States and China interact," Biden said.
