KOICA donates 3 vehicles to Ministry of Health and Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri Provincial Health Departments
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) on September 10, 2021 provided three vehicles to the Ministry of Health and the Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri Provincial Health Departments through the Maternal and Child Health Project in the Northeast. Of Cambodia.
The handover ceremony was held at the Ministry of Health under the chairmanship of Mr. Eng Hout, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Mr. Rho Hyunjun, Director of KOICA Cambodia, and handed over to the Ministry and Project Team in Ratanakkiri and Mondul Provinces. Kiri.
These vehicles will play an important role in overseeing and directing project implementation, especially training in remote areas. A four-year maternal and child health project in northeastern Cambodia (2019-2023) implemented under a grant from the Republic of Korea through KOICA at a cost of approximately US $ 7 million.
The project is being implemented in Ratanakiri and Mondulkiri provinces, which aims to improve maternal and child health through improved quality and access to maternal and child health services.
The project has the following key components: capacity building for health workers, improvement of health facilities, strengthening outreach services for remote areas, and community outreach. The project provides transportation such as boats and motorbikes to health centers and to vulnerable communities.
Death news! Mother-in-law Chan Yutha, spokeswoman and secretary of state at the Ministry of Water Resources, has died at the age of 76.
(Battambang): Disciple Lim Chin, the mother of Mr. Chan Yutha, Spokesman and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, passed away on Wednesday, September 8, 2015. 2021 at 12:00 noon at the age of 76 due to illness.
The death of Disciple Lim Yin is the loss of a pious mother, mother-in-law and grandmother who raised, nurtured and educated her children in a moral way. The funeral of Disciple Lim Chin was held at the funeral home in Battambang City, Battambang Province.
In this sad atmosphere, we, the leaders and members of the family of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, would like to share our condolences with His Excellency and his family and pray for the blessings of Preah Ratanatray, all the sacred objects in the world, for the soul of Disciple Lim Yin went to hell, not to be missed.
Battambang provincial governor Nguon Rattanak also paid his respects at the funeral home.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that the requirement to pay tax on duty-free vehicle owners under various license plates is equitable for all taxpayers. Each.
Dr. Kun Nhem made the remarks at a press conference on "Collection of Import Tax on Shelter Vehicles under Various License Plates" held on September 10, 2021 via video.
He stressed that it is very difficult for law enforcement if tax evaders refuse to pay taxes, so from time to time we face all kinds of problems by using gentle and hot measures.
"We live in a society where we have to look at ourselves, if the law requires it to be implemented in this way, the owners of tax-free cars have a decent role and status, this is a time when it should show the implementation of tax obligations," he said. As for paying taxes, it is not to help the Ministry of Finance or to any side, but to help the government, which is facing the burden of Kovid 19 disease, and to support social work and victims of the disease. Kovid 19 as well.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, on September 10, 2021, confirmed that for the first eight months of 2021, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia collects revenue. More than $ 1.5 billion in taxes.
This statement was made by Dr. Kun Nhem at the press conference on "Collection of import tax on pigs under various license plates and no import duties and taxes" via the online system on the afternoon of September 10, 2021. .
In addition, Dr. Kun Nhem emphasized that the implementation of the collection of import tax on vehicles under various license plates and duty-free and import duties is to help reduce the declining tax revenue and also a source to meet the needs of expenditures.
At the same time, Dr. Kun Nhem also pointed out the difficulties in cracking down on those cars, as the customs encountered many complicated problems, such as fake license plates and not being an official who was a businessman but wearing a K.PK number plate.
Dr. Kun Nhim also said that the revenue collected by the Customs plays a very important role in the national budget, with two units collecting taxes into the national budget: the General Department of Taxation and the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise. .
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia claims that these two entities are the exporters of import-export taxes from international trade, and the General Department of Taxation collects taxes on the country.
Dr. Kun Nhim stated that the main sources of revenue collected by the customs are vehicles: cars, machinery, motorcycles and many other types of vehicles.
He said that in 2019, revenue from vehicle imports accounted for 53 percent of total customs revenue, and in 2020, customs revenue from vehicle imports fell to 42 percent due to an increase in vehicle smuggling activities.
