Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: Without the leadership of Samdech Techo, Cambodia may not have been able to fight the 19-year-old Kovid War that lasted for two years.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, said on September 10, 2021 that without development and progress in all areas under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Many years ago, Cambodia may not have had the resources and resources to fight the 19-year-old Kovid War, which lasted for about two years.
The presence of Kovid 19 in Cambodia has been going on for almost two years, as large-scale community outbreaks in Cambodia began on February 20, 2021. According to the announcement of the Ministry of Health, so far, Cambodia has found 19 cases of Kovid: a total of 97,524, a total of 92,495 people have been cured, a total of 2,007 deaths. There were 3,731 new metabolic infections.
However, so far, Cambodia has received 19 doses of Kovid vaccinated, a total of nearly 30 million doses to give to the people, of which China has supplied the most vaccines to Cambodia. In addition, there is the World Health Organization through the COCAC mechanism, Japan, the United Kingdom and the United States through CAVAC.
The large presence of Chinese vaccines has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's implementation of a 12-year-old vaccination plan for an estimated 12 million people. The presence of the Chinese Kovid 19 vaccine in Cambodia clearly demonstrates the spirit of steel friendship between China and Cambodia, the spirit of helping each other through adversity. In particular, it shows the strong Chinese spirit of participation in helping to fight Kovid 19 in Cambodia.
As of the night of September 9, 2021, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of National Defense have vaccinated 19 Kovid 19 civil servants, citizens and the armed forces across the country, a total of 11,385,200 people.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has set out the following five principles and mechanisms:
1: Suspend the crackdown on vehicles in the country for a while (except border areas) from now on to allow time for car owners to take refuge under various license plates and have not yet paid taxes and duties to fulfill their tax and duty obligations. Tax according to the law in force.
2. In order to encourage vehicle owners to come and fulfill their tax and duty obligations on time, vehicle owners will receive a tax deduction of 10% of the total tax amount to be paid.
This mitigation has a deadline of December 31, 2021 and does not cover vehicles with a production year of 2021. From January 1, 2022 to June 30, 2022, which is the deadline for entry to pay taxes, vehicle owners must fulfill their full tax and duty obligations without any tax deduction. .
3. For right-hand drive vehicles, car owners must deposit a deposit equal to the total tax and levy of 10% and must take the car to repair the steering wheel from right to left until June 30, 2022. After changing the steering wheel, the car owner can get the tax receipt and license plate from the customs officer.
4. Allow branches and offices of Customs and Excise throughout the country to pay taxes and duties on vehicles under various license plates and have not yet fulfilled their tax and duty obligations.
5: From July 1, 2022 onwards, tax-free vehicles that have been suppressed will be required to pay taxes and duties, including fines, according to the regulations in force. Right-hand drive vehicles, which are prohibited from being imported in the event of a crackdown, will be demolished or dismantled as spare parts.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has called on all duty-free vehicle owners to voluntarily come to fulfill their tax and import duties in a timely manner in accordance with the principles and mechanisms set out in this notice. Donors Continue to Donate Food to Pursat Provincial Administration to Participate in 19 Measles Prevention Rules
