(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, confirmed that the Ministry is studying the cable network from districts to communes in six provinces of Cambodia and is scheduled to be completed in January 2022.
This statement was made on the occasion that Mr. Chea Vandeth allowed the delegation of the Digital Technology Association of Cambodia to pay a courtesy call and discuss the work online.
Mr. Chea Vandeth said that this connection connects all districts to communes, connecting schools, commune offices or health centers and other areas in the commune where people use the Internet.
In addition, Mr. Chea Vandeth said that he gave the team to study the installation of telephone antenna towers in all communes to prepare for the use of digital to turn the country into a digital country.
Mr. Chea Vandeth claimed that by 2027, all internet must reach all communes, whether the state gives money or not to the Ministry, he is determined to do so, taking into account the Ministry's revenue budget to deploy.
Dr. Heng Vuthy, Honorary Vice President of the Digital Technology Association of Cambodia, emphasized that Cambodia now has more online businesses than ever before, in line with the growth of smartphone use and e-commerce.
Dr. Heng Vuthy said that digital transformation has become a major policy direction in many countries as they have been struggling to adapt to the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
According to the President of the Digital Technology Association of Cambodia, the Cambodian Digital Economy and Social Policy Framework has set out a vision to build a vibrant digital economy and society to accelerate new economic growth and improve social welfare based on normalization.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, said that the Ministry will reorganize the postal policy to protect the online trade law, reduce the maximum amount of fraud on online purchases.
The Minister said that the postal and telecommunications sector is an indispensable sector, one of the most important in the current situation in Cambodia during the 19 crisis of Kovid. This sector really plays a core role in all sectors.
The Minister made the remarks during a courtesy call and discussion with the Digital Technology Association of Cambodia on September 9, 2021.
Movement for Health of Cambodia supports the action of the Ministry of Health, which reminds tobacco companies to stop promoting tobacco products or sponsoring other materials to ministries-institutions or sub-national administrations
(Phnom Penh): Movement for Health of Cambodia supports the action of the Ministry of Health in requesting the cooperation of ministries and institutions that are members of the Tobacco Products Control Committee, all relevant institutions at both national and sub-national levels must not receive assistance Sponsored by a tobacco company with no product name or tobacco company name.
It should be noted that Article 3 of the Sub-Decree on the Establishment and Functioning of the Tobacco Products Control Committee stipulates that its members shall not have any conflict of interest or relationship with the tobacco industry. Some ministries and institutions and the 25 capital-provincial administrations are members of this committee.
The Cambodian Movement for Health has observed that in the past, a number of tobacco companies have donated 19 Kovid vaccines to ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations by posting these activities on social media to cover up the fact that smoking Cigarettes pose a higher risk of contracting Kovid, and smokers with Kovid have the highest health risk compared to non-smokers.
It should be noted that due to diseases caused by tobacco use, about 15,000 Cambodians die every year and cost the national economy 649 million US dollars, according to a United Nations study for Cambodia.
Chamkar Mon District Authority cleans the environment in Hun Sen Bun Rany High School, Phsar Doeum Thkov to be ready to reopen on September 15
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, this morning, September 10, 2021, led the district administration officials, the People's Defense Force, teachers and students to clean and spray pesticides to clean the environment in Hun Sen Bun Rany High School. Phsar Doeum Thkov is located in Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkar Morn to prepare for the re-admission of students on September 15, 2021.
Mr. Theng Sothol said that the situation of Kovid 19 in Cambodia has been relieved and with the joint cooperation of people from all walks of life and authorities at all levels, the number of infections and the death rate of the disease. Kovid-19 is in decline.
Mr. Theng Sothol added that the re-opening of the school by the head of the Royal Government is a good time to continue to develop human resources in Cambodia, but requires all people to be very careful not to In order for the transmission of Kovid disease into the school building, in particular, it must continue to participate in the implementation of the recommendations of the head of the Royal Government.
Mr. Chamkar Mon District Governor emphasized that according to the minutes of the meeting with the Capital Governor and relevant authorities, the case of students who have not been vaccinated against Kovid 19 is not allowed to attend the school. Limit the number of people in each room to no more than 15 people.
Please note that all public and private institutions will be open for students to return to school from September 15, 2021 onwards after missing for more than 7 months due to the Kovid-19 outbreak. The reopening of schools for students is only possible if they meet the Ministry of Health's statute of belief that there is no spread of Kovid-19 disease.
