Kampong Cham Province Will Reopen Students on September 20
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, has decided to reopen students from secondary school, high school and Buddhist school on September 20, and on October 11, it will reopen primary school students. Followed by.
The provincial governor made this decision after discussing with relevant officials on the morning of September 10, 2021 in the meeting to review and evaluate the reopening of public and private educational institutions in Kampong Cham province.
According to the provincial governor, "Kampong Cham Provincial Administration will open the school to students in two stages, including:
* First: for students from secondary school and Buddhist school: enrollment on September 20 * Second: Primary school enrollment on October 11. The decision to enroll students from junior high school was made because they had already been vaccinated against Kovid 19 and they were at a very educated age on measures to prevent and spread Kovid 19. .
For primary school students, the provincial administration will arrange for them to return to school in the second phase, leaving the opportunity for teachers, the Department of Education as well as local authorities to develop strategies to manage them well. Primary is small, difficult to control.
The provincial governor confirmed that in districts with a high risk of contracting Kovid 19, the admission of students according to the situation, that is, if the commune has a lot of infection is not allowed to open schools.
