Ms. Men Sam An: We hope that Chinese-Cambodian entrepreneurs will invest in the "Silk Road e-commerce" project in the "Belt and Road" initiative.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kittisang Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, expressed hope that Chinese-Cambodian entrepreneurs will invest and cooperate in the "Silk Road e-commerce" project in the "Belt and Road" initiative. Road.
Ms. Men Sam An expressed her hope during a special speech at the 2021 China Silk Road e-commerce program in Xi'an, the 21st China International Trade and Investment Fair, an enterprise forum and an international cooperation forum. Held in Fujian Province, China on September 8, 2021.
The theme of the conference is "Deepening the E-Trade Dialogue and Multilateral Cooperation". Work together to promote building a community with a common future for humanity and to unite and work together to meet new challenges.
Ms. Men Sam An emphasized in her speech that Cambodia-China friendly relations have a long history. China is Cambodia's largest donor and humanitarian donor, as well as Cambodia's largest source of tourism and foreign investors.
