General Vong Pisen Allows Chinese Military Attaché to Conclude
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, on September 10, 2021, received Special Lieutenant Colonel Li Jingfeng, Deputy Chief of Staff of the People's Republic of China in Cambodia, for a courtesy call. Goodbye.
On that occasion, Special Colonel Li Jingfeng expressed his gratitude to the leadership of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for nearly two years for providing support and good cooperation, making his diplomatic mission a success and success. The fruitful results should be a source of pride.
In response, General Vong Pisen highlighted the traditional ties of solidarity and friendship between Cambodia and China, which have existed for a long time and the two countries still have close relations with each other, especially in difficult times. Relationships support each other.
General Vong Pisen thanked the People's Republic of China for providing 19 Kovid vaccines, as well as medicines and equipment to combat the spread of Kovid 19 into the community.
On the military front, General Vong Pisen thanked the Chinese People's Army for providing air defense equipment, strengthening the capacity of the Cambodian Blue Hat Forces to carry out demining missions within the framework of the United Nations, as well as Building infrastructure, building training schools, training human resources, both domestic and foreign, especially joint exercises in the past, to exchange experiences and increase the capacity of the two countries' armies.
The Commander-in-Chief also wished Lt. Col. Li Jingfeng more success in his new assignment and expressed confidence that China would continue to assist Cambodia as a steel friend and ally. As a strategic partner in all aspects. General knowledge: Why do football players have to stand in a circle before starting a match?
(Phnom Penh): Before the start of each football match, both sports teams always stand close to each other in a circle, and some teams also sing their national anthem, while such gestures seem to strengthen the spirit of unity in the team. But the history of doing so is much more. Why do football players have to stand in a circle before the start of a match?
Gallardard University is the world's first university for deaf students, founded in 1864 in Washington, D.C., where they also formed the first American football team for the deaf. Also.
For American football, players from both sides must stand facing each other in a circle in the middle of the field before the match. Before 1890, the signal of each team always shouted the strategy of the game to the team and the other opponent heard all.
To solve this problem, the coach of the deaf team often uses hand gestures to tell the strategy of the game so that his team has an advantage over other teams who have normal ears. But when playing with the same group of deaf people, the other side will easily understand, only in 1894 the same coach began to hide his hand signals by calling the strikers in a circle before each game.
Using this technique is so effective that it becomes a habit to do it all the time before the game starts. Until 1896, the circle also spread to other universities and became a practice to this day.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks Chinese friends for supporting Cambodia through all forms of assistance, especially assistance and supply of vaccines
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of China for providing assistance and support to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia through all kinds of technical assistance in the treatment of Kovid disease. 19 In particular, the provision and assistance of the Kovid-19 vaccine in the past.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this morning, September 10, 2021, on the occasion of Samdech attending the opening ceremony of the 18th China-ASEAN Expo 2021 via online video, which was held under the theme "Distribution "Sharing the opportunities gained from the new corridor, land and sea to build a China-ASEAN community for a common future."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "On behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, I would like to express my deep gratitude to the Chinese government and people for their support to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia through all forms of assistance. "Kovid-19 treatment techniques, medical equipment and especially Kovid-19 vaccine assistance, as well as facilitating the Cambodian side in purchasing vaccines from China."
He also commended the Chinese government and people for their active participation and leading role in the global fight against Kovid-19 through the production and distribution of vaccines and the provision of equipment. Physicians and sharing experiences in the prevention, care and treatment of Kovid-19 patients.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that clearly understanding this opportunity with a proactive spirit, the Royal Government of Cambodia has made unremitting efforts to improve the business environment, investment and enhance Cambodia's competitiveness through the introduction and implementation of measures. Subsequent sharp reforms as well.
It should be noted that so far, Cambodia has received 19 vaccines against Kovid, a total of nearly 30 million doses to give to the people, of which China has supplied the most vaccines to Cambodia. In addition, there is the World Health Organization through the COCAC mechanism, Japan, the United Kingdom and the United States through CAVAC.
The large presence of Chinese vaccines has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's implementation of a 12-year-old vaccination plan for an estimated 12 million people. The presence of the Chinese Kovid 19 vaccine in Cambodia clearly demonstrates the spirit of steel friendship between China and Cambodia, a spirit of mutual support in the face of adversity. In particular, it shows the strong Chinese spirit of participation in helping to fight Kovid 19 in Cambodia.
